//www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-harvest-farming-guide-best-crop-rotation-strategy-for-lifeforce-and-divines.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Harvest Farming Guide: Best Crop Rotation Strategy for Lifeforce and Divines","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-14","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-harvest-farming-guide-best-low-cost-fruiting-astrolabe-strategy-for-lifeforce-and-divine-farming.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Harvest Farming Guide: Best Low-Cost Fruiting Astrolabe Strategy","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-29-harvest-farming-guide-how-to-use-fruiting-astrolabe-strategy-for-massive-life-force-profits.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Harvest Farming Guide: How to Use Fruiting Astrolabe Strategy","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-29-latest-farming-meta-why-this-harvest-astrolabe-strategy-delivers-consistent-profits.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Latest Farming Meta: Harvest Astrolabe Strategy","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.iggm.com/news/poe-3-29-harvest-farming-guide-how-to-build-consistent-lifeforce-currency-farming-setup","title":"PoE 3.29 Harvest Farming Guide: How to Build a Consistent Lifeforce Currency Farming Setup","publisher":"IGGM (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-11 (modified 2026-08-12)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.ezg.com/blog/poe-3-29-1-harvest-farming-guide-best-setup-for-divines","title":"PoE 3.29.1 Harvest Farming Guide: Best Setup for Divines","publisher":"EZG (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-01 (modified 2026-09-18)","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-harvest-farming-guide","title":"PoE 3.29 Harvest Farming Guide","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (boosting/currency seller)","date":"2026-08-25","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Astrolabe","title":"Astrolabe","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (fetched 2026-11-04)","patch":"3.28+"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Originator_Voidstone","title":"Originator Voidstone","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (fetched 2026-11-04)","patch":"3.28+"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Oshabi%2C_Avatar_of_the_Grove","title":"Oshabi, Avatar of the Grove","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (may be the original 3.11 version)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Economy_vivid-lifeforce","title":"Vivid Crystallised Lifeforce economy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"live data, fetched 2026-11-04 (no timestamp shown)","patch":"unknown (Allflame 3.29 likely)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Economy_primal-lifeforce","title":"Primal Crystallised Lifeforce economy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"live data, fetched 2026-11-04 (no timestamp shown)","patch":"unknown (Allflame 3.29 likely)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Economy_wild-lifeforce","title":"Wild Crystallised Lifeforce economy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"live data, fetched 2026-11-04 (no timestamp shown)","patch":"unknown (Allflame 3.29 likely)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Economy_sacred-lifeforce","title":"Sacred Crystallised Lifeforce economy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"live data, fetched 2026-11-04 (no timestamp shown)","patch":"unknown (Allflame 3.29 likely)"},{"url":"https://outof.games/news/9298-path-of-exiles-mirage-league-ends-july-20-mirage-to-not-go-core/","title":"Path of Exile's Mirage League Ends July 20 - Mirage to Not Go Core","publisher":"Out of Games","date":"unknown (circa July 2026)","patch":"3.28 -> 3.29"},{"url":"https://www.poecurrency.com/news/poe-3-28-0c-patch-made-harvest-overflowing-with-value","title":"PoE 3.28.0c Patch Made Harvest Overflowing with Value","publisher":"POECurrency (currency seller)","date":"2026-03-20","patch":"3.28.0c"},{"url":"https://www.ssegold.com/poe-3-28-harvest-farming-guide-mirage-league","title":"PoE 3.28 Harvest Farming Guide (Mirage League)","publisher":"SSEGold (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28"}]},"breach":{"title":"Breach (3.29)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Breach has been core since 3.28. From the Act 6 Mud Flats, areas can spawn Breach Hives or Unstable Breaches. They pay out Hiveblood and Wombgifts, which you grow into currency, uniques and rares at the Genesis Tree or sell to other players. 3.29 nerfed Unstable Breaches (2 open at most, fewer monsters), but Maxroll still ranks the Unstable Breach farm S tier as the best raw currency farm. A cheap league-start version farms Hiveblood and Wombgifts instead.","howTo":[{"text":"From the Act 6 Mud Flats, areas can spawn a Breach Hive or Unstable Breaches. An area never has both, and never more than one Hive.","stage":["all"],"cite":[2,18]},{"text":"Unstable Breach: touch the Breach Hand to open it. Kill its monsters fast to stabilise it before it collapses.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Stabilise and close every Unstable Breach in the area. The area reward only comes when all of them are done.","stage":["all"],"cite":[18]},{"text":"Since 3.29 only 2 Unstable Breaches can be open at the same time.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,17]},{"text":"Hive: defend Ailith through the waves. Her remaining hits show above the wave counter, and the encounter fails if she dies.","stage":["all"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Hive walls near you burn away. Breaking more walls before you start makes the Hive harder and more rewarding.","stage":["all"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Hives are about 30% smaller since 3.28. You and your allies can break their walls with damage, but only while no encounter is running.","stage":["all"],"cite":[2,18]},{"text":"Hive Fortress: a portal takes you to a separate area with your map's mods. It ends in a 24-wave Hive defence, and all its loot drops back in the map as one burst.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Grasping Coffers in a Fortress can drop Wombgifts and Foulborn uniques.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Rewards are Hiveblood and Wombgifts (Ancient, Lavish, Mysterious, Provisioning). Grow them at the Genesis Tree or sell them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[5,7]},{"text":"Hiveblood is shared by all your characters in the league and caps at 100,000.","stage":["all"],"cite":[2,18]},{"text":"Set a stash tab to Breach affinity. The Genesis Tree takes Wombgifts straight from it, so you do not need to carry them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,17]},{"text":"What each Wombgift grows: Provisioning gives armour or jewellery, Lavish gives currency, Ancient gives a unique, and Mysterious gives a random item.","stage":["all"],"cite":[47,18]},{"text":"Growing a Wombgift costs much more Hiveblood at higher item levels: 210 at ilvl 68, 1,458 at ilvl 84.","stage":["all"],"cite":[46]},{"text":"Genesis Tree points come from body-part quest items. Your first Hive or Unstable Breach gives the Horned Skull. Strange Limb and Foul Hand give 3 Unique points each.","stage":["all"],"cite":[46]},{"text":"Vendor any Breachstones you have. They no longer open domains, and a vendor gives a Hivebrain Gland for them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[13,18]},{"text":"Put a Hivebrain Gland in your personal Map Device to open the Hive Colony (area level 83). It needs no map and is used up in one go.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[12,18]},{"text":"Killing It That Was Tul and It That Was Esh drops Breachlord Limbs: 1 Equipment, 3 Unique and 1 Mysterious point.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[46,50]},{"text":"More Genesis Tree points unlock as your total Hiveblood spent passes 300, 1k, 3k, 6k, 12k, 18k and 30k.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[46,50]},{"text":"Grasping Astrolabe: adds a Shaped Region of Breach maps to one Atlas quadrant. To complete a map there, stabilise and close every Unstable Breach. Each map you complete makes the region harder and richer.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[9]},{"text":"Pick one atlas keystone: Enemy at the Gates makes every Breach an Unstable Breach, and Dimensional Foothold makes every Breach a Hive.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[31,32,18]},{"text":"Flesh of Xesht turns a Breach unique into its alternate version.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[14,18]},{"text":"Mysterious Wombgift results are not fully known. They seem to give Stacked Decks, other Wombgifts, and levelled or quality gems.","stage":["all"],"cite":[51]}],"dangers":[{"text":"If you leave any Unstable Breach open, you lose the whole area's reward.","stage":["all"],"cite":[18]},{"text":"Old guides that farm Chayula's domain with Breachstones are out of date. Breachstones only vendor for a Hivebrain Gland now.","stage":["all"],"cite":[13,18,28]},{"text":"Maxroll's Unstable Breach guide (3.29.1) still says 3 can be open at once. The real cap is 2.","stage":["late"],"cite":[4,0]},{"text":"Maxroll's 3.29 patch note copy has the first draft numbers (25% fewer packs, 17% more progress). The final values are 15% fewer packs and 25% more progress.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,1]},{"text":"Breach monsters drop less gold and fewer maps than normal monsters. This matters for map sustain early.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[18,20]},{"text":"The Hive fails if Ailith dies.","stage":["all"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Hive Colony bosses each have about 117.8M life, 50% elemental and 30% chaos resistance. You gain and lose no XP there.","stage":["late"],"cite":[28,48,49]},{"text":"Tul fights in melee with a shield (throws, slams, ice showers, tentacles). Esh is a ranged chaos caster (beam, eruptions, portals, summons). Both have an ultimate.","stage":["late"],"cite":[48,49]},{"text":"Hive Colony loot comes from Tul (+15000% rarity). Esh has a no-drops modifier.","stage":["late"],"cite":[48,49]},{"text":"The Grasping Astrolabe region gets harder with every map you complete.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[9]},{"text":"Older Resonant Cascade text (50% more reward per Breach) is from 3.26 and out of date.","stage":["late"],"cite":[25,20]},{"text":"Never take Dimensional Barrier on a Breach tree. It turns Breaches and Breach Scarab drops off.","stage":["all"],"cite":[45,7]},{"text":"MMOexp warns that Scarab of Wisps does not stack well with Wildwood.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[41]},{"text":"Vaal Breach is still disabled.","stage":["all"],"cite":[18]}],"sell":[{"text":"Lavish Wombgift price depends on item level: ilvl 84 about 40c (0.1 div), ilvl 75 about 5.5c (2026-11-04).","stage":["all"],"cite":[34,38]},{"text":"Ancient Wombgift: ilvl 84 about 13c, ilvl 75 about 10c. ilvl 75 is the most listed, with about 1,100 listings.","stage":["all"],"cite":[34]},{"text":"Mysterious Wombgifts sell for about 1c at any item level. Sorting them by level is not worth it.","stage":["all"],"cite":[34]},{"text":"Provisioning Wombgifts are almost worthless on the market (0.04c at ilvl 75, 0.75c at ilvl 84). Use them on the Genesis Tree.","stage":["all"],"cite":[34]},{"text":"Hivebrain Gland about 10.6c. Flesh of Xesht about 60c, down about 56% over the week.","stage":["all"],"cite":[36,35]},{"text":"Breach scarabs: Resonant Cascade about 58c, Incensed Swarm 9.4c, Instability 6.3c, Marshal 3.4c, Hive 0.4c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[37]},{"text":"The Unstable Breach farm drops mostly raw currency: Divines, Chaos and Valdo's Puzzle Boxes, with rare Hinekora's Lock or Mirror. Hiveblood and Wombgifts come on top.","stage":["late"],"cite":[4]},{"text":"Divine Orb was about 412c on 2026-11-04.","stage":["all"],"cite":[35]}],"strategies":[{"name":"League-start Hiveblood and Wombgift farm (Maxroll, Milkybk_)","investment":"Low. Maxroll rates profit as Average.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"steps":["Run T16 Jungle Valley. Its altars cannot roll boss mods until you enter the boss arena.","City Square or Dunes also work.","Stack Breach Scarab of Instability.","As budget grows, add Breach Scarab of the Marshal for extra bosses and Scarab of Monstrous Lineage for bigger packs.","Use a fast-clearing build.","Influence is not essential.","Spend the Hiveblood and Wombgifts on the Genesis Tree for rares and Foulborn uniques."],"atlasPassives":["Enemy at the Gates","Clawed Open","Massing Forces","Fortified Dominance","Fecund Colony","Swelling Ranks","Evolving Hives","Broken Border","Eldritch Gaze","Rampant Growth","Small: Breach Hiveblood Quantity x5 (5% each)","Small: Wombgift Quantity (5%)","Small: Ancient Wombgift Chance x2, Provisioning Wombgift Chance x2 (25% each)","Scarab nodes; no Synthesised Stability, no Beyond"],"scarabs":["Breach Scarab of Instability x2","Breach Scarab of the Marshal (upgrade)","Scarab of Monstrous Lineage (upgrade)"],"cite":[5,43,45]},{"name":"Unstable Breach currency farm (Maxroll, BawLoch, 3.29.1)","investment":"Extremely High. Maxroll rates profit as Excellent.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Place a Grasping Astrolabe to make a Shaped Region of Breach maps.","Take Synthesised Stability. Finishing a map in the region then collapses a different map, so you can keep running Dunes.","Run T16 Dunes with Originator influence.","Roll maps to at least 92% more currency on a budget, or 140% or more with high investment.","Use Maven's Chisel of Avarice and 1-5 Delirium Orbs (Armoursmith's).","Use Eater of Worlds influence.","Rush the boss first to get better Eldritch altars.","Pick currency duplication, item quantity and scarab duplication altars.","Clear the Breaches from the edges inward.","The guide still says 3 Unstable Breaches can be open at once. The cap is 2 since 3.29."],"atlasPassives":["Enemy at the Gates","Clawed Open","Massing Forces","Violent Skirmish","Swelling Ranks","Evolving Hives","Broken Border","Synthesised Stability (via 3 Memory Tear Chance nodes after Invasive Adversaries)","Invasive Adversaries","Mounting and Multiplying Modifiers","Shaping the Mountains and Skies","Beyond: Endless Tide, Scent of Blood, Pale Clarion, 11 Beyond Chance nodes","Eater of Worlds: Eldritch Gaze, The Shadow of Hunger","138 points total"],"scarabs":["Budget: Scarab of Wisps, Breach Scarab of Instability x2, Scarab of Monstrous Lineage x2","High: Scarab of Wisps, Breach Scarab of Instability x2, Horned Scarab of Bloodlines, Cartography Scarab of Risk"],"cite":[4,9,10,11,42,45]},{"name":"Budget Unstable Breach (POECurrency)","investment":"Budget. Skips Horned Scarab of Bloodlines because of its cost.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run T16.5 Dunes rolled to at least 90% increased currency.","Add 2-5 Fine Delirium Orbs.","Kill the map boss when you enter.","Then clear the Unstable Breaches.","The setup comes from a currency seller. Its profit figures are not verified."],"scarabs":["Breach Scarab of Instability x2","Scarab of Monstrous Lineage x2","Scarab of Wisps x1"],"cite":[39]},{"name":"Breach Fortress farm (Maxroll B tier, MMOexp)","investment":"Not rated in these sources","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Breach Scarab of the Marshal so Hives lead to a Hive Fortress.","Use eight-mod maps, ideally T16.5.","Take Dimensional Foothold (every Breach is a Hive) and Protracted Siege.","Clear the Fortress for its loot burst of currency, scarabs and maps at the end.","MMOexp warns that Scarab of Wisps does not stack well with Wildwood.","Maxroll calls this the best way to farm Hiveblood."],"atlasPassives":["Dimensional Foothold","Protracted Siege","Adaptive Reaction","Fortified Dominance","Violent Skirmish","Fecund Colony","Swelling Ranks","Evolving Hives","Broken Border","Beyond","Eldritch Gaze (Eater of Worlds)","Small: Breach Hiveblood Quantity x5, Breach Flammable Burrows x4, Ailith Skill Damage x2, Wombgift Quantity x3, Ancient Wombgift Chance x2, Lavish Wombgift Chance x2","No Synthesised Stability"],"scarabs":["Breach Scarab of the Marshal","Scarab of Monstrous Lineage x2"],"cite":[6,44,41,45]},{"name":"Genesis Tree priorities","investment":"Hiveblood and quest points","stage":["all"],"steps":["Equipment: take Remove Lowest Tier Modifier first, then every Modifier Tier Rating node, then Solid Cysts (fractured mod).","Equipment: Sockets and Links is strong early for making 6-links.","Unique: Multiple Foulborn Modifiers is a must if you want several Foulborn mods.","Unique: Additional Unique is nearly a must. Unique Rarity is recommended. Take Corrupted Uniques only if you chase Foulborn.","Unique: Lord's Descent gives 150% more chance for Breach uniques. Remembered Origins gives 300%, but no Foulborn.","Unique: Throbbing Veins rolls sockets and links 50 times and keeps the best.","Currency: Prodigal Offspring, Fertile Genesis, Additional Currency Chance and Flawed Seeds.","Currency: Encrusted Fruit turns 25% of results into Gold.","Miscellany: Parthenogenesis plus the 800% notables turn junk Mysterious Wombgifts into Lavish ones."],"cite":[51,46,40]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough: Unstable Breach is S tier and the best raw currency farm in the game, despite the 3.29 nerfs.","who":"Maxroll Endgame Farming Tier List (BawLoch)","date":"2026-09-19","cite":[6]},{"text":"Rough: Breach Fortress is B tier and the best way to farm Hiveblood, plus currency, scarabs and maps.","who":"Maxroll Endgame Farming Tier List (BawLoch)","date":"2026-09-19","cite":[6]},{"text":"Rough: the Unstable Breach farm is rated Excellent profit for Extremely High investment.","who":"Maxroll (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","cite":[4]},{"text":"Rough: the league-start Breach farm is rated Average profit.","who":"Maxroll (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-07-24","cite":[5]},{"text":"Rough, unverified: about 2-2.5 div per map on a budget Unstable setup. At 10 maps an hour that is about 20 div/hr, or 10-12 div/hr at 10-12 minutes per map.","who":"POECurrency (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-30","cite":[39]},{"text":"Rough: a 20-map Unstable Breach test netted 75.64 div (about 3.78 div per map) on about 186c per map, plus about 90,000 Hiveblood. No hourly rate given.","who":"MMOexp (currency seller)","date":"2026-09-11","cite":[40]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"No Breach changes.","cite":[22]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Abysses no longer spawn inside Breach Hive encounters.","cite":[15]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"The Unique subtree was 2 points short. The fix gives the points through Strange Limb and Foul Hand, retroactively for players who already turned them in.","cite":[16,21]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Only 2 Unstable Breaches can be open at once (was 3).","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Unstable Breaches have 15% fewer monster packs, and each kill gives 25% more progress. These are the final values from 2026-07-24.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Breach monster packs contain fewer monsters on average.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Swelling Ranks fell from 20% to 10% pack size. Evolving Hives fell from 25% to 15%. Small pack-size nodes now give 5% Rare monsters. Small 8% Magic nodes are now 5%.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"GGG says the nerfs do not lower the Hiveblood or Wombgifts you get.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Genesis Tree equipment was nerfed. The subtree max fell from 20 to 16 points. Extra-item small nodes fell from 50% to 25%, and the base extra-item chance is also lower. Modifier notables fell from 500% to 300%. Equipment rolls slightly lower tiers on higher-tier bases.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The Breach Stash Tab is enabled again (2026-07-22). The Genesis Tree pulls Wombgifts from a Breach-affinity tab.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Breach became core. Hives and Unstable Breaches spawn from the Act 6 Mud Flats.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Breachstones no longer open domains. A vendor swaps them for a Hivebrain Gland, which opens the Hive Colony.","cite":[2,13,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Graftblood was renamed Hiveblood. It needs no Grafts, caps at 100,000 and is shared league-wide. Grafts can no longer be grown.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The Genesis Tree starts fully grown with every womb unlocked. Ailith still has to unlock passive points.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Fleshgrafts and Growing Wombgifts were deleted, and Ailith stopped selling Fleshgrafts. Provisioning Wombgifts no longer grow weapons or quivers.","cite":[18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Breach scarabs were renamed. Breach Scarab became Hive, Snares became Instability, Lordship became Marshal and Splintering became Incensed Swarm. The Breach sub-stash in the Fragment tab is now remove-only.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"New keystones: Enemy at the Gates (all Unstable) and Dimensional Foothold (all Hives).","cite":[31,32,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Hives are about 30% smaller, and you can break their walls.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Breach atlas clusters are back. The Incursion Temple and Delve Breach rooms are back with Unstable Breaches. Vaal Breach stays disabled.","cite":[18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The gold and map drop penalty on Breach monsters was increased.","cite":[18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Flesh of Xesht was added. The Breachlord achievement now asks you to kill It That Was Tul and It That Was Esh.","cite":[14,18]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Breach was removed from other content: Valdo's Puzzle Box, Heist Breach rooms (now Gold rooms) and Vaal Breach. The Breach atlas clusters and Kirac's Breach craft were also removed.","cite":[19]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Breach Blessings now only upgrade Breachstones, not Breach uniques.","cite":[19]}],"tables":[{"title":"Breach scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Effect","Per map","Price 2026-11-04"],"rows":[["Breach Scarab of the Hive","Adds a Breach Hive","1","~0.4c"],["Breach Scarab of Instability","Adds 2 Unstable Breaches","2","~6.3c"],["Breach Scarab of the Marshal","Boss in each Unstable Breach; Hives lead to a Hive Fortress","1","~3.4c"],["Breach Scarab of the Incensed Swarm","Ailith's skills enrage the Hive; harder, richer later waves","1","~9.4c"],["Breach Scarab of Resonant Cascade","Each Unstable Breach 10% faster, harder and richer per one already opened","1","~58c"]],"cite":[8,23,24,25,26,27,37]},{"title":"Support scarabs for the Unstable Breach farm","columns":["Scarab","Use","Price 2026-11-04"],"rows":[["Horned Scarab of Bloodlines","1 per map; 150% more Magic monsters, each with an extra mod; high-investment core","~613c (~1.5 div)"],["Cartography Scarab of Risk","High-investment setup","~116c"],["Scarab of Wisps","Budget and high setups","~30c"],["Scarab of Monstrous Lineage","Budget setup, x2","~9.3c"]],"cite":[11,37,39,4]},{"title":"Wombgifts","columns":["Type","Grows","ilvl 84 price","ilvl 75 price"],"rows":[["Lavish","Currency","~40c","~5.5c"],["Ancient","Unique","~13c","~10c"],["Mysterious","Random item","~1c","~1c"],["Provisioning","Armour or jewellery","~0.75c","~0.04c"]],"cite":[47,34,38]},{"title":"Hiveblood cost to grow a Wombgift","columns":["Item level","Hiveblood"],"rows":[["68","210"],["74","667"],["76","822"],["84","1,458"]],"cite":[46]},{"title":"Breach atlas nodes","columns":["Node","Effect"],"rows":[["Enemy at the Gates","Every Breach is an Unstable Breach"],["Dimensional Foothold","Every Breach is a Hive"],["Massing Forces","10% chance for 2 extra Unstable Breaches"],["Clawed Open","+6s before collapse; 2 Rares when each is stabilised"],["Violent Skirmish","Breach encounters 20% faster"],["Fecund Colony","Bosses 50% chance for an extra Wombgift; Coffers 50% more likely to have Wombgifts"],["Protracted Siege","+2 Hive waves; doubles Ailith skills in non-Fortress Hives"],["Fortified Dominance","Hives 40% more likely to lead to a Fortress; bosses 25% chance to be duplicated"],["Broken Border","+20% chance for Breaches; 20% more Breach Scarabs"],["Swelling Ranks","10% pack size (was 20%); 20% more Wombgifts"],["Evolving Hives","15% more Rare and Magic monsters (was 25%)"],["Adaptive Reaction","Burrow explosion radius 100% more; each burrow: Hive monsters 4% tougher, 2% more Hiveblood and Wombgifts"],["Dimensional Barrier","Turns Breach off; never take it"]],"cite":[7,29,30,31,32,33,45,0]},{"title":"3.29 Breach numbers","columns":["Value","Before","3.29"],"rows":[["Unstable Breaches open at once","3","2"],["Unstable Breach monster packs","-","-15%"],["Progress per Breach kill","-","+25%"],["Swelling Ranks pack size","20%","10%"],["Evolving Hives Rare/Magic","25%","15%"],["Small Magic monster nodes","8%","5%"],["Genesis Equipment max points","20","16"],["Extra-item small nodes","50%","25%"],["Modifier-type notables","500%","300%"]],"cite":[0,17]},{"title":"Genesis Tree point sources","columns":["Source","Gives"],"rows":[["Horned Skull","First Hive or Unstable Breach"],["Strange Limb","Map Hive; 3 Unique points"],["Foul Hand","Map Unstable Breach; 3 Unique points"],["Spiked Limb","Hive Fortress"],["Head of Vruun","Kill Vruun, Marshal of Xesht"],["Breachlord Limbs","Tul and Esh in the Hive Colony; 1 Equipment, 3 Unique, 1 Mysterious"],["Hiveblood spent","Points at 300, 1k, 3k, 6k, 12k, 18k, 30k"]],"cite":[46,50,16]}],"quickCard":["Close every Unstable Breach or lose the reward","Max 2 Unstable Breaches open at once","Vendor Breachstones for Hivebrain Glands","Set a stash tab to Breach affinity","Sell ilvl 84 Lavish; tree the Provisioning","Never take Dimensional Barrier"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 — Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame (patch notes)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07 (notes updated 2026-07-22 and 2026-07-24)","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-patch-notes","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-07-16","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-28-mirage-patch-notes","title":"3.28 Mirage Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-02-26","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-27-keepers-of-the-flame-patch-notes","title":"3.27 Keepers of the Flame Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2025-10-23","patch":"3.27"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/unstable-breach-currency-farming","title":"Unstable Breach Currency Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/breach-league-start-strategy","title":"Breach League Start Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-09-19","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach","title":"Breach","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (shows current 3.29 data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Scarab","title":"Scarab","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (latest league icon Allflame 3.29)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Grasping_Astrolabe","title":"Grasping Astrolabe","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Synthesised_Stability","title":"Synthesised Stability","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Horned_Scarab_of_Bloodlines","title":"Horned Scarab of Bloodlines","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Hivebrain_Gland","title":"Hivebrain Gland","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Chayulas_Breachstone","title":"Chayula's Breachstone","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Flesh_of_Xesht","title":"Flesh of Xesht","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-1-patch-notes","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"3.29.0 Patch Notes (mirror)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"3.28.0 Patch Notes (Mirage) – Keepers of the Flame as a Core League","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (includes Updates for 2026-03-01)","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"3.27.0 Patch Notes (Keepers of the Flame)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.27.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"3.26.0 Patch Notes (Secrets of the Atlas / Mercenaries of Trarthus)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.1","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (forum thread 2026-07-31)","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach_Scarab_of_Instability","title":"Breach Scarab of Instability","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach_Scarab_of_the_Marshal","title":"Breach Scarab of the Marshal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach_Scarab_of_Resonant_Cascade","title":"Breach Scarab of Resonant Cascade","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach_Scarab_of_the_Incensed_Swarm","title":"Breach Scarab of the Incensed Swarm","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Breach_Scarab_of_the_Hive","title":"Breach Scarab of the Hive","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Hive_Colony","title":"Hive Colony (area)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Clawed_Open","title":"Clawed Open (atlas passive)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Massing_Forces","title":"Massing Forces (atlas passive)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Enemy_at_the_Gates","title":"Enemy at the Gates (atlas keystone)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Dimensional_Foothold","title":"Dimensional Foothold (atlas keystone)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Fecund_Colony","title":"Fecund Colony (atlas passive)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=Wombgift","title":"poe.ninja Wombgift price overview (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 snapshot","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Currency","title":"poe.ninja Currency exchange overview (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 snapshot","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Fragment","title":"poe.ninja Fragment exchange overview (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 snapshot","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja Scarab exchange overview (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 snapshot","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://outof.games/realms/pathofexile/economy/wombgifts/","title":"Path of Exile Wombgifts Prices - Allflame League","publisher":"outof.games","date":"unknown (hourly refresh, read 2026-11-04)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.poecurrency.com/news/poe-3-29-budget-scarab-breach-farming-strategy-yields-20-divines-per-hour","title":"PoE 3.29 Budget Scarab Breach Farming Strategy Yields 20 Divines per Hour","publisher":"POECurrency (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-30","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-breach-farming-guide-75-divines-in-20-maps-with-the-best-atlas-setup.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Breach Farming Guide: 75 Divines in 20 Maps","publisher":"MMOexp (currency seller)","date":"2026-09-11","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-breach-fortress-farming-guide-the-best-way-to-farm-blood-gifts-and-currency.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Breach Fortress Farming Guide","publisher":"MMOexp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-15","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://planners.maxroll.gg/profiles/poe/f14ih20i","title":"Maxroll planner 'breach - mid league both trees' (atlas embed used by the Unstable Breach guide)","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-03-24 (planner save date)","patch":"3.28 tree version, linked from 3.29.1 guide"},{"url":"https://planners.maxroll.gg/profiles/poe/cga40fls","title":"Maxroll planner 'Unstable Breach League Start' (Full Atlas variant)","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-24 (planner save date)","patch":"3.29 (variant version 3290)"},{"url":"https://planners.maxroll.gg/profiles/poe/ephnmk0u","title":"Maxroll planner 'B Tier: Breach Fortress Farming' (linked from the tier list)","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-05-14 (planner save date)","patch":"3.28 tree version, linked from 3.29 tier list"},{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grindinggear/atlastree-export/master/data.json","title":"Official atlas passive tree export (node names and stats)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (GitHub)","date":"unknown (values match 3.29 nerfs)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Genesis_Tree","title":"The Genesis Tree","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 node values (300% modifier notables); point-source table still says Graftblood (3.27 wording)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wombgifts","title":"Wombgifts","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current site version Allflame 3.29)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/It_That_Was_Tul","title":"It That Was Tul","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current site version Allflame 3.29)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/It_That_Was_Esh","title":"It That Was Esh","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current site version Allflame 3.29)"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/keepers-of-the-flame-mechanic-guide","title":"Keepers of the Flame Mechanic Guide","publisher":"PoE Vault","date":"2026-03-06","patch":"3.28 (page header shows 3.29)"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/keepers-of-the-flame-mechanic-guide-genesis-tree","title":"Keepers of the Flame Mechanic Guide: Genesis Tree","publisher":"PoE Vault","date":"2026-03-06","patch":"3.28 (page header shows 3.29)"}]},"legion":{"title":"Legion (3.29 rework)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"In 3.29 Incubators are gone. Legion's own reward is now Vestigial uniques: you Enshroud a unique armour piece with a crystal that only map Generals drop, then charge it in the Domain of Timeless Conflict until it turns into a different unique that carries a weaker copy of the donor's signature mod. Run it now because Legion is a cheap mapping strategy, and the crystals, emblems and Vestigial results are all things you can sell.","howTo":[{"text":"Run Legion in maps and break out Generals first. Only Generals in normal maps drop Enshrouding Crystals. They never drop inside the Domain.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,39]},{"text":"Each crystal works on one slot. Karui = gloves, Imperial = boots, Vaal = helmets, Templar = shields, Maraketh = body armours. The faction name gives no hint, so learn the list.","stage":["all"],"cite":[20,21,22,23,24,33,39]},{"text":"Each crystal comes from one General. Marceus Lioneye drops Imperial, Viper Napuatzi drops Vaal, Aukuna drops Maraketh, Queen Hyrri drops Karui and Cardinal Sanctus Vox drops Templar.","stage":["all"],"cite":[40]},{"text":"Right-click the crystal, then left-click a unique to Enshroud it. Crystals stack to 10 and trade on the Currency Exchange.","stage":["all"],"cite":[21,39]},{"text":"Only gloves, boots, helmets, shields and body armours can be Enshrouded. Weapons, rings, amulets and belts cannot. IGGM says only core drop-pool uniques can be converted.","stage":["all"],"cite":[33,40,43]},{"text":"The donor is destroyed and you get a random unique of the same class. You choose the Vestigial mod by choosing the donor, not the result.","stage":["all"],"cite":[40]},{"text":"Second source of Enshrouded uniques: Vagan's Fortification safehouse reward in Betrayal is now a trapped stash of them. This does not apply in Ruthless.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"To open the Domain, put 2 or more different Timeless Emblems in the map device. Each emblem is used up. 100 splinters of one faction make 1 emblem, and using all five is a '5-way'.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26,37,46]},{"text":"The Domain is area level 80. No 3.29 source names a way to push it higher.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[13,36,37]},{"text":"The Domain has four Crystals of Permutation. Put an Enshrouded item in each one. Every kill charges all of them at once, so fill all four.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,39,40]},{"text":"A progress bar fills as you kill and resets at each charge level. No fixed kill count is published. EZG's rough estimate is about 4,000 kills for a Greed's Embrace.","stage":["all"],"cite":[44,43]},{"text":"Once the item is fully charged, either break the crystal out to take the Vestigial unique, or keep charging, up to 3 times, for more Variant Rarity.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[2,16]},{"text":"Domain rewards now show as 100 small crystals in the centre of the screen. Each one equals 3 of the old icons. Kills still give rewards after all 100 are lit.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Reward monsters still exist but are no longer marked. There are no icons above monsters and no bottom icon bar.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"In maps, the encounter releases everything left once you have broken out 90% of its monsters. That includes chests, Sergeants and Generals.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Map routine: use small open maps such as Dunes. Pop shrines and sulphite buffs, break out Generals and Sergeants, then hoards and chests, and loot at the end.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[4,6]},{"text":"Splinters drop only from Legion encounters and from maps that Kingsmarch Atlas Runners complete for you.","stage":["ssf","all"],"cite":[0,45,39]},{"text":"Domain data from poedb: Generals have +500% gold dropped, the monolith pulses every 20 seconds, and monsters can have up to 2 Archnemesis mods.","stage":["late"],"cite":[13]},{"text":"The new Abyss Timeless-style jewels drop from the new Abyss pinnacle boss, which needs four different eyes. AOEAH calls it 'Eye of the Endless'. MMOGAH calls it Zorath.","stage":["late"],"cite":[48,47]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Every emblem gives Domain monsters 10% more damage and 10% more toughness each time they revive.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,26]},{"text":"Each emblem also adds its own per-revive buff. Karui: +50% crit chance and +5% crit multiplier. Maraketh: +5% attack and cast speed. Templar: 3% elemental penetration. Vaal: 5% of physical as extra chaos. Eternal: +10% accuracy and +5% area of effect.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"The longer you stay, the more stacks the waves carry. The 2nd and 3rd charges are fought against heavily stacked monsters.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[39,45]},{"text":"Choose emblems your build resists. Playnews says Templar is safest for capped-res league-start characters, Vaal is worst with negative chaos res, and Eternal hurts evasion builds.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[39]},{"text":"My reading of the notes, not a player report: Karui crit stacks and Templar penetration stacks hit low-defence characters hardest.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Do not take the Sealed Domain notable. It removes Legion from your maps.","stage":["all"],"cite":[39,45]},{"text":"The donor unique is destroyed and the result is random within its class.","stage":["all"],"cite":[40]},{"text":"Launch-week reports of encounters starting early and deleting monsters in stasis are out of date. This was fixed in 3.29.0b on 27 Jul 2026.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[1,17,7]},{"text":"In the Treasures/Eternal Conflict setup, do not scale Legion duration. Chests spread their rewards only once.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[5]}],"sell":[{"text":"Sell Timeless Emblems as sets. The Currency Exchange is the easiest way.","stage":["all"],"cite":[4,5]},{"text":"Sell Enshrouding Crystals on the Currency Exchange. Maraketh (body armour) is by far the most valuable and Vaal (helmet) is second.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[23,20,21,39]},{"text":"Crystal volumes are low and prices move fast. Check before you dump a stack.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[39]},{"text":"Also sell Stacked Decks, scarabs, Nightmare maps and Heist blueprints and contracts from Legion chests.","stage":["all"],"cite":[4,5]},{"text":"poe.ninja has no Vestigial category, so price Vestigial uniques through trade.","stage":["all"],"cite":[14]},{"text":"Early in the league, splinters, emblems and chest currency hold a stable floor. Early Vestigial prices are speculative.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[47]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Maxroll league-start Legion (Milkybk_)","investment":"Low. Rated Easy, average investment, 'Good' profit. The scarabs cost only a few chaos each (rough, poe.ninja, 2 Nov 2026).","stage":["league-start","mid"],"steps":["Run T16 Dunes.","Use Domination shrines and Niko sulphite buffs.","Break out Generals and Sergeants first, then hoards and chests.","Loot after the encounter ends.","Maxroll says the farming method is largely unchanged by the 3.29 reward overhaul."],"atlasPassives":["Monumental (+16% Legion chance)","Constant Battle (+16% Legion chance)","Chain of Command (+2 Sergeants)","War Supplies (+1 War Hoard)"],"scarabs":["3x Legion Scarab","1x Legion Scarab of Officers","1x Cartography Scarab of Escalation"],"cite":[4,6,8,34,15]},{"name":"Eternal Conflict Legion (BawLoch, Maxroll)","investment":"High. Rated 'Great' profit with high management. Scarabs cost roughly 100c per map (rough, poe.ninja, 2 Nov 2026).","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run 8-mod T16 Dunes with Eater of Worlds influence and a Timeless Astrolabe.","Eternal Conflict keeps nearby monsters in stasis, so the Treasures chest spread (20% chance) applies reliably.","Monsters can be broken out several times. Each break is harder and gives more reward.","Do not scale Legion duration on the atlas, because chests spread rewards only once."],"scarabs":["1x Legion Scarab","3x Legion Scarab of Treasures","1x Legion Scarab of Eternal Conflict"],"cite":[5,8,10,30,15]},{"name":"Cheap crystal starter (Playnews)","investment":"Very low. Uses the two cheapest crystals and spare uniques.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Take Face Off and one or two Legion Monolith Chance small nodes.","Farm maps for Karui (gloves) and Imperial (boots) crystals.","Enshroud spare unique gloves and boots.","Move on to helmets and body armours once you have the budget."],"atlasPassives":["Face Off","Legion Monolith Chance (small)"],"cite":[39]},{"name":"Vestigial crafting in the Domain","investment":"Emblems plus crystals. A Maraketh body-armour crystal was about 430c on 4 Nov 2026 (rough).","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Enshroud up to four donors. Choose each donor for its Vestigial mod.","Open the Domain with 2+ different emblems from factions your build can tank.","Fill all four Crystals of Permutation, since every kill charges all of them.","On cheap donors, cash out at the first charge.","On expensive donors (Maraketh body armour), push to 3 charges, but only if you can survive the later revives.","Playnews says the best value is in body armours and helmets.","RPGStash example pairings: Cloak of Flame mod on Lightning Coil, Fourth Vow on Incandescent Heart, Saffell's Frame on Aegis Aurora, Crown of Eyes on Indigon, Stampede on Replica Alberon's Warpath, Darkray Vectors on Ralakesh's Impatience."],"cite":[0,2,16,39,40,23]},{"name":"Timeless Astrolabe General farm","investment":"Medium. Needs a Timeless Astrolabe.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["The Astrolabe adds a Legion-shaped atlas region whose maps get +1 Legion encounter.","Every Legion there comes with a General. You must kill at least one General per encounter to complete the map.","Difficulty and rewards scale with each completed map.","Possible mods: 20-40% Legion duration, 10-15% chance for chests to spread rewards, and 75-100% chance for dropped scarabs to be Legion Scarabs."],"cite":[35]},{"name":"Generals-first splinter and crystal farm","investment":"Atlas points only.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Aim to meet as many Generals as possible, not to kill as many Legion monsters as possible.","Generals drop the most splinters and are the only crystal source. Sergeants come next. Normal monsters drop no splinters.","Face Off: 60% more chance of a General, and encounters that roll one get both.","Take the 20% General chance small node and the 10% more General splinters small node.","Emblematic is now only 0.3%. Map item quantity now helps Sergeant and chest splinters less."],"atlasPassives":["Face Off","Legion General Chance (small, 20%)","General Splinter Amount (small, 10%)","Emblematic (0.3%)","Monumental","Constant Battle"],"scarabs":["Legion Scarab of Officers"],"cite":[0,9,27,34,39]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough scarab prices: Legion Scarab ~2.4c, Officers ~4.4c, Treasures ~15.9c, Eternal Conflict ~52c. That makes the league-start setup cheap and the Eternal Conflict setup ~100c per map.","who":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","cite":[15]},{"text":"Rough crystal values (US realm, 24h): Maraketh ~430c (1.82 div), Vaal ~47.9c, Templar ~20.2c, Karui ~17.6c, Imperial ~15.2c.","who":"PoEDB","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[23,20,21]},{"text":"Rough: the same crystal ranking held in August. Maraketh was far ahead, Vaal second, and the other three were within a few chaos of each other.","who":"Playnews (citing PoEDB)","date":"2026-08-10","cite":[39]},{"text":"Rough and anecdotal: high-end Vestigial results sell for anywhere from a few to hundreds of divines. Players reportedly made 100+ div in about 6 hours of Domain charging. This is not a measured per-hour rate.","who":"EZG","date":"2026-08-10 (modified 2026-09-18)","cite":[44]},{"text":"After 3.29.2, the best value is in body armours and helmets, if you pay the Maraketh crystal's entry cost.","who":"Playnews","date":"2026-08-11","cite":[39]},{"text":"Profit ratings: the league-start setup is rated 'Good' and the Eternal Conflict setup 'Great'.","who":"Maxroll (Milkybk_ / BawLoch)","date":"2026-07-24 / 2026-08-03","cite":[4,5]},{"text":"About 498 Vestigial variants exist, each with a fixed donor mod. Examples: the Kaom's Heart variant gives +200 max Life and the Cospri's Will variant gives an extra Curse.","who":"poedb","date":"unknown","cite":[25]},{"text":"The Matryoshka divination card now gives an item level 86 Vestigial unique.","who":"GGG 3.29.0 patch notes","date":"2026-07","cite":[0]},{"text":"Legion is rated the top early pick in 3.29 for its high monster count and cheap setup.","who":"MMOGAH","date":"3.29 launch (exact date unknown)","cite":[47]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"6 Aug 2026: items can be charged up to 3 times, and each charge adds Variant Rarity. You can break out and take the result after the first full charge.","cite":[2,16]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Fixed the Vestigial Gravebind implicit, which previously did nothing.","cite":[2]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Added four Crystals of Permutation to the Domain. Enshrouded uniques placed in them turn into Vestigial uniques, which are exclusive to Legion.","cite":[0,3,19]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Added five Enshrouding Crystals (Karui, Imperial, Maraketh, Templar, Vaal). They drop only from map Generals.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Incubators can no longer be obtained. Rog's Incubator craft, the Incubator stash affinity and the Timeless Delirium Orb were removed. Existing copies in Standard still work.","cite":[0,3]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Older guides that call Incubators a key Legion reward are out of date. Matryoshka and The Catch no longer give Incubated items.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Unrelenting Timeless Emblems were removed, and existing ones were converted to regular emblems.","cite":[0,3]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"All emblems now share the same base mods: +10% XP, +20% reward progress, monsters deal 10% more damage and gain 10% toughness per revive. Each faction also adds its own per-revive buff.","cite":[0,26]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Domain reward icons were removed and replaced by 100 centre crystals, each worth 3 old icons. Guides that tell you to target monsters by icon are out of date.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Map encounters now release everything left once 90% of the monsters are broken out.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Splinters now come only from Legion and from Kingsmarch Atlas Runner maps. Normal monsters drop none and Generals drop more. Sergeants and chests drop them less often but in bigger stacks, and map item quantity affects them less.","cite":[0,3]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"The Heist rogue-equipment splinter-duplication mod is gone. Trinkets that gave extra Legion items now give extra gold.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Emblematic was cut to 0.3% (from 0.6%). The small node before it now gives 10% more splinters from Generals.","cite":[0,9]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"The Logistical Support and Pillaged Treasures small nodes no longer duplicate splinters. Atlas guides that rely on this are out of date.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Vagan's Fortification safehouse reward is now a trapped stash of Enshrouded uniques (not in Ruthless).","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Domain area level is unclear. Old guides used Unrelenting emblems to reach level 84, and those emblems are gone. One reading of the 3.22 rules gives a max of 82, while PoEDB's note says no emblem adds levels. Assume 80.","cite":[8,0,36,37]},{"patch":"3.29.0b","text":"27 Jul 2026: fixed encounters starting early and deleting monsters still in stasis.","cite":[1,17,7]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Legion Scarab of Command was renamed Legion Scarab of Treasures and now gives chests a 20% chance to pass rewards to monsters. Possessed Legion monsters no longer release Tormented Spirits.","cite":[18,30]}],"tables":[{"title":"Enshrouding Crystals","columns":["Crystal","Slot","Dropped by","PoEDB value 4 Nov 2026 (rough)"],"rows":[["Maraketh","Body armour","Aukuna the Black Sekhema","~430c (1.82 div)"],["Vaal","Helmet","Viper Napuatzi","~47.9c"],["Templar","Shield","Cardinal Sanctus Vox","~20.2c"],["Karui","Gloves","Queen Hyrri Ngamaku","~17.6c"],["Imperial","Boots","Marceus Lioneye","~15.2c"]],"cite":[20,21,22,23,24,33,40]},{"title":"Emblem per-revive monster buffs (on top of base +10% dmg, +10% toughness)","columns":["Emblem","Per-revive buff","Playnews note"],"rows":[["Karui","+50% crit chance, +5% crit multiplier","-"],["Maraketh","+5% attack and cast speed","-"],["Templar","3% elemental penetration","Safest for capped-res league starters"],["Vaal","5% phys as extra chaos","Worst with negative chaos res"],["Eternal","+10% accuracy, +5% area of effect","Hurts evasion builds"]],"cite":[0,39]},{"title":"Legion scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Effect","Limit","poe.ninja 2 Nov 2026 (rough)"],"rows":[["Legion Scarab","+1 Legion encounter","up to 5","~2.4c"],["Officers","+5 Sergeants per faction","1","~4.4c"],["Treasures","Chests: 20% chance to pass rewards to released monsters (harder)","up to 3","~15.9c"],["Eternal Conflict","Monsters can be broken out multiple times, harder and more rewarding each time","1","~52c"]],"cite":[28,29,30,10,15]},{"title":"Legion atlas nodes (PoEDB, 3.29)","columns":["Node","Effect"],"rows":[["Monumental","+16% Legion chance, 16% more Legion Scarabs"],["Constant Battle","+16% Legion chance, 16% more Legion Scarabs"],["Face Off","60% more General chance; encounters with a General get both"],["Chain of Command","+2 Sergeants, +20% Sergeant reward chance"],["War Supplies","+1 War Hoard"],["Protracted Battle","40% longer encounters; monsters in stasis take 50% more damage"],["Pillaged Treasures","+1 random reward in chests"],["Logistical Support","50% more life per extra reward"],["Emblematic","0.3% splinters drop as emblems (was 0.6%)"],["Timeless Conflict (keystone)","No timer, starts after a Schism; older Maxroll guide says lower profit"],["Sealed Domain","Removes Legion from maps; avoid"],["Small nodes","Monolith +8%, General 20%, General splinters 10%, Duplicate splinter 5%, Sergeant reward 6%, Chest break-out range 20%, Duration 20%, Vaal Legion 75%"]],"cite":[34,27,0,9,39,8,6]},{"title":"Best donors by slot (RPGStash)","columns":["Slot","Donors (Vestigial mod)"],"rows":[["Body armour","Dialla's Malefaction (+2 red-socket gem levels or +20% green quality), Belly of the Beast (20% max life), Skin of the Loyal/Lords (50% global defences), Cloak of Flame (20% phys taken as fire), The Fourth Vow (20% armour vs chaos hits)"],["Helmet","Thrillsteel (Onslaught on kill), Crown of Eyes (Arcane Might on attacks), Honourhome (+2 socketed gems), Abyssus (+50% melee crit multi), The Formless Flame (armour from overcapped fire res)"],["Gloves","Meginord's Vise (melee splash), Maligaro's Virtuosity (50% crit chance), Admiral's Arrogance (max rage chance), Null and Void (Rampage), Aurseize (40% rarity)"],["Boots","The Stampede (150% base move speed), Annihilation's Approach (no chill/freeze), Mutewind Whispersteps (70% spell crit), Kaom's Roots (action speed floor), Legacy of Fury (scorch nearby)"],["Shield","The Squire (+30% support quality), Atziri's Reflection (unaffected by curses), Magna Eclipsis (Elemental Aegis), Matua Tupuna (10% non-curse aura effect), Saffell's Frame (+2 all max res)"]],"cite":[40]},{"title":"Vestigial tier lists (build value, not price)","columns":["Tier","Uniques"],"rows":[["S","Dialla's Malefaction, Aegis Aurora, The Iron Fortress"],["A","Crown of Eyes, Belly of the Beast, Seven-League Step, Inpulsa's Broken Heart"]],"cite":[41,42]},{"title":"Timeless jewels","columns":["Faction","Jewel","Note"],"rows":[["Vaal","Glorious Vanity","Keystones: Divine Flesh, Immortal Ambition, Corrupted Soul"],["Karui","Lethal Pride","Large radius, 1 Historic"],["Maraketh","Brutal Restraint","Large radius, 1 Historic"],["Templar","Militant Faith","Large radius, 1 Historic"],["Eternal","Elegant Hubris","Large radius, 1 Historic"],["Kalguuran","Heroic Tragedy","-"],["Abyss: Tecrod","Festering Vengeance","Abyss jewel; keystone Overwhelming Hate (20% less life, Rage gives up to 30% more attack dmg)"],["Abyss: Ulaman","Extinguishing Grasp","Abyss jewel, 1 Historic"],["Abyss: Kurgal","Baleful Dominion","Abyss jewel, 1 Historic"],["Abyss: Amanamu","Destructive Aspiration","Abyss jewel, 1 Historic"],["Abyss: Zorath","Reclaimed Malevolence","Vendor recipe from all four"]],"cite":[12,11,31,32,38]}],"quickCard":["Break Generals first: only map Generals drop crystals","Karui gloves, Imperial boots, Vaal helm, Templar shield, Maraketh body","Domain: 2+ different emblems, fill all 4 crystals","Cheap donor: take it at charge 1. Pricey: push to 3","Pick emblems your build resists; revives stack","Sell emblems in sets; price Vestigials on trade"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 — Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"July 2026","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3989412","title":"3.29.0b Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29.0b"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-reveal-summary","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Reveal Summary","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/legion","title":"Legion League Start Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/eternal-conflict-legion-farming","title":"Eternal Conflict Legion Farming","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/legion-farming-guide","title":"Legion Farming Guide","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2025-06-18","patch":"3.24"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/upcoming-changes-and-farming-strategies-in-3-29","title":"Upcoming Changes and Farming Strategies in 3.29","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-29","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion_league","title":"Legion league","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Emblematic","title":"Emblematic (Atlas passive)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion_Scarab_of_Eternal_Conflict","title":"Legion Scarab of Eternal Conflict","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Lethal_Pride","title":"Lethal Pride (Timeless Jewel)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Timeless_Jewel","title":"Timeless Jewel","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Domain_of_Timeless_Conflict","title":"Domain of Timeless Conflict","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Fragment","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview – Fragments (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview – Scarabs (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994130","title":"Path of Exile 1: Curse of the Allflame Improvements","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-05","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3989358","title":"What We're Working On - Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Content Update 3.28.0 — Path of Exile: Mirage","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Allflame_league","title":"Allflame league overview","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vaal_Enshrouding_Crystal","title":"Vaal Enshrouding Crystal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Karui_Enshrouding_Crystal","title":"Karui Enshrouding Crystal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Imperial_Enshrouding_Crystal","title":"Imperial Enshrouding Crystal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Maraketh_Enshrouding_Crystal","title":"Maraketh Enshrouding Crystal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Templar_Enshrouding_Crystal","title":"Templar Enshrouding Crystal","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vestigial","title":"Vestigial Uniques list","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Timeless_Karui_Emblem","title":"Timeless Karui Emblem","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Atlas_passive_skill","title":"Atlas passive skill stats list","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion_Scarab","title":"Legion Scarab","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion_Scarab_of_Officers","title":"Legion Scarab of Officers","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion_Scarab_of_Treasures","title":"Legion Scarab of Treasures","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28+"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Glorious_Vanity","title":"Glorious Vanity","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Festering_Vengeance","title":"Festering Vengeance (Abyss Timeless jewel)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Enshrouded_Item","title":"Enshrouded Item","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Legion","title":"Legion (atlas passives, astrolabe, splinters)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Timeless_Astrolabe","title":"Timeless Astrolabe","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Timeless_Conflict","title":"Timeless Conflict","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Emblem","title":"Emblem","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Festering_Vengeance","title":"Festering Vengeance","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.playnews.gg/en/guides/path-of-exile-3-29-the-permutation-crystals-guide-to-transform-a-unique-into-a-vestigial-unique","title":"Path of Exile 3.29: the Permutation Crystals guide to transform a unique into a Vestigial unique","publisher":"Playnews","date":"2026-08-11","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.rpgstash.com/blog/poe-vestigial-mods-guide","title":"PoE 3.29 Vestigial Mods: Complete Guide and Best Modifiers","publisher":"RPGStash","date":"2026-09-10","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4718--poe-329-best-vestigial-uniques-tier-list--implicit-mods","title":"PoE 3.29 Best Vestigial Uniques Tier List & Implicit Mods","publisher":"AOEAH","date":"2026-07-28","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mtmmo.com/news/2301--poe-329-vestigial-uniques-tier-list--best-vestigial-uniques--mods-in-path-of-exile","title":"PoE 3.29 Vestigial Uniques Tier List","publisher":"MTMMO","date":"2026-08-18","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.iggm.com/news/poe-3-29-vestigial-unique-crafting-enshrouding-crystals-variant-rarity","title":"PoE 3.29 Vestigial Unique Crafting: Enshrouding Crystals & Variant Rarity","publisher":"IGGM","date":"2026-09-07","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.ezg.com/blog/poe-3-29-players-turning-5-ways-into-new-unique-item-goldmine","title":"PoE 3.29 players turning 5-Ways into new unique item goldmine","publisher":"EZG","date":"2026-08-10","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4712--best-poe-329-legion-farming-strategy-atlas--build","title":"Best PoE 3.29 Legion Farming Strategy, Atlas & Build","publisher":"AOEAH","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-legion-farming-guide","title":"PoE 3.29 Legion Farming Guide","publisher":"Timesaver.gg","date":"2026-08-27","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.mmogah.com/news/poe/stop-farming-wrong-poe-329-best-farming-strategies-new-money-makers","title":"Stop Farming Wrong! PoE 3.29 Best Farming Strategies & New Money-Makers","publisher":"MMOGAH","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4716--poe-329-abyss-farm-guide-jewel-mods-atlas-scarab--map-strategy","title":"PoE 3.29 Abyss Farm Guide","publisher":"AOEAH","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"}]},"abyss":{"title":"Abyss (3.29 rework)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"In 3.29 Abyss pits are already open when you enter a map. Kills inside a pit's range feed it souls until an Abyssal legion comes out, and sealing the Abyss leaves troves and chests behind. After the 3.29.1 and 3.29.2 buffs, Abyss is the only source of Abyssal Jewels and Stygian Vises. It also leads to Abyssal Depths Liches and the new pinnacle boss Zorath, whose drops (Historic jewels, Eyes, ilvl 86 jewel bases) sell well.","howTo":[{"text":"Pits and their cracks are already open when you arrive. Monsters in their range start out subjugated. You no longer chase a moving crack.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,7,8,16]},{"text":"Kill monsters inside a pit's range to send their souls into it. When it has enough souls, the Abyssal legion comes out. The patch notes give no kill count.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,16]},{"text":"Abysses spread over a whole section of the map. Enough kills spawn special Abyss enemies with extra loot, and those lead to the Abyss chests.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9]},{"text":"Kill the monsters that emerge to seal the Abyss. Treasure troves then spawn along it.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7,13]},{"text":"Focus on the rares and elites. After 3.29.2, magic Abyss monsters still drop almost nothing of value (MMOEXP).","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[47]},{"text":"The last Abyss in an area can open an Abyssal Depths dungeon instead. Its Lich boss is Ulaman or Amanamu (area level 78 per PoEDB).","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[13,14]},{"text":"Abyss Scarab of Descending (limit 1) guarantees an Abyssal Depths in the map.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[14,18,24]},{"text":"Since 3.29.1 there is no spire side-room phase. Just kill the Lich, then open the 3 reward chests it leaves.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1,2]},{"text":"Relic pit-count mods give Abysses that do not lead to a Depths at least 3 or exactly 4 pits. Timesaver says a 4-pit Abyss in a level 78+ zone has a small chance to open the Depths.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[13,43]},{"text":"Lightless Astrolabe: maps in its Shaped Region get 1 extra Abyss. Every Abyss must be done for a map to count, and Abyss monsters scale up with each completed map in the region.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[20,13]},{"text":"Zorath, Vile Assembled is the new pinnacle boss. You fight him in The Lightless Hollow (area level 84, no XP gain or loss, minimap revealed) after using a Zorath's Eye in a personal Map Device.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21,30,15,7]},{"text":"There are four Eyes: Malevolence, Authority, Endless and Inevitable. allthings.how (single source) says each one drops from a specific Lich and that you need all four.","stage":["late"],"cite":[15,31,32,33,41]},{"text":"Zorath and the Depths Liches have +15000% item rarity and +100% experience on kill.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21,38]},{"text":"The four Historic Eye jewels drop from Zorath and cannot be chanced. Vendor one of each to get Reclaimed Malevolence.","stage":["late"],"cite":[42,35]},{"text":"Maxroll: the Coral Reef chart room's Abyss Pit always drops a Merrick's Ducat.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[12]},{"text":"To turn Abyss off, take Loved by the Sun. You get no Abysses, no Abyss Scarab drops, and +2% chance for other content.","stage":["all"],"cite":[13,19,4]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Abyss rares hit hard. Put survivability ahead of clear speed in juiced maps.","stage":["league-start","ssf","mid"],"cite":[41]},{"text":"Avoid cannot regenerate, no leech and reduced recovery map mods. Prefer open layouts.","stage":["league-start","ssf","mid"],"cite":[41]},{"text":"Since 3.29.1, crystal spires in Lich arenas fire beams at each other. Dodge them.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Liches have about 21M base life, 40% elemental and 25% chaos resistance, and heal 1% each time they lose a Spirit Charge. Kill them fast.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[38,39]},{"text":"Amanamu: Maim thrust, a 4-second piercing channelled Incinerate, a lightning beam, and a pillar that summons minions.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[39]},{"text":"Zorath has about 215.9M base life and 149,751 armour, 50% elemental and 30% chaos resistance, and cannot be knocked back.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21]},{"text":"Zorath's Head Slam leaves burning ground for 6s and Vomit Ground deals about 2,650 base physical damage per second for 10s. He also has a beam, piercing Dagger Breath and Flame Breath.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21]},{"text":"The Lightless Hollow also has Crystal Phylacteries (about 282k life) and Volatile Skeletons (about 35k life). Skeletons give no loot or XP.","stage":["late"],"cite":[30,21]},{"text":"Bug (1 Nov 2026): if Alva's Time Portal spawns on the Depths pit, the Depths entrance may never open. Running Incursion Scarabs with Descending is at your own risk.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"Propagation: some mobs can become unkillable.","stage":["late"],"cite":[45]},{"text":"Abyss chest icons are hard to read, and opened chests are hard to tell from unopened ones. Lower the minimap terrain transparency.","stage":["all"],"cite":[28]},{"text":"Old guides are wrong for 3.29: crack chasing, Abyssal Delirium Orbs, the Edifice and Profound Depth names, and clearing spires first are all gone.","stage":["all"],"cite":[13,14,0,2]}],"sell":[{"text":"Keep item level 86 Murderous, Searching and Ghastly Eye bases (about 10 div each) and ilvl 86 Hypnotic (about 2,061c). Bases at ilvl 85 and below sell for only 1-11c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[57]},{"text":"Only ilvl 83-84 Stygian Vises hold value. Vendor low-level ones. A corrupted 6-mod Abyss Jewel is the top prize (allthings.how).","stage":["all"],"cite":[41]},{"text":"Historic jewels: Reclaimed Malevolence about 85 div, Festering Vengeance 27.5, Extinguishing Grasp 20, Baleful Dominion 14, Destructive Aspiration 12 div.","stage":["late"],"cite":[54,53]},{"text":"Zorath's Eyes: Inevitable about 4.8 div, Endless about 2.3 div, Authority about 110c, Malevolence about 80c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[51,49]},{"text":"Zorath's own uniques are cheap: Subsume the Source about 1 div, Spinesnatch about 80c.","stage":["late"],"cite":[55,56]},{"text":"Players call Subsume the Source a niche, high-cost item. It is mainly for stacking crit multi, accuracy or minion physical damage.","stage":["late"],"cite":[27]},{"text":"Most older Abyss uniques are worth 1-2c. The exception is the 1-jewel Shroud of the Lightless at about 9 div.","stage":["all"],"cite":[55,58]},{"text":"Abyss Scarab prices: Abyss about 12.2c, Consort 11.4c, Multitudes 6.5c, Descending 2.2c, Crystals 0.5c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[52]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Scarab-juiced Abyss maps (allthings.how setup)","investment":"Low: about 40c of scarabs per map (poe.ninja prices, 4 Nov 2026)","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run T16 maps (area level 78+) with good pack size. Timesaver cites about 2 to 2.5 min per map for a fast mapper.","Slot 2 Abyss Scarabs, 2 Abyss Scarabs of Multitudes and 1 Abyss Scarab of Descending.","Amanamu-loyal Abysses are a solid default. Kurgal or Ulaman are worth trying.","Prefer open layouts. Skip maps with no-regen, no-leech or reduced-recovery mods.","Clear each pit's range and kill every rare and elite, because they drop the loot.","Finish in the Depths: kill the Lich and open all 3 reward chests."],"atlasPassives":["Trail of Destruction (pit count rolled twice, keep the higher)","Sustained Horde (20% chance for 3 extra pits)","Inspired Darkness (pits twice as likely to have rewards)","Reactive Swarm (4% more monsters per pit already closed)","Darkness Rising (5% chance per earlier pit that all monsters are at least Magic)","Abyssal Army (+50% XP, +25% monsters)","Awakened Depths (+100% Depths chance)"],"scarabs":["Abyss Scarab x2","Abyss Scarab of Multitudes x2","Abyss Scarab of Descending x1"],"cite":[41,43,47,52,13,19,2]},{"name":"Abyssal Depths and Zorath's Eye farming","investment":"Low to medium: Descending costs about 2.2c a map, and the Eyes sell for about 80c to 4.8 div","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Abyss Scarab of Descending in every map to guarantee a Depths.","Take Awakened Depths and the 15% small Depths node so maps without the scarab can open Depths too.","Kill the Lich quickly. It has about 21M base life and heals 1% each time it loses a Spirit Charge (3 max).","Dodge the beams the crystal spires fire at each other in the arena.","Open all 3 reward chests.","Per allthings.how (single source), each Lich can drop a specific Eye. Sell the cheap Eyes or keep a set for Zorath."],"atlasPassives":["Awakened Depths","Abyssal Depths Chance small node (15%)","Underground Kingdom (+2% Abyss chance per 2% Pack Size)"],"scarabs":["Abyss Scarab of Descending x1"],"cite":[14,18,19,38,39,2,41,51]},{"name":"Lightless Astrolabe region","investment":"Unknown: these sources give no Astrolabe price","stage":["late"],"steps":["Apply a Lightless Astrolabe to an Atlas quadrant to make a Shaped Region of Abyss maps.","Each map in the region gets 1 extra Abyss.","Complete every Abyss in a map or it does not count.","Abyss monsters get harder and more rewarding with each completed map in the region.","Look for these mods: 2 extra pits, 50% chance for 3 extra pits, 2-4 extra rares, 50-100% Depths chance, Area contains an Abyssal Depths, 10-15% more monsters, 75-100% chance for Abyss Scarabs.","GGG updated its Abyss mods on 24 Jul 2026 to fit the new combat."],"cite":[20,13,0]},{"name":"Abyss Propagation","investment":"High: MMOEXP cites about 10 div (Wisp) to 20 div (Risk) per 20 maps. The Ember costs about 380c each.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use a City Square map rolled for 88%+ more scarabs, inside a Lightless Astrolabe region.","Add 1 Allflame Ember of Propagation. When its pack members die while Rare, they spread their mods to other Rares.","Add 2 Nemesis Scarabs, an optional Betrayal Scarab of the Allflame, and a Wisp or Risk Scarab. This setup uses no Abyss Scarabs.","Boss-rush the map first and clear everything except the Abyss.","Run the Abyss last, pit by pit, so the spread mods land on Abyss rares.","Headhunter is strongly recommended. Some mobs can become unkillable.","Maxroll rates it near the bottom of A tier: rewarding but very hard. MMOEXP says it pays best around league day 3-4."],"scarabs":["Nemesis Scarab x2","Betrayal Scarab of the Allflame (optional)","Wisp Scarab or Risk Scarab x1","Allflame Ember of Propagation x1"],"cite":[11,45,46,40,50]}],"profit":[{"text":"Abyss Propagation, 20-map test: about 1.5-2 div profit per map. The Wisp setup cost about 10 div and returned about 45 div. The Risk setup cost about 20 div and returned about 55 div. (Rough figures.)","who":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-05","cite":[45]},{"text":"Claims 25-30 div/hour for both Propagation and raw-currency Abyss. The author admits it needs more testing. (Rough figures.)","who":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-07","cite":[46,47]},{"text":"Jungle Valley Propagation: about 60.5 maps/hour and 63 div of loot/hour, with a headline of 36 div/hour net. At the stated cost of about 0.9 div per map, the net would be closer to 9 div/hour. (Rough figures; they do not add up.)","who":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-13","cite":[48]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Abyssal Crystals now shatter when the final pit closes. This is visual only.","cite":[5]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Elites drop more items and give more XP. More elites spawn, and they are more effective.","cite":[3,4]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Amanamu-loyal Abysses now spawn only the Lightless Abomination, which drops more and gives more XP.","cite":[4]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Scarab of Crystals now makes a crystal on every non-final pit close.","cite":[3,4]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"The Trail of Destruction double roll now also applies to bonus-pit chances such as Sustained Horde.","cite":[4,19]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"No more Abysses inside Breach Hives. Fixed a rare bug where an Abyss blocked a Ritual.","cite":[4]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Fixed Underground Kingdom spawning Abysses while Loved by the Sun was allocated.","cite":[4]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Lich immunity phases (spire side rooms) removed. Lich life raised 25%, and the arena now has spire beams.","cite":[1,2]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Killing the Depths boss spawns 3 reward chests.","cite":[1,2]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Abyss chests drop more consistently and give more and better loot, especially Currency and Scarabs. Greater chests now stand out more.","cite":[1,2]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Passive tree nodes affected by an Abyss Jewel now have their own border visuals.","cite":[1,2]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Pits and cracks start already open, and crack chasing is gone.","cite":[0,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Abyss is now the only source of Abyssal Jewels and Stygian Vises. Jewels can still rarely drop in Delve Abyss biomes.","cite":[0,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Abyssal Delirium Orbs can no longer be obtained.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Removed jewel mods: damage, minion damage and physical damage reduction against Abyssal Monsters, plus physical damage reduction if not hit recently.","cite":[0,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Jewel top tiers raised: Cold/Lightning ailment effect 15 to 20%, Minion Movement Speed 10 to 15%, recoup as Mana 3 to 5%, Unholy Might 5 to 8%, Elusive ailment avoid 10 to 20%.","cite":[0,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Added spell damage buffed: Fire to Spells 23-32 becomes 30-42, Lightning 6-45 becomes 8-59. Shield, 2H and dual-wield versions got the same buff.","cite":[0,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Maximum Mana roll cut from +40 to +34. Impale effect raised from 6 to 8%, but it no longer rolls on Hypnotic or Ghastly Eye.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"The Abyss Scarab limit goes from 2 to 5. Extra-Abyss effects in an area that already has an Abyss add 2 pits instead.","cite":[0,18]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Scarab of Edifice is renamed to Crystals and Profound Depth to the Consort.","cite":[0,18]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"The Abyss Atlas clusters and Lightless Astrolabe mods were reworked. The patch notes list no values.","cite":[0,20]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"New Abyss pinnacle boss with its own uniques.","cite":[0,7]},{"patch":"3.29.0b","text":"Hotfix 4: fixed Mercenaries equipping items with more Abyss sockets than allowed, and Energy Blade with Abyss-socket swords.","cite":[17]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"On 27 Jul 2026 GGG said Abyss rewards, and sometimes its combat and density, missed the mark. Fixes followed.","cite":[6,10]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Abyss Scarab of Descending was added. Ancient Conflict scarab chance went from 3 to 10%. Tujen no longer sells Abyss jewels.","cite":[24,19]},{"patch":"3.27.0","text":"Scarab of Edifice spawned Minor Stygian Spires. 3.29 replaced this with Crystals.","cite":[25,0]},{"patch":"3.26.0","text":"Multitudes was cut to 50% increased monsters. In 3.29 it is 100% more per soul fed.","cite":[26,18]}],"tables":[{"title":"Abyss Scarabs (prices from poe.ninja, 4 Nov 2026)","columns":["Scarab","Limit","Effect","Price"],"rows":[["Abyss Scarab","5","Adds an Abyss, or 2 pits if the area already has one","~12.2c"],["Abyss Scarab of Multitudes","2","100% more monsters per soul fed","~6.5c"],["Abyss Scarab of Crystals","1","Non-final pits make an Abyssal Crystal on closing; later monsters are harder and more rewarding","~0.5c"],["Abyss Scarab of the Consort","1","One pit spawns an Abyssal Consort, stronger and more rewarding for each pit opened before it","~11.4c"],["Abyss Scarab of Descending","1","Guarantees an Abyssal Depths","~2.2c"]],"cite":[0,18,36,37,3,4,52]},{"title":"Abyss Atlas passives (PoEDB)","columns":["Node","Effect"],"rows":[["Trail of Destruction","Rolls the pit count twice and keeps the higher; since 3.29.2 this includes bonus-pit chances"],["Sustained Horde","20% chance for 3 extra pits"],["Inspired Darkness","Pits twice as likely to have rewards"],["Reactive Swarm","4% more monsters per pit already closed"],["Darkness Rising","5% chance per earlier pit that all monsters are at least Magic"],["Abyssal Army","+50% Abyss XP, +25% monsters"],["Corrupted Gaze","Abyss Jewels have a 20% chance to drop corrupted with 5-6 mods"],["Skittering Darkness","Abyssal Skitterlocks (scarab chests) can replace Troves"],["Votive Hoard","Troves have a 20% chance to drop a rare item with an Abyssal Socket"],["Awakened Depths","+100% Abyssal Depths chance"],["Underground Kingdom","+2% Abyss chance per 2% Pack Size"],["Loved by the Sun","No Abyss, no Abyss Scarab drops, +2% other content"],["Small nodes","+8%/+12% Abyss chance, 5% more monsters, 15% extra pit chance, +1 rare, 10% more jewels, 15% Depths chance"]],"cite":[13,19,4,23]},{"title":"Zorath's Eyes","columns":["Eye","Jewel base link","Drops from (allthings.how, unconfirmed)","Price 4 Nov"],"rows":[["Malevolence","Murderous","Ulaman","~80c"],["Authority","Searching","Amanamu","~110c"],["Endless","Ghastly","Catarina","~942c"],["Inevitable","Hypnotic","Kurgal","~1,986c"]],"cite":[15,31,32,33,41,51]},{"title":"Historic Abyss jewels (drop from Zorath)","columns":["Jewel","Lord","Keystone","Price 4 Nov"],"rows":[["Festering Vengeance","Tecrod","Overwhelming Hate","~27.5 div"],["Extinguishing Grasp","Ulaman","Weighted Exchange","~20 div"],["Baleful Dominion","Kurgal","Reconstructed Essence","~14 div"],["Destructive Aspiration","Amanamu","The Loyal Few","~12 div"],["Reclaimed Malevolence","Zorath","Not listed (vendor recipe: one of each of the four above)","~85 div"]],"cite":[13,44,42,35,54]},{"title":"Abyssal Jewel roll changes in 3.29.0","columns":["Mod","Old top","New top"],"rows":[["Cold/Lightning ailment effect","15%","20%"],["Minion Movement Speed","10%","15%"],["Damage taken recouped as Mana","3%","5%"],["Unholy Might on Melee Kill","5%","8%"],["Avoid ele ailments while Elusive","10%","20%"],["Impale effect","6%","8% (not on Hypnotic/Ghastly)"],["Maximum Mana","+40","+34"],["Added Fire Damage to Spells","23-32","30-42"],["Added Lightning Damage to Spells","6-45","8-59"]],"cite":[0,16]}],"quickCard":["Pits start open: kill in range to feed souls","Kill rares/elites; magic mobs drop little","Seal it, then loot troves and chests","Descending = Depths: Lich, 3 chests","Lich: burst fast, dodge spire beams","Keep ilvl 86 jewel bases and Zorath Eyes"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 — Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame (patch notes)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-16/17 (updates for 2026-07-22 and 2026-07-24 appended)","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991633","title":"Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes 3.29.1 Preview","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991672","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994130","title":"Curse of the Allflame Improvements","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-05","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-05/06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3989358","title":"What We're Working On - Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-reveal-summary","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Reveal Summary","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-patch-notes","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-22","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/poe-3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-league-branch-update","title":"PoE 3.29 Curse of the Allflame League Branch Update","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/upcoming-changes-and-farming-strategies-in-3-29","title":"Upcoming Changes and Farming Strategies in 3.29","publisher":"Maxroll (Cptn Garbage, reviewed by Crouching_Tuna)","date":"2026-07-29","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-09-19 (tier list updated 2026-08-11)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/curse-of-the-allflame-farming-strategy","title":"Curse of the Allflame Farming Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyss","title":"Abyss","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (data includes 3.29 scarab names)","patch":"3.29 data (page header shows Abyss league v3.1)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyssal_Depths","title":"Abyssal Depths","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (data includes Scarab of Descending)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Zoraths_Eye_of_Malevolence","title":"Zorath's Eye of Malevolence","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (internal name AbyssPinnacleKey)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3990687","title":"3.29.0b Hotfix 4","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-29","patch":"3.29.0b"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyss_Scarab","title":"Abyss Scarab","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Atlas_passive_skill","title":"Atlas passive skill","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Lightless_Astrolabe","title":"Lightless Astrolabe","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Zorath%2C_Vile_Assembled","title":"Zorath, Vile Assembled","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Subsume_the_Source","title":"Subsume the Source","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyssal_Skitterlock","title":"Abyssal Skitterlock","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown (~2026-02/03)","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown (before 2025-10-24)","patch":"3.27.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown (~2025-06)","patch":"3.26.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/4012283","title":"I feel like Subsume the Source abyss helmet is held hostage by 1~ BIS modifier","publisher":"Official forum (players)","date":"2026-10-31","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/4011733","title":"Visual Clarity abyss icons on map/minimap etc","publisher":"Official forum (players)","date":"2026-10-25","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/4012346","title":"Time Portal on Abyssal Depths","publisher":"Official forum (bug report)","date":"2026-11-01","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Lightless_Hollow","title":"The Lightless Hollow","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Zoraths_Eye_of_Authority","title":"Zorath's Eye of Authority","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Zoraths_Eye_of_the_Endless","title":"Zorath's Eye of the Endless","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Zoraths_Eye_of_the_Inevitable","title":"Zorath's Eye of the Inevitable","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Spinesnatch","title":"Spinesnatch","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Reclaimed_Malevolence","title":"Reclaimed Malevolence","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (has 3.29.2 version history)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyss_Scarab_of_Crystals","title":"Abyss Scarab of Crystals","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Abyssal_Consort","title":"Abyssal Consort","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Ulaman%2C_Sovereign_of_the_Well","title":"Ulaman, Sovereign of the Well","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Amanamu%2C_Liege_of_the_Lightless","title":"Amanamu, Liege of the Lightless","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Allflame_ember","title":"Allflame Item list","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://allthings.how/path-of-exile-3-29-abyss-how-the-rework-works-and-how-to-farm-it/","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Abyss: How the Rework Works and How to Farm It","publisher":"allthings.how","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4690--poe-329-new-unique-items-best-uniques-changes--farming","title":"PoE 3.29 New Unique Items, Best Uniques, Changes & Farming","publisher":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-abyss-farming-guide","title":"PoE Abyss Farming Guide (3.29): Scarabs, Atlas Tree & Why the Rework Made It Print","publisher":"timesaver.gg","date":"2026-08-24","patch":"3.29 (through 3.29.3)"},{"url":"https://timelesscalc.com/poe-3-29-abyss-timeless-jewels/","title":"PoE 3.29 Abyss Timeless Jewels Guide","publisher":"timelesscalc.com","date":"2026-08-30","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-guide-abyss-propagation-farming-how-to-farm-scarabs-divine-orbs-and-tier-zero-uniques.html","title":"PoE Guide: Abyss Propagation Farming","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-05","patch":"3.29 (not stated, league-dated)"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-2-abyss-currency-farming-guide-best-strategies-for-25-30-divines-per-hour.html","title":"PoE 3.29.2 Abyss Currency Farming Guide","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-07","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/abyss-buffed-was-it-good-enough-path-of-exile-3-29-2-new-patch-review.html","title":"Abyss Buffed: Was It Good Enough? 3.29.2 review","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-07","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-abyss-farming-guide-best-strategy-for-36-divines-per-hour.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Abyss Farming Guide: 36 Divines per Hour","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://outof.games/realms/pathofexile/economy/fragments/","title":"Fragments prices - Allflame","publisher":"Out of Games (poe.ninja-sourced)","date":"live, fetched 2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://outof.games/realms/pathofexile/economy/allflame-embers/allflame-ember-of-propagation/","title":"Allflame Ember of Propagation price","publisher":"Out of Games","date":"live, fetched 2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Fragment","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview - Fragments (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview - Scarabs (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Currency","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview - Currency (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueJewel","title":"poe.ninja unique jewels (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueArmour","title":"poe.ninja unique armours (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueWeapon","title":"poe.ninja unique weapons (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=BaseType","title":"poe.ninja base types (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueAccessory","title":"poe.ninja unique accessories (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"}]},"delirium":{"title":"Delirium and Simulacrum","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Delirium is a fog that spreads from a Mirror of Delirium or from Delirium Orbs. It makes monsters harder and pays rewards as its bars fill. It is the main source of cluster jewels and the only real source of ilvl 84 clusters in 3.29, and its splinters combine into Simulacrums. Maxroll rates it A tier for 3.29, and community-tracked mirror farms list roughly 25-32 div/hour profit.","howTo":[{"text":"Getting a mirror: maps have at least an 8% base chance to contain one. The base Delirium Scarab (0.6c) guarantees one and is the cheapest way to do it.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[6,13,19,45]},{"text":"Mirrors also appear in the campaign from Act 5 (Torched Courts) onwards.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Reward bars: a 2nd bar opens at level 3 of the first bar, a 3rd at level 5, then 1 more every 2 levels. Rewards pay out when the encounter ends.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Fog stops spreading during Breach, Legion monoliths, Incursion, Betrayal research, active Ritual altars and near active Blight.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Opening Strongboxes, killing Essence monsters and capturing red beasts extend the timer.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Mirror farm target: reach 8 reward tiles, then go into the boss arena. Tiers past that are harder but pay the same.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Build check: you should clear a map in about 3 minutes or less. If you can't, skip mirror farming.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[50,51]},{"text":"Delirium Orbs: each adds 20% deliriousness, up to 5 per map.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6,2,36]},{"text":"Orb fog has no mirror and no timer, pays a reward every time a bar fills, and never drops Delirium Orbs.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6,9]},{"text":"Orb maps: use 4 orbs (80%), because 100% is too hard and slow. Stop adding mechanics at 13 rewards (14 with the passive), then kill the boss.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Deceptive Astrolabe: guarantees a mirror in every map of its Shaped Region. Those maps only count as completed after you earn 5 Delirium rewards.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[54]},{"text":"Simulacrum: combine 300 splinters (they stack to 300). It is used once in a personal map device and opens 6 portals.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7,17,20,30]},{"text":"Other Simulacrum sources: 3 Altered Perception cards give 1 Simulacrum, and 8 Checkmate cards give 76 splinters.","stage":["all"],"cite":[17,18]},{"text":"Simulacrum has 15 waves. Wave 1 is 10% delirious with ilvl 75 rewards. Waves 10-15 are 100% with ilvl 84 rewards.","stage":["late"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Omniphobia can spawn from wave 3 and Kosis from wave 5. Clearing all 15 waves spawns the Altar of Lies, which lets you take or switch to the Delirious Bloodline.","stage":["late"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Between Simulacrum waves, put loot in the in-zone stash.","stage":["late"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Boss rushing: Delirium pairs well only if you can finish it on the way to the boss.","stage":["late"],"cite":[39]}],"dangers":[{"text":"At 100% delirium, monsters deal 30% more damage and take 80-96% less damage, depending on rarity (wiki estimate).","stage":["late"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Past about 8 reward tiles, mirrors get exponentially harder for the same pay, and the late part of a mirror map can get extremely hard.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Scarab of Mania fills meters 100% faster but makes difficulty climb 50% faster with distance from the mirror.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[12,29,19]},{"text":"Unending Nightmare doubles distance scaling and blocks splinter and orb drops. Never take it for a splinter or orb farm.","stage":["late","ssf"],"cite":[14,31,29]},{"text":"Delirium-infused (Delirious) maps stop the mirror from spawning. Avoid Jungle Valley, because its boss has to die before the fog clears.","stage":["all"],"cite":[50,52]},{"text":"Stacking Beyond, Breach or Abyss on mirror maps can cause big frame-rate drops.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[50,52]},{"text":"Neuroses only works on T11+ maps and spawns no bosses in orb-fogged maps.","stage":["mid","late","ssf"],"cite":[11,34]},{"text":"Mirror-only atlas nodes (That Which You Seek, Descent Into Madness, The Singular Eternity) do nothing in orb maps.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Simulacrum: starting the next wave destroys items left on the ground.","stage":["late"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Simulacrum monsters can still have physical damage reduction, which is a problem for physical builds. Overwhelm and Impale chance mods are gone since 3.25.","stage":["late"],"cite":[29]}],"sell":[{"text":"Always combine splinters before selling. A Simulacrum is about 226c, while 300 loose splinters are about 63c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[46]},{"text":"Price Skittering (58.9c), Diviner's (36.1c) and Fine (29.5c) orbs individually.","stage":["all"],"cite":[44,1]},{"text":"Cartographer's is now only about 10c, below Armoursmith's, Blacksmith's and Jeweller's (15-17c). Bulk it with the cheap orbs.","stage":["late"],"cite":[44,1]},{"text":"Bulk-sell the cheap orb types (Whispering, Blighted, Thaumaturge's, Fragmented and the like).","stage":["all"],"cite":[1,44]},{"text":"Minimum cluster keep rule: 4/5-passive Mediums and 8-passive Larges. Hide the rest.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1,2]},{"text":"Item level matters. The 35% effect prefix and the top small-passive line need ilvl 84.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[21,37]},{"text":"ilvl 84 Large 12-passive is where the money is: Minion Damage about 824c, Spell about 412c, Claw/Dagger about 360c. The median is only about 26c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[48]},{"text":"ilvl 84 Large 8-passive has a median of about 30c. Minion Damage is 89c and Attack while holding a Shield is 82c. Plain Attack Damage is 4-10c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[48]},{"text":"ilvl 84 Mediums: 4-passive median about 19c (Herald 80c). 5-passive median about 3.6c, topping out around 40-60c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[48]},{"text":"Simulacrum uniques: unrolled Megalomaniac about 9c, Split Personality about 1c, 7-passive Voices about 1c. A 3-passive Voices is about 109 div.","stage":["late"],"cite":[49]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Mirror Paranoia farm (3.29 standard)","investment":"Low-medium. About 70c of scarabs per map at end-of-league prices, plus about 3.6 Deceptive Astrolabes (about 405c) per hour. Nerotox lists 4.8 div/hour cost.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Roll 8-mod T16 Strand with 110%+ quantity and 40%+ pack size.","Add 3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia, 1x Mania and 1x Neuroses.","Use a Deceptive Astrolabe, because this tree takes no mirror-chance points.","Do not use Delirious maps. Do not stack Beyond, Breach or Abyss.","Reach about 8 reward tiles, then kill the boss.","Expect about 20 maps/hour (from 60 Paranoia and 20 Neuroses per hour).","Combine splinters into Simulacrums and sell them, since they are the main income."],"atlasPassives":["Imagined Pursuits","Screaming Whispers","Delusions of Persecution","Paranoid Fixation","Descent Into Madness","The Singular Eternity","Scarab nodes such as Significant Troves","Divination Scarab nodes","Red Eldritch Altars (a Mercenary variant is the alternative)"],"scarabs":["3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","1x Delirium Scarab of Mania","1x Delirium Scarab of Neuroses"],"cite":[40,45,47,50,51,52]},{"name":"Maxroll Delirium Mirror (3.28 guide)","investment":"Low (Maxroll rating). Difficulty Average, Profitability Average.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run 8-mod T16 Strand, with Beach as the backup map. Eater of Worlds influence is optional.","Add 4x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia and 1x Neuroses.","Reach 8 reward tiles before the boss arena. Do not push higher.","The tree takes Ritual chance only for the extra monsters that spawn around the pylon. Do not complete the Ritual.","Imagined Pursuits is core.","The tree skips Delusions of Persecution, which loses value as unique cluster supply grows."],"atlasPassives":["Imagined Pursuits","Ritual chance nodes (for monsters only)"],"scarabs":["4x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","1x Delirium Scarab of Neuroses"],"cite":[1,0,15]},{"name":"Fast City Square loop (Joeyboy)","investment":"Medium. 10 div/hour listed cost.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run 8-mod City Square with 100%+ quantity and Templar Astrolabes.","Aim for about 40 maps/hour (240 maps in 6 hours).","Scarabs: 1x Neuroses plus 4x Paranoia, 3x Paranoia + 1x Mania, or 3x Paranoia + 1x Infamy. Profit per hour was nearly the same with all three.","City Square is easy and fast for weaker builds, but gives fewer splinters and depends more on orb RNG."],"scarabs":["1x Delirium Scarab of Neuroses","4x Paranoia, or 3x Paranoia + 1x Mania, or 3x Paranoia + 1x Infamy"],"cite":[41,50,51]},{"name":"80% Delirium Orb farm (Ghazzy)","investment":"Low to medium. It does not work without the scarabs and orbs.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run Dunes.","Add 4x Fine Delirium Orbs (for currency) or 4x Diviner's (for Stacked Decks).","Add 2x Delirium Scarab of Mania and 3x Paranoia.","Use Kingsmarch Verisium ore nodes for extra monster density.","Ghazzy does not recommend Skittering orbs for most players."],"atlasPassives":["Imagined Pursuits (essential)","Screaming Whispers (for splinters)","Skip That Which You Seek, Descent Into Madness and The Singular Eternity, which do nothing for orb maps"],"scarabs":["2x Delirium Scarab of Mania","3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia"],"cite":[3,2]},{"name":"Orb layering rules (Maxroll 2024 guide)","investment":"Depends on orb type. Skittering is the most expensive.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use 4 orbs (80%).","Strand has the highest hidden reward-threshold multiplier. Caldera and Crimson Temple are alternatives.","The guide ranked Skittering as the best orb (about 2.5 scarabs per orb per threshold), with Cartographer's next for consistency.","Stop at 13 rewards (14 with the passive) before the boss.","Compulsive Hoarder and Pathological are usually skipped."],"atlasPassives":["Imagined Pursuits","Screaming Whispers"],"cite":[2]},{"name":"Awakened Deli (TheRealTobl)","investment":"6 div/hour listed cost.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Run mirrors in T16 Tropical Island, Strand or Beach. City Square is optional.","Each map gets 3x Paranoia, 1x Horned Scarab of Awakening and 1x Mania.","Note: since 3.28 the Horned Scarab only adds bosses from a random Maven Invitation to T16+ maps.","The top drop was Maven's Chisel of Avarice (13 div)."],"scarabs":["3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","1x Horned Scarab of Awakening","1x Delirium Scarab of Mania"],"cite":[42,43,35,26]},{"name":"SSF unique clusters","investment":"Low.","stage":["ssf"],"steps":["Put Delirium Scarab of Neuroses on T11+ mirror maps. It forces both unique Delirium bosses to spawn.","It does not spawn bosses in orb-fogged maps.","Voices and Megalomaniac drop from Delirium bosses.","Optional: the Unending Nightmare keystone. Rewards almost always include a cluster jewel, but you get no splinters or orbs."],"atlasPassives":["Unending Nightmare (optional)","Delusions of Persecution"],"scarabs":["1x Delirium Scarab of Neuroses"],"cite":[11,34,2,14]},{"name":"Running Simulacrums","investment":"300 splinters, or about 226c to buy one.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Bring a build that handles 100% delirium. Physical builds should watch for physical damage reduction on monsters.","Kill the Delirium bosses for Voices, Split Personality and Megalomaniac. Expect slightly over 2 uniques per run (max 3).","Stash loot before starting each wave.","Clear all 15 waves for the Altar of Lies (Delirious Bloodline).","At 3.29 prices most of these uniques are cheap. Only low-passive Voices is valuable."],"cite":[7,29,46,49]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough: 25 div/hour profit (34 revenue, 4.8 cost), tracked over 5 hours on 3P+Mania+Neuroses T16 Strand mirrors.","who":"Nerotox (Wealthy Exile)","date":"2026-10-21","cite":[40,43]},{"text":"Rough per hour: about 14 Simulacrums (7.5 div), 215 Stacked Decks (4.1 div), 2.8 Divine Orbs, 20 Fine orbs (1.4 div). Simulacrums are the main income.","who":"Nerotox (Wealthy Exile)","date":"2026-10-21","cite":[40]},{"text":"Rough: 32 div/hour profit (44 revenue, 10 cost) over 240 maps in 6 hours on 8-mod City Square.","who":"Joeyboy (Wealthy Exile)","date":"2026-09-01","cite":[41,43]},{"text":"Rough: 42 div/hour revenue against 6 div/hour cost. Top drop was Maven's Chisel of Avarice (13 div).","who":"TheRealTobl (Wealthy Exile)","date":"2026-08-06","cite":[42,43]},{"text":"Delirium is A tier: a small step behind S, but one of the best farms at every stage. No div/hour figure is given.","who":"Maxroll tier list","date":"2026-09-19","cite":[0]},{"text":"Mirror strategy rated Low investment, Average difficulty, Average profitability. No numeric profit.","who":"Maxroll","date":"2026-03-30","cite":[1]},{"text":"Skittering orbs may average more profit but cost more and need bulk-selling know-how.","who":"GhazzyTV (PoE Vault)","date":"2026-08-17","cite":[3]},{"text":"The '25-30 div/hour' headline does not hold up, because its own cost and profit figures don't add up. Do not use it as a benchmark.","who":"MMOEXP","date":"2026-08-05","cite":[53]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Single-attribute mods on small clusters can now be swapped with Genteel's Ducat.","cite":[25]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Genteel's Ducat now rerolls attribute affixes on Large and Medium clusters. The Horrific Halls objective needs 5 Scarabs and 5 Delirium Orbs.","cite":[24]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Abyssal, Primal and Timeless Delirium Orbs can no longer be obtained. Primal had already stopped dropping in 3.16. Existing Primal and Timeless orbs still work in Standard.","cite":[4,5,8,9,23]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Delirium was not buffed directly, but it gains from two low-value orbs leaving the reward pool.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Clusters from Betrayal Trapped Stashes and Crafting Sprees are capped at ilvl 83, which leaves Delirium as the source of ilvl 84 clusters.","cite":[5,4]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Openness gained 15% Mana Cost Efficiency. Daring Ideas gained 25% Cost Efficiency of Attacks.","cite":[4]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Harbinger was removed, so Obscured and Foreboding orbs are gone. Existing Obscured orbs drop Breach Rings, and Foreboding orbs were turned into Fine. Fossilised orbs are also gone.","cite":[26]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Map Device crafting was removed, so the Kirac Delirium craft is gone. Older guides that use it are out of date.","cite":[26,28]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Horned Scarab of Awakening was reworked, and its Delirium pack-size option is gone.","cite":[28,35,26]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Neuroses buff: +1 to each reward type's count for every unique Delirium boss killed.","cite":[26,34]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Kingsmarch mappers stopped returning clusters above ilvl 83, and Tujen stopped selling clusters.","cite":[26]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Primordial Bond golem buff halved (40% to 20%). Follow-Through capped at 100%. New notables: Fiery Aegis and Holy Word.","cite":[26]},{"patch":"3.27.0","text":"Delirium voices and whispers moved to the Ambient Sound Volume slider.","cite":[27]},{"patch":"3.26.0","text":"More gold at the end of each Simulacrum wave, and a lower gold penalty on Delirium monsters.","cite":[28]},{"patch":"3.25.0","text":"The first 15 Simulacrum waves were removed, so it now has 15 waves, and uniques such as Voices are easier to get. Overwhelm and Impale chance mods were removed.","cite":[29,7]},{"patch":"3.25.0","text":"Paranoia limit raised from 2 to 5. Mania and Unending Nightmare now speed up difficulty scaling with distance.","cite":[10,29,31]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"The PoEDB orb page still lists Abyssal, Timeless, Fossilised and Obscured, and Maxroll's 3.28 guide sells Abyssal. None of these drop in 3.29.","cite":[36,1,4]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"PoEDB Simulacrum wave numbers (20/30 waves, Omniphobia at wave 10, Kosis at 15) are pre-3.25. Trust the 15-wave layout instead.","cite":[20,29]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"The 2024 Maxroll orb guide says the Paranoia limit is 2. It is 5.","cite":[33,2]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"3.29 setups use 3 Paranoia + Mania + Neuroses, not Maxroll's 3.28 set of 4 Paranoia + Neuroses. IGGM says a full Paranoia set lowers efficiency.","cite":[40,50,51,1]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"Maxroll's mirror page has no 3.29 revision (last updated 2026-03-30), and its tree is only an image.","cite":[1]},{"patch":"guide conflict","text":"PoE Vault's 3.10 Delirium guide still uses Zana mods, Watchstones and Awakening Level, none of which exist now.","cite":[38,26]}],"tables":[{"title":"Delirium Orb prices (Allflame, 2026-11-04, 1 div = 412c)","columns":["Orb","Price"],"rows":[["Skittering","58.9c"],["Diviner's","36.1c"],["Fine","29.5c"],["Armoursmith's","16.6c"],["Blacksmith's","15.3c"],["Jeweller's","14.8c"],["Singular","14.0c"],["Cartographer's","10c"],["Fragmented","8.9c"],["Thaumaturge's","7.1c"],["Blighted","6.9c"],["Whispering","4.9c"]],"cite":[44]},{"title":"Delirium scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Limit","Effect","Price (2026-11-04)"],"rows":[["Delirium Scarab","1","Guarantees a mirror","0.6c"],["Paranoia","5","+2 reward types","20.5c"],["Neuroses","1","T11+: all unique bosses, +1 count per kill; none in orb maps","7.5c"],["Mania","2","Meters 100% faster; difficulty scales 50% faster with distance","1.2c"],["Delusions","1","Delirium layers on maps found in the area; very limited use","1.05c"]],"cite":[13,10,33,11,34,12,55,45,2]},{"title":"Community 3.29 mirror runs (rough)","columns":["Who","Map","Scarabs","Maps/hr","Revenue","Cost"],"rows":[["Nerotox","8-mod T16 Strand + Deceptive Astrolabe","3 Paranoia, Mania, Neuroses","~20","34 div/h","4.8 div/h"],["Joeyboy","8-mod City Square + Templar Astrolabe","Neuroses + 4 Paranoia (or variants)","~40","44 div/h","10 div/h"],["TheRealTobl","T16 Tropical Island / Strand / Beach","3 Paranoia, Horned Awakening, Mania","n/a","42 div/h","6 div/h"]],"cite":[40,41,42]},{"title":"Joeyboy scarab set comparison (all with 1x Neuroses)","columns":["Set","Delirium Orbs/hr","Simulacrums/hr"],"rows":[["4x Paranoia","242","6"],["3x Paranoia + 1x Mania","180","6.6"],["3x Paranoia + 1x Infamy","165","5"]],"cite":[41]},{"title":"Delirium atlas notables","columns":["Node","Effect"],"rows":[["Imagined Pursuits","+1 to every reward type count on map completion (core)"],["Delusions of Persecution","Unique bosses 100% more likely; +50% splinters and unique cluster chance from them"],["Screaming Whispers","18% larger splinter stacks"],["That Which You Seek","+24% mirror chance; scarabs 24% more likely Delirium (mirror only)"],["Compulsive Hoarder","8% chance for 3 extra reward types"],["Paranoid Fixation","Delirious uniques: 2% extra cluster, 1% extra orb"],["Unending Nightmare (keystone)","Fog never clears, 2x distance scaling, no splinters/orbs"]],"cite":[19,6,15,16,14,31]},{"title":"Simulacrum and cluster prices (Allflame, 2026-11-04)","columns":["Item","Price"],"rows":[["Simulacrum","~226c (~0.55 div)"],["300 Simulacrum Splinters","~63c"],["ilvl 84 Large 12-passive Minion Damage","~824c"],["ilvl 84 Large 12-passive Spell Damage","~412c"],["ilvl 84 Large 8-passive (median)","~30c"],["ilvl 84 Medium 4-passive (median)","~19c"],["3-passive Voices","~109 div"],["Unrolled Megalomaniac","~9c"]],"cite":[46,48,49]}],"quickCard":["Mirror: 8-mod T16 Strand, 3 Paranoia + Mania + Neuroses","Stop at ~8 reward tiles, then kill the boss","Orb maps: 4 orbs, stop at ~13 rewards","Combine splinters: Sim ~226c vs ~63c loose","Keep ilvl 84 Large 8/12 + Medium 4/5 clusters","No Delirious maps, no Jungle Valley, no Beyond/Breach/Abyss"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-09-19","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/delirium-mirror","title":"Delirium Mirror Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll (Milkybk_, reviewed by Facefoot and IBoilerUp)","date":"2026-03-30","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/delirium-orb-farming-guide","title":"Delirium Orb Farming Guide","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2024-07-25","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/atlas-passive-skill-tree-strategies","title":"Atlas Passive Skill Tree Strategies Guide","publisher":"PoE Vault (GhazzyTV)","date":"2026-08-17","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 - Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delirium","title":"Delirium","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Simulacrum","title":"Simulacrum","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25+"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Abyssal_Delirium_Orb","title":"Abyssal Delirium Orb","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Timeless_Delirium_Orb","title":"Timeless Delirium Orb","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delirium_Scarab_of_Paranoia","title":"Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delirium_Scarab_of_Neuroses","title":"Delirium Scarab of Neuroses","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.24+"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delirium_Scarab_of_Mania","title":"Delirium Scarab of Mania","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25+"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delirium_Scarab","title":"Delirium Scarab","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.24+"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Unending_Nightmare","title":"Unending Nightmare (Atlas keystone)","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25+"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Imagined_Pursuits","title":"Imagined Pursuits","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Delusions_of_Persecution","title":"Delusions of Persecution","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Simulacrum_Splinter","title":"Simulacrum Splinter","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Altered_Perception","title":"Altered Perception","publisher":"poewiki.net","date":"unknown","patch":"3.18+"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium","title":"Delirium","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 client data"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Simulacrum","title":"Simulacrum","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/resources/cluster-jewels-explained","title":"Cluster Jewels Explained","publisher":"Maxroll (Tenkiei)","date":"2023-12-05","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://expcarry.com/poe-3-29-challenges-guide-all-40-rewards","title":"PoE 3.29 Challenges Guide: All 40 Curse of the Allflame Challenges and Rewards","publisher":"ExpCarry","date":"2026-11-01","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0 patch notes","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0 patch notes (Mirage)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0 patch notes (Keepers of the Flame)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.27"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0 patch notes (Secrets of the Atlas)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.25.0","title":"Version 3.25.0 patch notes (Settlers of Kalguur)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Simulacrum_Splinter","title":"Simulacrum Splinter","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Unending_Nightmare","title":"Unending Nightmare (keystone and unique idol)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.25"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Perceived_Greatness","title":"Perceived Greatness (Minor Idol)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"Phrecia event"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium_Scarab_of_Paranoia","title":"Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium_Scarab_of_Neuroses","title":"Delirium Scarab of Neuroses","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Horned_Scarab_of_Awakening","title":"Horned Scarab of Awakening","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium_Orb","title":"Delirium Orb","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Cluster_Jewel","title":"Cluster Jewel","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/delirium-league-guide","title":"Guide for Delirium in Path of Exile","publisher":"PoE Vault","date":"2023-02-05","patch":"3.10"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/nightmare-boss-rush","title":"Nightmare Boss Rush","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://wealthyexile.com/strategies/8198/delirium_mirror_paranoia_farm","title":"Delirium Mirror Paranoia Farm (by Nerotox)","publisher":"Wealthy Exile","date":"2026-10-21","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://wealthyexile.com/strategies/8026/delirium_orbsred_altarscachesmercatrolabes","title":"Delirium Orbs/Red Altars/Caches/Merc/Atrolabes (by Joeyboy#0005)","publisher":"Wealthy Exile","date":"2026-09-01","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://wealthyexile.com/strategies/7499/awakened_deli","title":"Awakened Deli (by TheRealTobl#4323)","publisher":"Wealthy Exile","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://wealthyexile.com/strategies/public","title":"Strategies (public list)","publisher":"Wealthy Exile","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=DeliriumOrb","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Delirium Orbs (Allflame exchange)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Scarabs (Allflame exchange)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Fragment","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Fragments incl. Simulacrum (Allflame exchange)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Astrolabe","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Astrolabes (Allflame exchange)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=ClusterJewel","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Cluster Jewel bases (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueJewel","title":"poe.ninja economy API - Unique Jewels (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.iggm.com/news/poe-3-29-delirium-mirror-farming-strategy-how-to-maximize-simulacrum-splinters-delirium-orbs","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Delirium Mirror Farming Strategy","publisher":"IGGM (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-25","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.ssegold.com/poe-3-29-delirium-mirror-farming","title":"PoE 3.29 Delirium Mirror Farming","publisher":"SSEGold (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-delirium-mirror-farming-guide-best-scarabs-maps-atlas-tree-simulacrum-splinters.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Delirium Mirror Farming Guide: Best Scarabs, Maps, Atlas Tree","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-25","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-29-currency-farming-guide-25-30-div-hour-fast-delirium-map-strategy.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Currency Farming Guide: 25-30 Div/Hour Fast Delirium Map Strategy","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-05","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Deceptive_Astrolabe","title":"Deceptive Astrolabe","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium_Scarab_of_Delusions","title":"Delirium Scarab of Delusions","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"}]},"bestiary":{"title":"Bestiary (Einhar, the Menagerie)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Einhar shows up in your maps. You capture yellow and red beasts and either sell them or spend them at the Blood Altar in the Menagerie on beastcrafts and Bestiary Boss portals. In 3.29, Talismans are back as a Bestiary-only reward on new beast-named bases, and Maxroll's 3.29 farming tier list puts Beasts in A Tier.","howTo":[{"text":"Get Einhar into your maps. A Bestiary Scarab guarantees him (limit 1). The Bestiary Chance (+8%) and Eternal Hunt (+20%) passives raise the odds.","stage":["all"],"cite":[23,42,36,38]},{"text":"Capture every yellow beast. Only capture red beasts that are valuable or that you need for a recipe.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,4]},{"text":"In the Menagerie, open the Bestiary (H) and Ctrl+click valuable beasts to turn them into items. You no longer need Bestiary Orbs (since 3.27), and the gold fee is low (since 3.28).","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,4,33,32]},{"text":"Release unwanted red beasts from the Menagerie. Sell yellow beasts in bulk, because crafters buy whole inventories.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,4]},{"text":"Every beastcraft takes four beasts. Most recipes need one named beast and any three others. Black Mórrigan recipes need two named beasts and any two others.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7,41]},{"text":"Since 3.29, Einhar can identify items in the Menagerie, and 3.29.2 added a crafting bench there. You can ID, bench-craft and beastcraft in one place.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,1]},{"text":"Look at every Talisman's influence before you vendor it. Influenced bases can be worth thousands of chaos.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[52]},{"text":"Open a boss portal with its beast plus any three others. The boss area's level equals that beast's level, so use beasts from area level 80+ if you want the boss body armour.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,6,10,47]},{"text":"EZG's simple loop: run a white T16 Dunes (T14+ is fine), take about one minute per map, and empty the Menagerie every 25-30 maps.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[39]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Deadly Prey (since 3.28): capturable beasts always have Bestial Rage, with more speed and damage. This is risky for squishy builds.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[28,32]},{"text":"If you die in a Blood Altar fight, the recipe fails and you lose the beasts. Only use expensive beasts on a build that can win the fight.","stage":["all"],"cite":[38]},{"text":"Black Mórrigan hits hard in melee. At monster level 68 it has about 51k life, 50k armour and 50% elemental resistance, and uses Leap Slam, Sunder and Ground Slam.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Since 3.29, Bestiary Bosses have more life, and their area level equals the sacrificed beast's level.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,31]},{"text":"Farrul: bleeding Fangs, Lacerate that maims, a Teleport Slam (12s cooldown) and Stampede. Bring bleed and maim removal and movement.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[48]},{"text":"Fenumus: poisoning chaos mortars, bleeding Tail Spikes, a chaos ground DoT, six minions and Hallucinate. You need chaos resistance and poison/bleed handling.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[50]},{"text":"Craiceann: Burrow, Charge Wall, a Tectonic Slam that converts 25% of physical damage to cold, summons and Firestorm.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[51]},{"text":"Saqawal: Leap Slam, Bird Swarm, Tail Spike, Screech and Charge.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[49]},{"text":"The Shadowed Crow scarab can no longer drop, so ignore guides that are built around it.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26,30]},{"text":"Old guides are wrong about recipes. The Split recipes are gone, Chimeral is now Croaker, Chromatics became a 4-link helmet, and Horizons became Unmaking.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,6,32]},{"text":"Hinekora's Lock cannot target Corrupted items (since 3.28). Fracture two fails on Influenced or Fractured items.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[2,8,9]},{"text":"Talismans cannot be anointed, and the crafting bench cannot remove their Enchantment mods.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]}],"sell":[{"text":"The Black Mórrigan is worth about 1237c (about 3 div), more than three times the best Unique Talisman. Sell it unless you need a guaranteed craft.","stage":["late"],"cite":[29,53]},{"text":"Craicic Croaker is worth about 824c (about 2 div). Farric Tiger Alpha is worth about 180c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"Mid-tier reds: Plagued Arachnid about 180c, Bristle Matron 108c, Vivid Vulture 55c, Hellion Alpha 50c, Brambleback 30c, Cystcaller 20c, Vivid Watcher 17c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"Captured First Ones: Farrul about 310c, Fenumus 111c, Craiceann 20c, Saqawal 6.2c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[29,38]},{"text":"Most common reds sell for under 1c, for example Shield Crab, Gargantuan, Widow, Retch, Frost Hellion Alpha, Rhoa and Magma Hound. Release them or bulk them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"Sell yellow beasts in bulk as full inventories.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,4]},{"text":"Talisman bases worth picking up (ilvl 85): Great Maw about 824c, Rhex 412c, Saqawine 331c, Croaker 150c. Carrion Queen, Cobra and Plagued Arachnid are about 25c. Most others are under 6c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[52]},{"text":"Influenced bases are worth far more, for example Rhex Shaper/Warlord about 4204c, Great Maw about 4452c, Taurus Warlord about 5359c and Cobra Redeemer about 989c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[52]},{"text":"Unique Talismans: Eyes of the Greatwolf about 412c and Natural Hierarchy about 378c. The rest are under 10c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[53]},{"text":"Non-armour boss uniques are mostly low value, at 4-80c.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[54]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Red Maps Bestiary (Maxroll, Zen_M)","investment":"Low by Maxroll's rating. Scarabs alone cost roughly 50c per map with Herd x2 and Duplicating (poe.ninja, 2 Nov 2026).","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run any T16, preferably Strand, Beach or Dunes.","Alch every map. Reroll unrunnable ones with Scouring plus Alchemy.","Capture every yellow beast and only valuable red ones.","Find a Starfall Crater (its Black Knight can drop Svalinn).","Do only the Bismuth and Crimson Iron encounters and click every Sulphite Vein.","Kill the map boss. Searing Exarch influence is optional.","Watch for Black Mórrigan, Craicic Croaker, Fenumal Plagued Arachnid, Farric Tiger Alpha, the Vivid and Wild beasts, Primal Cystcaller and Primal Rhex Matriarch. Talismans also drop."],"atlasPassives":["Maxroll shows its exact tree only as an image","Eternal Hunt (+20% Einhar, more Bestiary Scarab drops)","Bestiary Chance (+8% Einhar)","Mighty Hunter (Einhar stays after his mission)","Two-Hearted Hunt (reds may survive the Blood Altar, up to 20%)","Big Game / Red Beast Chance / Red Beast Pair Chance (more reds)","Natural Selection (more uncommon beast varieties)"],"scarabs":["Bestiary Scarab (adds Einhar, which Herd needs)","Bestiary Scarab of the Herd x2","Bestiary Scarab of Duplicating","Kalguuran Scarab (Settlers variant)"],"cite":[3,24,25,30,42,36,35,27]},{"name":"White Maps Bestiary (Maxroll)","investment":"Low. Maxroll rates it Easy, with Average profit and Average management.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Run Dunes, Strand, Belfry or Cemetery.","Use Shadow Shaping favourites to block unwanted T1-4 maps.","Bring a stack of Vaal Orbs and activate the Delirium Mirror.","Capture all yellow beasts, plus Farric Wolf Alpha, Farric Lynx Alpha, Saqawine Vulture, Fenumal Plagued Arachnid and Craicic Croaker.","Vaal the Screaming Essences of Envy, Dread, Scorn and Misery.","Kill the boss, then collect the Delirium rewards."],"atlasPassives":["Maxroll shows its exact tree only as an image"],"cite":[4,42]},{"name":"Fast white T16 Dunes (EZG)","investment":"About 45-50c per map, mostly scarabs plus the map (EZG).","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run a white T16 Dunes. T14 or higher also works.","Aim for about one minute per map.","Empty the Menagerie roughly every 25-30 maps."],"cite":[39]},{"name":"Budget scarabs (poe-vault)","investment":"Low","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run Bestiary Scarab of the Herd only while it is cheap.","Skip Duplicating, which is usually expensive."],"scarabs":["Bestiary Scarab","Bestiary Scarab of the Herd (when cheap)"],"cite":[5]},{"name":"Bestiary Boss body armours","investment":"One portal beast per run, for example Farric Tiger Alpha at about 180c.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Keep portal beasts captured in area level 80+ maps. The boss area takes the beast's level.","Open the portal at the Blood Altar with that beast plus any three others.","Only at area level 80+ can the boss drop its body armour: Farrul's Fur, Saqawal's Nest, Fenumus' Shroud or Craiceann's Carapace.","Bosses also drop Unique Talismans and Talismans."],"cite":[0,10,29,54,48]}],"profit":[{"text":"Red Maps Bestiary is rated Low investment and High profitability, but no chaos/hour figure is given and beast prices change daily (rough).","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-08-04","cite":[3]},{"text":"White Maps Bestiary is rated Average profitability and Low investment (rough).","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-08-04","cite":[4]},{"text":"Costs about 45-50c per map, mostly scarabs plus the map. No income figure is given (rough).","who":"EZG","date":"2026-09-18","cite":[39]},{"text":"Beasts are A Tier on the endgame farming list, mainly because of the reworked Talismans (rough).","who":"Maxroll tier list","date":"2026-09-19","cite":[37]},{"text":"Area 80+ boss body armours: 6-link Farrul's Fur about 1237c (90c unlinked), Saqawal's Nest about 742c (28c), Craiceann's Carapace about 412c (70c) (rough).","who":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[54,48]},{"text":"Herd x2 plus Duplicating costs roughly 50c in scarabs per map (rough).","who":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","cite":[30]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"A crafting bench was added to the Menagerie.","cite":[1]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Talismans are now a Bestiary reward. They drop from Red Beasts and Bestiary Bosses, and each base is tied to one beast.","cite":[0,31]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Talismans now carry Enchantment mods instead of implicits and are no longer corrupted by default. They cannot be anointed.","cite":[0,31]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Unique Talismans come only from Bestiary Bosses or the Black Mórrigan craft. Non-unique ones come only from Bestiary, Talisman div cards or Jorgin's safehouse.","cite":[0,7,31]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Boss area level equals the sacrificed beast's level, and bosses have more life. Boss body armours drop only at area level 80+.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The two Split recipes became Fracture one mod (Frost Hellion Alpha, 4+ mods) and Fracture two mods (Plagued Arachnid + Mórrigan, 6+ mods). Both work on Rare Talismans only.","cite":[0,6,9,46]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The Rare Talisman craft now rerolls a Talisman's base type (Craicic Squid). Amulet-to-Talisman became Imprint of a Rare Talisman (Plagued Arachnid).","cite":[0,6]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Craicic Chimeral was renamed Craicic Croaker. It still makes the Magic-item Imprint.","cite":[0,8]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The Vivid Vulture Synthesis-implicit reroll now works on Unique items only.","cite":[0,13]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The 8 Chromatic Orbs craft (Saqawine Rhoa) now makes a Rare Four-Linked Helmet.","cite":[0,6]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Einhar can identify items in the Menagerie.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Call to the First Ones now gives a Rare Talisman, and Jorgin's Talisman reward gives regular currency. Old Talisman bases can no longer be obtained.","cite":[40]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"In Ruthless, Talismans do not drop from Red Beasts. They are beastcrafted in the Menagerie.","cite":[0,40]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Horizons became 3 Unmaking, five Kirac missions became a Nightmare Map, and free map crafts became a valuable Scarab.","cite":[2,32,6]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The Awakened level-up became +500m XP to an Exceptional Support (Wild Brambleback). Vivid Watcher turns an Exceptional into 3 high-level supports.","cite":[2,12,15]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The map corrupt craft now adds an implicit instead of 30% quality, and Hinekora's Lock no longer works on Corrupted items.","cite":[2,32]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The itemise gold fee was cut sharply and is now flat. Harvest beasts became much more common.","cite":[2,32]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Two-Hearted Hunt: the save mod is now always applied, but the cap fell from 40% to 20%. Deadly Prey gives beasts Bestial Rage.","cite":[2,27,28,32]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Bestiary Orbs were removed. You itemise beasts straight from the Bestiary UI.","cite":[33]},{"patch":"3.26/3.27","text":"The gold penalty on Bestiary monsters was lowered.","cite":[34,33]}],"tables":[{"title":"Bestiary Boss portals","columns":["Boss / area","Portal beast","Base level","Body armour (80+ only)","Other drops"],"rows":[["Farrul, Farrul's Den","Farric Tiger Alpha (~180c)","80","Farrul's Fur (6L ~1237c)","Bite, Chase, Pounce"],["Saqawal, Saqawal's Roost","Saqawine Rhex","70","Saqawal's Nest (6L ~742c)","Flock (~80c), Talons, Winds"],["Fenumus, Fenumus' Lair","Fenumal Hybrid Arachnid","77","Fenumus' Shroud","Toxins (~57c), Spinnerets (~43c), Weave"],["Craiceann, Craiceann's Cove","Craicic Spider Crab","74","Craiceann's Carapace (6L ~412c)","Pincers (~61c), Chitin, Tracks"]],"cite":[6,10,22,47,48,49,50,51,29,54]},{"title":"Key beastcrafts","columns":["Recipe","Named beast(s)","Notes"],"rows":[["Imprint of a Magic item","Craicic Croaker","Renamed from Chimeral"],["Hinekora's Lock on Magic item","Croaker + Black Mórrigan","Not on Corrupted items"],["Unique Talisman","Black Mórrigan","+3 any beasts"],["Fracture 1 mod","Farric Frost Hellion Alpha","Rare Talisman, 4+ mods"],["Fracture 2 mods","Plagued Arachnid + Mórrigan","Rare Talisman, 6+ mods, not Influenced/Fractured"],["Reroll Talisman base","Craicic Squid (~4c)","Keeps mods"],["Imprint of Rare Talisman","Fenumal Plagued Arachnid",""],["Max links / max sockets","Mórrigan + Sand Spitter / + Shield Crab",""],["Level 30 Aspect","First One + Mórrigan","First One alone = normal Aspect"],["Prefix in, suffix out","Farric Wolf Alpha","Rares only"],["Suffix in, prefix out","Farric Lynx Alpha","Rares only"],["Crafted meta-mod","Wild Bristle Matron","Non-unique items"],["Reroll Watcher's Eye mod","Wild Hellion Alpha","Not life/mana/ES mods"],["Reroll Synthesis implicit","Vivid Vulture","Uniques only"],["+500m XP Exceptional Support","Wild Brambleback",""],["Exceptional -> 3 supports","Vivid Watcher",""],["Mod on influenced item","Craicic Maw + influence beast","Shaper: Devourer, Elder: Blood Viper, Redeemer: Queen, Hunter: Watcher, Crusader: Goliath, Warlord: Scrabbler"],["Nightmare Map / valuable Scarab","Primal Cystcaller / Primal Crushclaw",""],["Synthesis Unique Map","Primal Rhex Matriarch",""],["Guardian or Conqueror Map","Vivid Abberarach",""],["Unique Map / corrupt map (implicit)","Farric Taurus / Craicic Vassal",""],["Corrupt map twice","Craicic Vassal + Fenumal Scorpion",""],["Add mod to Rare Map","Craicic Savage Crab + Saqawine Cobra",""],["3 Orbs of Unmaking","Frost Hellion Alpha + Farric Gargantuan",""],["Rare Four-Linked Helmet","Saqawine Rhoa","Was 8 Chromatics"]],"cite":[6,7,8,9,41,46,13,19,20,11,14,12,15,21,16,17,18]},{"title":"Talisman bases (poe.ninja ilvl 85, 4 Nov 2026)","columns":["Base","Beast","Enchant","Price"],"rows":[["Great Maw","not listed","15% increased Attributes","~824c"],["Rhex","Saqawine Rhex","100% of Cold and Lightning hit damage taken as Fire","~412c"],["Saqawine","Saqawal","100% increased Aspect effect","~331c"],["Croaker","Craicic Croaker","+1 to all Skill Gems","~150c"],["Carrion Queen","Fenumal Queen","+1 max Spectre","~25c"],["Cobra","not listed","+1 max Frenzy Charge","~25c"],["Plagued Arachnid","Fenumal Plagued Arachnid","not listed","~24c"],["Craicic","Craiceann","100% increased Aspect effect","20c"],["Spider Crab","not listed","+15% Quality to all Skill Gems","~14c"],["Taurus","not listed","+1 max Endurance Charge","10c"],["Wolf Alpha","not listed","+40% Crit Multiplier","~6.5c"],["Fenumal","Fenumus","100% increased Aspect effect","~6.5c"],["Tiger","Farric Tiger Alpha","not listed","~5.8c"],["Farric","Farrul","100% increased Aspect effect","3c"],["Retch / Scrabbler","not listed","+1 max Power Charge / +2 Herald gems","not listed"],["Black Widow / Hybrid Arachnid","Fenumal Widow / Hybrid Arachnid","not listed","not listed"]],"cite":[3,43,44,45,52]},{"title":"Bestiary scarabs (poe.ninja, 2 Nov 2026)","columns":["Scarab","Effect","Limit","Price"],"rows":[["Bestiary Scarab","Map contains Einhar","1","~1.4c"],["Scarab of the Herd","+5 Red Beasts if Einhar is present","2","~16.5c"],["Scarab of Duplicating","Copies captured beasts","1","~16c"],["Scarab of the Shadowed Crow","Black Mórrigan if Einhar is present","-","Drop-disabled, no price"],["Kalguuran Scarab","Used in Maxroll's Settlers variant","-","~2.2c"]],"cite":[23,24,25,26,30,3]},{"title":"Bestiary atlas passives","columns":["Node","Effect"],"rows":[["Bestiary Chance","+8% Einhar, +8% Bestiary Scarab drops"],["Eternal Hunt","+20% Einhar, +20% Bestiary Scarab drops"],["Mighty Hunter","Einhar stays after his mission, 100% faster cooldown, 1000% more damage to uniques"],["Two-Hearted Hunt","Reds always get a mod that may save them at the Blood Altar (up to 20%), plus an extra Bestiary mod"],["Deadly Prey","Beasts have Bestial Rage, and kills grant Hunters' Cunning (less damage taken, more damage, IIQ/IIR from beasts)"],["Big Game","15% chance for a yellow to be replaced by a red"],["Red Beast Chance / Pair Chance","5% extra red / 4% reds come in pairs"],["Yellow Beast Amount","+1 yellow beast"],["Natural Selection","Less common beast varieties are more likely"],["Saqawal / Fenumus / Farrul / Craiceann Hunt","100% more reds from Sands / Caverns / Wilds / Deep"]],"cite":[42,36,35,27,28,38]}],"quickCard":["Bestiary Scarab + Herd x2 (+Duplicating if cheap)","Capture all yellows, but reds only if valuable","Mórrigan ~1237c, Croaker ~824c: sell, don't waste","Check Talisman influence before vendoring","Boss portals: use beasts from 80+ maps","Release sub-1c reds and bulk-sell yellows"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 — Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"unknown (July 2026)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Content Update 3.28.0 — Path of Exile: Mirage","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/red-maps-bestiary","title":"Red Maps Bestiary","publisher":"Maxroll (Zen_M, reviewed by IBoilerUp)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/white-map-bestiary-farming","title":"White Maps Bestiary","publisher":"Maxroll (Zen_M, reviewed by Facefoot, IBoilerUp)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/atlas-passive-skill-tree-strategies","title":"Atlas Passive Skill Tree Strategies Guide (BBIR section)","publisher":"poe-vault.com","date":"2026-08-17","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Einhar","title":"Einhar (Bestiary recipe list)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Black_M%C3%B3rrigan","title":"Black Mórrigan","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Craicic_Croaker","title":"Craicic Croaker","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Fenumal_Plagued_Arachnid","title":"Fenumal Plagued Arachnid","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Farric_Tiger_Alpha","title":"Farric Tiger Alpha","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wild_Bristle_Matron","title":"Wild Bristle Matron","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wild_Brambleback","title":"Wild Brambleback","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vivid_Vulture","title":"Vivid Vulture","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wild_Hellion_Alpha","title":"Wild Hellion Alpha","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vivid_Watcher","title":"Vivid Watcher","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Primal_Cystcaller","title":"Primal Cystcaller","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Primal_Rhex_Matriarch","title":"Primal Rhex Matriarch","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vivid_Abberarach","title":"Vivid Abberarach","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Farric_Wolf_Alpha","title":"Farric Wolf Alpha","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Farric_Lynx_Alpha","title":"Farric Lynx Alpha","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Craicic_Maw","title":"Craicic Maw","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Fenumal_Hybrid_Arachnid","title":"Fenumal Hybrid Arachnid","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary_Scarab","title":"Bestiary Scarab","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary_Scarab_of_the_Herd","title":"Bestiary Scarab of the Herd","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary_Scarab_of_Duplicating","title":"Bestiary Scarab of Duplicating","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary_Scarab_of_the_Shadowed_Crow","title":"Bestiary Scarab of the Shadowed Crow","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Two-Hearted_Hunt","title":"Two-Hearted Hunt (Atlas passive)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Deadly_Prey","title":"Deadly Prey (Atlas passive)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=Beast","title":"poe.ninja Beast price overview (Allflame league)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja Scarab exchange overview (Allflame league)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-02","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0 patch notes mirror","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0 patch notes mirror (Mirage)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0 patch notes mirror (Keepers of the Flame)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.27"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0 patch notes mirror (Mercenaries of Trarthus)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Mighty_Hunter","title":"Mighty Hunter (Atlas passive)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Eternal_Hunt","title":"Eternal Hunt (Atlas passive)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-09-19","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-bestiary-farming-guide","title":"PoE Bestiary Farming Guide (3.29)","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (currency seller)","date":"2026-09-01","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.ezg.com/blog/poe-3-29-beast-farming-is-this-still-one-of-the-best-ways-to-make-currency","title":"PoE 3.29 Beast Farming: Is This Still One of the Best Ways to Make Currency","publisher":"EZG (currency seller)","date":"2026-09-18","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/jp/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0 patch notes","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary_league","title":"Bestiary league (recipes, passives, scarabs)","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Bestiary","title":"Bestiary (atlas mastery passives, bosses)","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Amulets","title":"Amulets (Talisman base types and uniques)","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Craicic_Talisman","title":"Craicic Talisman","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wolf_Alpha_Talisman","title":"Wolf Alpha Talisman","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Farric_Frost_Hellion_Alpha","title":"Farric Frost Hellion Alpha","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Craicic_Spider_Crab","title":"Craicic Spider Crab","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Farrul%2C_First_of_the_Plains","title":"Farrul, First of the Plains","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Saqawal%2C_First_of_the_Sky","title":"Saqawal, First of the Sky","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Fenumus%2C_First_of_the_Night","title":"Fenumus, First of the Night","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Craiceann%2C_First_of_the_Deep","title":"Craiceann, First of the Deep","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=BaseType","title":"poe.ninja Allflame base type prices (API)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueAccessory","title":"poe.ninja Allflame unique accessory prices (API)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/stash/current/item/overview?league=Allflame&type=UniqueArmour","title":"poe.ninja Allflame unique armour prices (API)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"}]},"eldritch":{"title":"Eldritch altars (Searing Exarch / Eater of Worlds)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Eldritch altars spawn in maps with Searing Exarch or Eater of Worlds influence. Each one offers two options, and each option pairs a downside with an upside aimed at you, the Eldritch minions or the map boss. They add loot to almost any mapping strategy for very little effort. In 3.28 currency became a bigger share of drops, which makes the quantity and duplication upsides worth more. In 3.29 Exarch altars gained Trarthan scarabs, and anyone in a party can now click an altar.","howTo":[{"text":"Unlock first: finish the eldritch questline and map completion early in the league, so influence and its altars are open.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[18]},{"text":"Altars appear in maps with Exarch or Eater influence. Each altar shows two options. Click one, or ignore the altar.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Each option targets the Player, Eldritch Minions or the Map Boss, and gives one downside plus one upside.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Pick the map's influence with the Maven/Eater/Exarch buttons at the Map Device. Since 3.28, using the Map Device opens the Atlas screen.","stage":["all"],"cite":[20,30]},{"text":"The influence buttons are hidden on unique maps that can't be Witnessed and in Kirac's Invitation. The 3.29 notes do not mention any change here.","stage":["all"],"cite":[20,31]},{"text":"Altars come from killing influenced monsters, so more kills means more altars. Map layout and density matter.","stage":["all"],"cite":[33]},{"text":"Altars use Extra Content slots, so a map full of other mechanics can block them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[33]},{"text":"If the boss is easy to reach (Dunes, City Square), kill it first. Altars that spawn after that have no boss options. Then clear the map.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,12,13]},{"text":"Minion upsides roll for each influenced monster, so their value grows with how many Eldritch monsters you kill.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Maxroll's general rule: minion options are the strongest and safest. Take boss options after checking the boss's loot. Mostly avoid player options, especially Exarch ones (this guide dates from 3.24).","stage":["all"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"The exception to that rule: player options with Eater influence can be worth taking for magic find, Harvest or Expedition.","stage":["all"],"cite":[29]},{"text":"Read the downside before you click. Some downsides shut down whole builds (see dangers).","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Since 3.29, any party member can click an altar, not only the map owner.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Tier 16 Jungle Valley is the go-to altar map. Its altars can't roll boss mods until you enter the boss arena.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[12,11,16]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Eater: projectiles fire in random directions. This cripples bow, wand and projectile-spell builds.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch: curses you inflict are reflected back to you. This is dangerous for curse-on-hit, hex and Blasphemy builds.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch: you take 600 chaos damage per second during any flask effect. Builds with flasks always running take constant damage.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch flask downsides: more flask charges used with shorter flask duration, a 30% chance to be targeted by a Meteor when you use a flask, and a mod that drains flask charges.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Eater: non-damaging ailments you inflict (chill, shock, freeze, sap) are reflected back to you. This hurts elemental ailment builds.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Eater charge downsides: reduced Defences per Frenzy charge, reduced recovery per Endurance charge, and lower crit multiplier per Power charge.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Resistance downsides: -40 to -60% Fire and Chaos (Exarch) or Cold and Lightning (Eater). The Exarch chaos penalty is the dangerous one if your chaos res is low.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch also has -3000 Armour and -3000 Evasion, Scorch, and Burning Ground when enemies hit you.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Enemy damage boosts: phys gained as extra Fire/Chaos (Exarch) or Cold/Lightning (Eater). These are deadly for builds with a low max hit.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Tankier boss: +50000 Armour or +80% Fire/Chaos res (Exarch), or 50-70% phys reduction or +80% Cold/Lightning res (Eater). Check these against your damage type.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch boss downsides: flask charge drain, a Hinder aura, more Armour and Evasion, and chaos damage with guaranteed Poison.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Eater boss downsides: Blind on hit, Life gained as extra Energy Shield, and always Shock or Chill with extra Lightning or Cold damage.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Exarch minion downsides: Burning or Consecrated Ground on death, Exposure on hit, more AoE, much more Evasion, and extra Chaos or Fire damage.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Rough frequency: each common Eater downside is about 10.4% of rolls, while the charge and random-projectile ones are about 4.2%. Each Exarch player downside is about 10%.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Wrath of the Cosmos: when an altar gets the extra upside, its downsides have 100% increased effect.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[23,3]},{"text":"PoEDB also lists 25% increased damage taken per stack of Wrath of the Cosmos. Check this in game.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[25]},{"text":"Eldritch Gaze always adds a second downside to every Eater altar.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[23,4]}],"sell":[{"text":"Exceptional Eldritch Ichor is about 281c and Exceptional Eldritch Ember about 235c. Sell them (4 Nov 2026).","stage":["all"],"cite":[27]},{"text":"Grand Eldritch Ember is about 11c, but Grand Eldritch Ichor is only about 2.45c.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[27]},{"text":"Valuable Eater-pool scarabs: Ultimatum Catalysing ~456c, Harvest Cornucopia ~199c, Harvest Doubling ~126c, and Breach Resonant Cascade, Legion Eternal Conflict and Kalguuran Refinement at ~55-58c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26,0]},{"text":"Valuable Exarch-pool scarabs: Ambush Containment ~129c, Cartography Risk ~116c, Domination Terrors ~65c, Trarthan Surprising Alliances ~61c and Divination Cloister ~47c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26,0]},{"text":"Base scarabs of these families sell for under 1c, so what matters is which scarab of the family drops.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26]},{"text":"Currency prices (4 Nov 2026): Divine 412.2c, Annulment 16.72c, Ancient 9.18c, Stacked Deck 7.95c, Exalted 3.16c, Scouring 0.55c, Regal 0.11c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[27]}],"strategies":[{"name":"League-start Breach with altars","investment":"Not stated (league-start strategy)","stage":["league-start"],"steps":["Unlock influence early: finish the questline and map completion.","Take three upsides first: increased item quantity, currency duplication and scarab duplication.","Maxroll runs Eater of Worlds here but says the influence choice is not essential.","On maps with an easy boss, kill the boss first, then clear the map for altars."],"cite":[12,18,9]},{"name":"Jungle Valley altar farming","investment":"Not stated","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run Tier 16 Jungle Valley.","Its altars have no boss mods until you enter the arena, so more of them roll player or minion upsides.","Take quantity and duplication upsides.","Increased quantity raises normal monster drops but not the eldritch rewards (embers, ichors, altar-only drops)."],"cite":[12,11,16,29]},{"name":"Exarch map farming with Wrath of the Cosmos (Nightmare/Originator and Kalguuran maps)","investment":"Low (Maxroll rating)","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Searing Exarch influence and the Wrath of the Cosmos keystone.","Maxroll's reason: Nightmare map drops have diminishing returns within one zone, so frequent weaker mods beat rarer strong ones.","Usual picks: map duplication, increased item quantity and scarab drop chance.","Skip any altar whose downside would be disastrous for your build."],"atlasPassives":["Wrath of the Cosmos","The Light of Dawn","Word of the Exarch (with its small nodes)"],"cite":[9,11,16,29]},{"name":"Eater altars for Expedition and scarab farming","investment":"Not stated","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Eater of Worlds influence with The Shadow of Hunger.","Expedition order: item quantity, then currency duplication, then map duplication, then scarab duplication.","Take any altar that would affect the Expedition encounter right away."],"atlasPassives":["The Shadow of Hunger","Rampant Growth (with its small nodes)"],"cite":[14,15,5,29]},{"name":"Stacked Deck farming","investment":"Not stated","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Use Eater of Worlds influence.","Click 'Basic Currency has a chance to be duplicated' altars. Stacked Decks count as basic currency.","Run Jungle Valley to see more of these altars.","Maxroll's last changelog entry for this page is from 3.28."],"cite":[17]},{"name":"Harvest with Eater altars","investment":"Not stated","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Eater of Worlds influence.","Eater altars more reliably raise Lifeforce from non-boss plots, which scales with quantity and pack size."],"cite":[16]},{"name":"Boss rush (Nightmare Boss Rush)","investment":"Not stated","stage":["late"],"steps":["Treat altars as a side bonus.","Take a good altar on the way to the boss.","Do not clear the whole map hunting for more altars."],"cite":[10]},{"name":"8-mod map farming with red altars (previous league)","investment":"About 47c per map (WealthyExile, previous league)","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Use red (Exarch) altars because they are easier to run.","Priority: map duplication, then quantity, then rarity.","About 16 T16 maps plus 1-2 T16.5 per run."],"cite":[35]},{"name":"Red altars as a passive income layer","investment":"Low effort (GhazzyTV)","stage":["mid"],"steps":["GhazzyTV builds several 3.29 atlas trees around red (Exarch) altars.","He pairs them with Heist/Ritual, Blight/Beast/Incursion or Legion/Beyond."],"cite":[19]}],"profit":[{"text":"Wrath of the Cosmos map farming is rated Profitability Excellent, Investment Low, Difficulty Moderate. No number given (rough).","who":"Maxroll (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-09-19","cite":[9]},{"text":"Rough: an Eater boss-currency upside is worth ~0.94c per extra orb (~2.8c for 3). About 65% of that value is the 0.15% Divine chance.","who":"This guide's calculation (PoEDB weights + poe.ninja)","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[0,27]},{"text":"Rough: an Exarch boss-currency upside is worth ~1.04c per extra orb (~3.1c for 3). Grand Embers give ~39% of the value and Chaos Orbs ~19%.","who":"This guide's calculation (PoEDB weights + poe.ninja)","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[0,27]},{"text":"Rough: 50 maps gave 63 div raw. One altar gave 4 div (~6%) and the guide removed it as an outlier. Its 25-30 div/h headline does not match its own figures. The author is a currency seller.","who":"MMOEXP","date":"2026-08-05","cite":[34]},{"text":"Rough: swapping blue altar nodes for red loses only Divine altars, which it calls too rare to matter. Its 34-45 div/h is for the whole strategy, not altars alone.","who":"SebK Blight sheet (3.27)","date":"unknown (3.27)","cite":[36]},{"text":"Rough: at least 96c returned per map against a 47c cost. This covers the whole strategy and is from the previous league.","who":"WealthyExile user strategy","date":"2026-03-23","cite":[35]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Zana's Ingenuity's protection against charge stealing or removal now works against the altar charge-removal downsides.","cite":[8]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Altar, Exarch and Eater atlas passives are unchanged since 3.25.3g.","cite":[23]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"New Exarch altar mods drop Mercenaries (Trarthan) scarabs.","cite":[6,0]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Any party member can now click altars. No Map Device changes.","cite":[6,31]},{"patch":"3.29 data","text":"Gem duplication (Eater) has weight 0, as do Eldritch Chaos, Eldritch Exalted and Eldritch Annulment on both altars. Older guides that recommend these are out of date.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Orb of Scouring upsides moved from Eater altars to Exarch altars.","cite":[7,0]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Eater altars gained Ancient Orb upsides for minions and the boss (weight 1500).","cite":[7,0]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Killing both the Exarch and the Eater now gives one Voidstone in total. The freed Voidstone moved to the Incarnation of Dread.","cite":[7]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"Currency became a much larger share of drops, which raises the value of currency duplication and quantity.","cite":[7]},{"patch":"3.28.0","text":"The Map Device now opens the Atlas screen and has influence buttons.","cite":[30,20]},{"patch":"3.28.0e","text":"Influence buttons are hidden on unwitnessable unique maps and in Kirac's Invitation. Fixed Eldritch influence toggling at Eagon's Map Device.","cite":[20]},{"patch":"3.27.0","text":"No altar changes.","cite":[22]},{"patch":"3.26.0","text":"The combined quantity/rarity upside was split into 10-20% Quantity and 15-30% Rarity.","cite":[21,0]},{"patch":"3.20","text":"Wrath of the Cosmos became less punishing and less rewarding, and Eldritch Gaze now affects only Eater altars. GGG's reason: players were accepting several deaths per map to keep the rewards.","cite":[3]},{"patch":"3.20","text":"Influenced maps went from exactly 60 packs to 20-60 packs, and altar spawn chance was raised by about 50% to compensate.","cite":[28]},{"patch":"3.20","text":"Divines from the Eater basic currency reward became more than twice as common. They are still the lowest active weight (1000).","cite":[28,0]}],"tables":[{"title":"Scarab pools by altar","columns":["Altar","Scarab types","Weight per type"],"rows":[["Eater (Tangle)","Breach, Delirium, Legion, Blight, Ritual, Harvest, Ultimatum, Abyss, Expedition, Betrayal, Bestiary, Incursion, Sulphite, Kalguuran","3187 (14 types)"],["Exarch (Cleansing Fire)","Influence, Cartography, Divination, Anarchy, Misc, Beyond, Torment, Ambush, Domination, Essence, Titanic, Trarthan","1584 (12 types)"],["Both","Boss drops 2-4 extra, or minions have a 1.6-3.2% chance each","All families equally likely"]],"cite":[0]},{"title":"Player upsides","columns":["Upside","Value","Share of player pool"],"rows":[["Item Quantity","10-20%","~33%"],["Item Rarity","15-30%","~33%"],["Dupe Basic Currency","15-30%","~6.7%"],["Dupe Scarabs","15-30%","~6.7%"],["Dupe Maps","15-30%","~6.7%"],["Dupe Div Cards","15-30%","~6.7%"],["Dupe Unique Items","15-30%","~6.7%"],["Dupe Gems (Eater)","-","0 (removed)"]],"cite":[0]},{"title":"Boss currency upsides (2-4 extra orbs)","columns":["Orb","Altar","Weight","Price 4 Nov 2026"],"rows":[["Divine","Eater","1000","412.2c"],["Ancient","Eater","1500","9.18c"],["Exalted","Eater","20000","3.16c"],["Regal","Eater","25000","0.11c"],["Fusing","Eater","100000","-"],["Alteration / Jeweller's","Eater","160000 each","Jeweller's 0.014c"],["Chaos","Exarch","48000","-"],["Scouring","Exarch","30000","0.55c"],["Annulment","Exarch","1000","16.72c"]],"cite":[0,27]},{"title":"Keystones","columns":["Keystone","Effect","Read"],"rows":[["Wrath of the Cosmos (Exarch)","50% chance of an extra upside; altars that get one have 100% increased downside effect","More consistent (Maxroll); high variance"],["Eldritch Gaze (Eater)","Always one extra downside; 50% increased upside effect","Raises the ceiling of blue altars; two downsides every time"]],"cite":[23,3,4,10,24]},{"title":"Atlas notables","columns":["Node","Effect","Maxroll verdict"],"rows":[["The Light of Dawn (Exarch)","50% chance to spawn an Exarch altar when Exarch influence first appears in a map","Must-have"],["The Shadow of Hunger (Eater)","20% increased chance to find Eater altars","Must-have"],["Word of the Exarch / Rampant Growth","10% chance to duplicate Embers / Ichor; 2% chance of an extra Flame Wraith / Tentacle Mass","Mandatory with small nodes"],["Baptised by Fire / Etched by Acid","10% chance of double boss-encounter progress","Not recommended"],["Small nodes","5% pack size for influenced packs (8 points); 0.2% chance for an Eldritch implicit item (5 points)","-"]],"cite":[23,24,29,5]},{"title":"Divination card upsides","columns":["Altar","Card reward types"],"rows":[["Eater","Basic/League Currency, other Div Cards (rarest, weight 3954), Gems"],["Exarch","Unique Weapons/Armour/Jewellery, Corrupted Uniques, Maps, Unique Maps (rarest, weight 2264), Corrupted Items"]],"cite":[0]},{"title":"Influence picks by strategy","columns":["Strategy","Influence","Altar priority"],"rows":[["League-start Breach","Eater (not essential)","Quantity, currency dupe, scarab dupe"],["Expedition","Eater","Quantity > currency dupe > map dupe > scarab dupe"],["Nightmare / Kalguuran maps","Exarch + Wrath","Map dupe, quantity, scarabs"],["Stacked Decks","Eater","Basic currency dupe"],["Harvest","Eater","Quantity, pack size"],["8-mod maps (WealthyExile)","Exarch","Map dupe > quantity > rarity"]],"cite":[12,14,9,11,17,16,35]}],"quickCard":["Easy boss? Kill it first, then clear for altars.","Minion option first; boss if safe; player rarely.","Best upsides: quantity, then currency/map/scarab dupe.","Check the downside: projectiles, curses, flasks, chaos res.","Boss Divine/Annul option: take it if the boss is safe.","Scarab altar: Ultimatum/Harvest (Eater), Ambush/Cartography (Exarch)."],"readMore":[{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Eldritch_Altar","title":"Eldritch Altar (modifier list with weights)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (site shows Allflame 3.29 as current)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Eater_of_Worlds","title":"The Eater of Worlds atlas tree modifiers","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (3.29 era)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Searing_Exarch","title":"The Searing Exarch atlas tree modifiers","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (3.29 era)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Wrath_of_the_Cosmos","title":"Wrath of the Cosmos (keystone + idol, version history)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"current text; history 3.20.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Eldritch_Gaze","title":"Eldritch Gaze (keystone + idol)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"current text; history 3.20.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Shadow_of_Hunger","title":"The Shadow of Hunger (atlas notable)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 - Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Content Update 3.28.0 - Mirage","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"approx. 2026-02-27 to 2026-03-01","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/endgame-strategies/map-farming-strategy","title":"Map Farming Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-09-19","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/nightmare-boss-rush","title":"Nightmare Boss Rush","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/kalguuran-map-farming","title":"Kalguuran Map Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/breach-league-start-strategy","title":"Breach League Start Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/unstable-breach-currency-farming","title":"Unstable Breach Currency Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/big-boom-expedition-farming","title":"Big Boom Expedition Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/ethereal-allflame-scarab-farming","title":"Ethereal Allflame Scarab Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-11","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/cornucopia-harvest","title":"Cornucopia Harvest","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/stacked-deck-farming","title":"Stacked Deck Farming","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Milkybk_)","date":"2026-07-24 (changelog last entry 2026-03-05)","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/league-start-alch-and-go","title":"League Start Alch And Go","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Zen_M)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/atlas-passive-skill-tree-strategies","title":"Atlas Passive Skill Tree Strategies Guide","publisher":"poe-vault.com (GhazzyTV)","date":"2026-08-17","patch":"not stated (site nav 3.29)"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3924293","title":"3.28.0e Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-03-26","patch":"3.28.0e"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3787013","title":"Content Update 3.26.0 - Secrets of the Atlas","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"June 2025","patch":"3.26.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3869068","title":"Content Update 3.27.0 - Keepers of the Flame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"Oct 2025","patch":"3.27.0"},{"url":"https://github.com/grindinggear/atlastree-export","title":"atlastree-export (official Atlas passive tree data)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (GitHub)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Atlas_passive_skill","title":"Atlas passive skill","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Wrath_of_the_Cosmos","title":"Wrath of the Cosmos","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (lists 3.20.0 history)"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Scarab","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview - Scarabs (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 (fetched)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Currency","title":"poe.ninja exchange overview - Currency (Allflame)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 (fetched)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"http://www.gamebanshee.com/9k8r6","title":"Path of Exile 3.20 Balance Manifesto - Eldritch Altars","publisher":"GameBanshee (reprint of GGG manifesto)","date":"unknown (Dec 2022)","patch":"3.20"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/influence-farming-guide","title":"Influence Farming Guide","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2025-01-30","patch":"3.24-era"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0","publisher":"PoEDB (GGG patch notes mirror)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0","publisher":"PoEDB (GGG patch notes mirror)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3579828","title":"Does Eldritch Altar quantity affect Strongboxes?","publisher":"PoE official forum (player thread)","date":"2024-10-03","patch":"3.25-era"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3301643","title":"How to maximize Eldritch altar spawns?","publisher":"PoE official forum (player thread)","date":"2022-08-29","patch":"3.19-era"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-29-currency-farming-guide-25-30-div-hour-fast-delirium-map-strategy.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Currency Farming Guide: 25-30 Div/Hour Fast Delirium Map Strategy","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-05","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://wealthyexile.com/strategies/6346/8mod_map_farming","title":"8mod map farming","publisher":"WealthyExile (user strategy)","date":"2026-03-23","patch":"unknown (previous league, likely 3.27)"},{"url":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xiJDgOAVBS8JkRd0nq9xp_3UrGbu1ZAk5XSEUtMxEeQ/edit","title":"Invigoration Bloodlines Blight (SebK/Mosorzasty strategy sheet)","publisher":"Google Sheets (streamer guide)","date":"unknown (written during 3.27)","patch":"3.27"}]},"essences":{"title":"Essence Farming","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Essences trap monsters in maps. Free a monster and kill it, and it drops the essences it held. A Vaal Orb on a monster holding a Screaming Misery, Envy, Dread or Scorn essence can turn them into tier-8 Hysteria, Insanity, Horror or Delirium, worth about 33-52c each late in the league. Since 3.28 each Essence Scarab adds 3 monsters, essences stack to 10 and Vaal Orbs cost under 1c, and 3.29 did not nerf essences.","howTo":[{"text":"To corrupt an essence monster, use a Vaal Orb on it. Vaal Orbs took over the Remnant of Corruption's job in 3.27.","stage":["all"],"cite":[4,10]},{"text":"Corrupting gives one random result: the monster breaks out stronger, all its essences go up one tier (not past Deafening), it gains an extra essence, or its essences change to the next type group.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,7,24]},{"text":"No source gives the odds for each corruption result.","stage":["all"],"cite":[24]},{"text":"Hysteria, Insanity, Horror and Delirium only come from corrupting a monster that holds a Screaming (tier 5) Misery, Envy, Dread or Scorn essence (MEDS).","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,3,7]},{"text":"Corrupting a monster with Shrieking essences is one way to get Deafening. The other is the vendor upgrade.","stage":["all"],"cite":[24]},{"text":"Tiers: Whispering 1, Muttering 2, Weeping 3, Wailing 4, Screaming 5, Shrieking 6, Deafening 7. Tier 8 is the corrupted set.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Tiers 1-4 only turn normal items rare. Tier 5 and up can also reforge a rare item with one guaranteed mod.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Upgrading: a vendor (or the Essence stash tab) combines 3 of the same type and tier into 1 of the next tier.","stage":["all","ssf"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Harvest: Wild Homunculus changes a stack's type within its tier. Vivid Watcher raises it one tier.","stage":["all","ssf"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Harvest type reroll costs Primal (blue) lifeforce: 30 per use, scaled to stack size.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[31]},{"text":"At league start, get to yellow maps fast. White maps cap essences at Screaming, yellow maps at Shrieking.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Amplified Energies caps essences at Screaming in white maps and Shrieking in yellow and red maps. Run yellow tier or above.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[7,3,18]},{"text":"Alch and Go: before entering, check for map mods that are dangerous for your build or would make the map impossible to finish.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Alch and Go: transmute, alch or Vaal each map so the run counts toward atlas completion.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"With Crystal Resonance: kill every essence monster first and the map boss last. The boss collects their mods and drops extra essences.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"With Crystal Resonance: don't use Vaal Orbs on essence monsters, because they can't give corrupted essences.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[1,8]},{"text":"Buy supplies for a big batch of maps up front, so you aren't stopping often to sell and restock.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Older pre-3.27 guide: essence rewards don't scale with map tier past T6, or with item quantity, rarity or pack size.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Older pre-3.27 guide: when combined with other mechanics, the farm map should yield to the other mechanic.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3]}],"dangers":[{"text":"A corrupted essence monster has a physical damage-over-time aura that slows you. You can't leech from it.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,7]},{"text":"When a corrupted essence monster dies, 2 Fleshmonsters spawn where its drop lands. Leech builds need care.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,7]},{"text":"A corrupted essence monster gets 700% more life and 30% reduced damage taken. You need damage to kill it fast.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[24]},{"text":"Since 3.25 each essence adds toughness (100% toughness = 50% less damage taken). Crystal Lattice and Adaptation make monsters much slower to kill.","stage":["all"],"cite":[24]},{"text":"With Adaptation, each release gives another monster an extra essence mod, so later monsters get tougher.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[16,7]},{"text":"Crystal Resonance makes the map boss much harder. The older guide calls these bosses 'extremely dangerous'. Bring single-target damage.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1,3]},{"text":"Crystal Resonance: an already damaged boss heals to full when it gains a mod. In multi-boss maps each mod goes to only one boss.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[28]},{"text":"City Square: when one of its 3 bosses dies, the others enrage. Kill the rest quickly.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[29,1]},{"text":"Crystal Resonance makes a Vaal Orb replace all of a monster's essences with one of its own types. You get no tier 8. Don't take it for corrupted farming.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[8,1]},{"text":"Essence-trapped monsters and beasts can be very tanky. Maxroll suggests dropping the Bestiary nodes to skip the beasts, at a small profit loss.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Dance of Destruction in the Corrupted tree gives monsters 25% more damage.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21,23]},{"text":"Outdated advice: Remnants of Corruption no longer exist, and the Kirac Essence map-device mod was removed in 3.28. Ignore guides or filters that still mention them.","stage":["all"],"cite":[10,3,11]}],"sell":[{"text":"Upgrade every essence to Deafening, reroll Deafening and corrupted ones into the priciest types at the Harvest bench, then sell in bulk.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,1]},{"text":"Late league, essences below Deafening barely sell. Most Shrieking and Screaming list at 1c or less in tiny volumes.","stage":["late"],"cite":[32]},{"text":"Exceptions: Shrieking Scorn (about 21c) and Shrieking Dread (about 5c).","stage":["late"],"cite":[32]},{"text":"Tier 8 (Insanity, Horror, Delirium, Hysteria) is the most valuable essence to aim for.","stage":["late"],"cite":[32]},{"text":"Corrupted strategy: Heist drops are a big share of income. Sell Rogue's Markers in bulk.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Deception contracts sell best. Late in the league only Deception sells well.","stage":["late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Deafening strategy: also sell beasts. Craicic Chimeral and Fenumal Plagued Arachnid are the best red beasts.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"League start: essences are your main trade funds. After the first few days, sell with bulk tools and upgrade to the single grade a buyer takes.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Older guide: sell tier 8 first, Shrieking early in the league and Deafening later.","stage":["league-start","late"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Older guide warns that Harvest rerolls can lose money, especially on Deafening. At about 0.04c per Primal lifeforce now, that risk looks small.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[3,31,33]}],"strategies":[{"name":"League-start Alch and Go (Maxroll 3.29)","investment":"Low. Maxroll names no scarabs, only rolling maps with transmute, alch or Vaal.","stage":["league-start"],"steps":["Push to yellow maps fast. White maps cap at Screaming, yellow maps drop Shrieking.","Check every map for mods that are deadly for your build or impossible to finish.","Transmute, alch or Vaal each map so it counts toward atlas completion.","Sell essences as your main source of trade funds.","After the first few days, sell with bulk tools. Upgrade to the one grade a buyer wants, since buyers take your whole stack of that grade.","Expect low profit. Income after your first 2 Voidstones is far higher than anything before."],"atlasPassives":["Prolific Essence (1 guaranteed imprisoned monster per map)","Amplified Energies (Screaming cap in white maps, Shrieking in yellow and red)"],"cite":[2,19,18,7]},{"name":"Deafening Essences (Crystal Resonance, Maxroll 3.29)","investment":"Average (Maxroll rating). Medium difficulty, Good profit, called a starter strategy.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"steps":["Use the 'Yellow Map Essence' atlas tree (Maxroll planner o3n7w034, tree #3, 3.29).","Run City Square. Its 3 bosses split the Crystal Resonance mods.","Alch every map at 20% quality. Scour and re-alch maps your build can't run.","Optional: roll for '% increased number of rare monsters' for more essence monsters. It costs more time and currency, and Maxroll says it is usually worth it.","Use Domination Shrines and Niko's Sulphite buffs to clear the very hard yellow maps.","Kill every essence monster first and the map boss last.","Don't use Vaal Orbs. Crystal Resonance blocks corrupted essences.","You need strong single-target damage for the boss.","Upgrade everything to Deafening, reroll at the Harvest bench into the priciest types, and sell in bulk. Sell the best red beasts too."],"atlasPassives":["Prolific Essence","Crystal Lattice","Amplified Energies","Crystal Resonance","Bestiary: Big Game, Eternal Hunt, Natural Selection, The Hunt for Craiceann, Two-Hearted Hunt","Ritual: Sacred Lands, Occult Devotion","Shrine and Delve notables","Refiner's Bargain"],"scarabs":["Essence Scarab of Calcification","Essence Scarab of Ascent","Essence Scarab of Adaptation","2x Scarab of Adversaries"],"cite":[1,22,23,8]},{"name":"Corrupted Essences, low investment (Maxroll 3.29)","investment":"Average (Maxroll rating). Medium difficulty, Amazing profit, low management.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Use Maxroll planner qzn97032, tree #3 (3.29, 138 points). It has no Crystal Resonance, so Vaal Orbs can still make tier 8.","Run Tier 16 Strand. Searing Exarch influence is optional.","Roll maps with Alchemy at 20% quality. Scour and re-alch mods your build can't run.","Optional: roll for '% increased number of rare monsters'.","Run Essence Scarab of Stability so corruption only upgrades or transforms.","Vaal only the purple MEDS monsters (Misery, Envy, Dread, Scorn). Maxroll calls the tier-8 chance high.","Kill corrupted monsters fast. They are much tankier.","Upgrade to Deafening, reroll at the Harvest bench, and sell in bulk. Sell Heist drops too."],"atlasPassives":["Prolific Essence","Crystal Lattice","Amplified Energies","Small nodes: 4x Essence Chance, 5x Imprisoned Monster Additional Essence Chance, 2x Essence Rare Chance","No Crystal Resonance"],"scarabs":["3x Essence Scarab (9 extra essence monsters)","Essence Scarab of Ascent","Essence Scarab of Stability"],"cite":[0,21,23,16,17]},{"name":"Corrupted Essences, high investment (Maxroll 3.29)","investment":"Higher. Swap the base Essence Scarabs for Calcification, Adaptation and Adversaries.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Same map, rolling and Vaal rules as the low-investment version (T16 Strand, Vaal only MEDS).","Adaptation passes essence mods between monsters, so later monsters get tougher and more rewarding.","The tree also takes a large Heist and Smuggler's Cache cluster. Heist drops are a big share of income.","Keystones: Dance of Destruction (monsters deal 25% more damage and have 25% less life), Refiner's Bargain, Synthesised Stability, Wrath of the Cosmos.","Strand's bosses (Master of the Blade, Massier) get no essence mods, because the tree has no Crystal Resonance."],"atlasPassives":["Prolific Essence, Crystal Lattice, Amplified Energies","Heist and Cache: Secret Stash, No Honour Among Thieves, Casing the Joint, Friends in High Places, The Dutiful Soldier","Shrine: Supplication, Syncretism, Drawn to Power","Delve: Frantic Mining, Packed with Energy, Mining Byproducts","Exarch: The Light of Dawn, Word of the Exarch","3 Shaping notables, Invasive Adversaries, Mounting Modifiers","Dance of Destruction, Refiner's Bargain, Synthesised Stability, Wrath of the Cosmos"],"scarabs":["Essence Scarab of Calcification","Essence Scarab of Ascent","Essence Scarab of Stability","Essence Scarab of Adaptation","Scarab of Adversaries"],"cite":[0,21,23,30]},{"name":"Einhar Memory of Crystal Prisons (older guide)","investment":"Low. One Atlas Memory run.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["From the pre-3.27 Maxroll guide. Not re-checked for 3.29.","Run it on a yellow Tier 6 map with Voidstones removed and no alch.","Rogue exiles in it often drop Shrieking and Deafening.","Atlas Memories ignore your atlas passives."],"cite":[3]}],"profit":[{"text":"Corrupted Essences: profit rated 'Amazing', investment Average, difficulty Medium, management Low. No chaos or divine per hour given. Rough rating only.","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-08-04","cite":[0]},{"text":"Deafening Essences: profit rated 'Good', investment Average, difficulty Medium. Rough rating only.","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-08-04","cite":[1]},{"text":"Alch and Go: profit rated 'Low'. Income after the first 2 Voidstones is far higher. Rough rating only.","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-07-24","cite":[2]},{"text":"Rough late-league prices: Insanity about 52c, Horror 52c, Delirium 41c, Hysteria 33c. Divine about 412c.","who":"poe.ninja Allflame exchange","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[32,33]},{"text":"Vaal Orb about 0.37c (rough). Corrupting every MEDS monster costs little next to a 33-52c tier-8 essence.","who":"poe.ninja Allflame exchange","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[33]},{"text":"Primal lifeforce about 0.04c each (rough), so 30 per reroll is cheap.","who":"poe.ninja Allflame exchange","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[31,33]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Larger range for freeing a trapped essence monster.","cite":[15,24]},{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Fixed the Essence Rare Chance node sometimes dropping items with Essence of Desolation mods.","cite":[15]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Dredged currency (Allflame) works on essences. Fixed Vesper essence upgrades not applying.","cite":[14]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"No direct changes to essence monsters, scarabs or notables. Essence mod values rose with the spell crit and added spell damage buffs.","cite":[6,12]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Underground Sea removed from the Atlas, so Maxroll dropped it. City Square and Strand are unchanged.","cite":[6,0,1]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Base Essence Scarab: 3 extra monsters per map, up from 2 (limit 5, so up to 15). Ruthless is unaffected.","cite":[5,11,16]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Essences stack to 10, up from 9.","cite":[5,11]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Vaal Orb corruption now awards the Essence Corruption achievement. The text says a Vaal Orb is required.","cite":[5,11]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Essence of Insanity ring mod: 60% of hit damage can't be reflected, up from 40%.","cite":[11]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Map device crafting removed and Cartographer's Chisels unobtainable, so the Kirac Essence mod is gone. Maxroll removed it from its guides.","cite":[11,1,0]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Essence of Desolation added (tier 0). Reforges normal or rare items, but its guaranteed mod is level 15 and below.","cite":[20]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Vaal Orbs can now corrupt essence monsters, doing what Remnants of Corruption did.","cite":[4,10]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Remnants of Corruption stopped dropping. Existing Remnants became Vaal Orbs.","cite":[4,10]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"Essence of Fear helmet mod now gives Minion Damage instead of Minion Accuracy.","cite":[10]},{"patch":"3.26","text":"Kirac Essence map mod: cost cut to 4 Chaos (from 6), adds 3 monsters (from 4).","cite":[13]},{"patch":"guide note","text":"Maxroll's older Essence Farming Guide (Jan 2025) still uses Remnants, the Kirac mod and 3x Essence Scarab + Ascent at 2 monsters each. That is outdated for 3.29.","cite":[3,10,11,16]}],"tables":[{"title":"Essence tiers","columns":["Tier","Name","What it can do"],"rows":[["1","Whispering","Turns a normal item rare"],["2","Muttering","Turns a normal item rare"],["3","Weeping","Turns a normal item rare"],["4","Wailing","Turns a normal item rare"],["5","Screaming","Also reforges a rare; MEDS at this tier can corrupt into tier 8"],["6","Shrieking","Also reforges a rare; yellow/red map cap with Amplified Energies"],["7","Deafening","Also reforges a rare; corruption won't raise it further"],["8","Hysteria / Insanity / Horror / Delirium","Corruption only"]],"cite":[7,9]},{"title":"Vaal Orb on an essence monster","columns":["Result","Without Stability","With Stability"],"rows":[["Breaks out empowered (no essence change)","Possible","Removed"],["All essences +1 tier (not past Deafening)","Possible","Possible"],["Extra essence","Possible","Likely excluded by wording, not confirmed"],["Types change to next group (MEDS to tier 8)","Possible","Possible"],["With Crystal Resonance","All essences become one of its own types, no tier 8","Same"]],"cite":[9,7,24,17,25,8]},{"title":"Essence scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Limit","Effect","Used in"],"rows":[["Essence Scarab","5","+3 imprisoned monsters each","Corrupted low (3x)"],["Ascent","1","Essences one tier higher","All three Maxroll setups"],["Stability","1","Corruption only upgrades or transforms","Corrupted low and high"],["Calcification","1","Natural rares get imprisoned","Deafening, Corrupted high"],["Adaptation","1","Passes essence mods on release; more difficulty and reward","Deafening, Corrupted high"],["Scarab of Adversaries","2","+4 packs of Mirrored Rares (link to Calcification not confirmed)","Deafening (2x), Corrupted high"]],"cite":[16,7,17,0,1,26,27]},{"title":"Essence atlas passives","columns":["Passive","Effect","Deafening tree","Corrupted tree"],"rows":[["Prolific Essence","+1 imprisoned monster per map","Yes","Yes"],["Essence Chance (small)","5% chance of +1 monster","Not listed","4x"],["Crystal Lattice","15% chance of 3 extra essences","Yes","Yes"],["Additional Essence Chance (small)","5% chance of +1 essence","Not listed","5x"],["Amplified Energies","One essence at max tier: Screaming white, Shrieking yellow/red","Yes","Yes"],["Crystal Resonance","Boss gets a mod per essence monster killed; blocks tier 8","Yes","No"],["Essence Rare Chance (small)","25% chance of an extra rare with an essence mod","Not listed","2x"],["Crystalline Carapaces","Map scarab drops 100% more likely to be Essence Scarabs","Not listed","Not listed"]],"cite":[7,8,18,19,21,22,23]},{"title":"Maxroll 3.29 strategies","columns":["Strategy","Map","Vaal Orbs","Difficulty","Investment","Profit"],"rows":[["Alch and Go","Any, yellow ASAP","Optional on maps","Not stated","Not stated","Low"],["Deafening Essences","City Square (yellow)","No","Medium","Average","Good"],["Corrupted Essences","T16 Strand","MEDS only","Medium","Average","Amazing"]],"cite":[2,1,0]},{"title":"Price snapshot, Allflame late league (rough)","columns":["Item","Price"],"rows":[["Essence of Insanity","about 52c"],["Essence of Horror","about 52c"],["Essence of Delirium","about 41c"],["Essence of Hysteria","about 33c"],["Shrieking Scorn","about 21c"],["Shrieking Dread","about 5c"],["Most other Shrieking / Screaming","1c or less"],["Vaal Orb","about 0.37c"],["Primal lifeforce","about 0.04c each"],["Divine Orb","about 412c"]],"cite":[32,33]}],"quickCard":["Vaal only purple Screaming MEDS monsters","Crystal Resonance on: no Vaal, boss last","Run yellow maps or higher (Shrieking cap)","Corrupted mob: slowing aura, no leech","Upgrade to Deafening, then sell in bulk","No Remnants now: Vaal Orbs do the job"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/corrupted-essences","title":"Corrupted Essences Farming Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Zen_M, reviewed by IBoilerUp)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/deafening-essences","title":"Deafening Essences - PoE 3.29","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Zen_M)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/league-start-alch-and-go","title":"League Start Alch And Go Farming Strategy - PoE 3.29","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Zen_M, reviewed by Facefoot)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/essence-farming-guide","title":"Essence Farming Guide","publisher":"Maxroll.gg (Tenkiei)","date":"2025-01-30 (changelog ends 2024-04-06)","patch":"unknown (pre-3.27; still describes Remnants of Corruption and the Kirac modifier)"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3869068","title":"Content Update 3.27.0 - Path of Exile: Keepers of the Flame (patch notes)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"unknown (3.27 launch, late Oct 2025)","patch":"3.27.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Content Update 3.28.0 - Path of Exile: Mirage (patch notes)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (Stacey_GGG)","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 - Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame (patch notes)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"unknown (image paths dated Jul 2026)","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Essence","title":"Essence (PoEDB)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (live database)","patch":"unknown (current game data; corruption section text still says Remnant)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Crystal_Resonance","title":"Crystal Resonance (PoEDB)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (live database)","patch":"unknown (current data; text references Vaal Orb, so post-3.27)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Remnant_of_Corruption","title":"Remnant of Corruption (PoEDB)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (pre-3.27 item; outcomes now apply to Vaal Orbs per 3.27 notes)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0 (Keepers of the Flame) patch notes","publisher":"poedb.tw (mirror of GGG patch notes)","date":"unknown (latest dated entry 2025-10-31)","patch":"3.27"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0 (Mirage) patch notes","publisher":"poedb.tw (mirror of GGG patch notes)","date":"unknown (image paths dated 2026-02-27)","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0 (Curse of the Allflame) patch notes","publisher":"poedb.tw (mirror of GGG patch notes)","date":"unknown (news image dated 2026-07-17)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0 (Mercenaries of Trarthus / Secrets of the Atlas) patch notes","publisher":"poedb.tw (mirror of GGG patch notes)","date":"unknown (2025)","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991672","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Essence_Scarab","title":"Essence Scarab","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Essence_Scarab_of_Stability","title":"Essence Scarab of Stability","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Amplified_Energies","title":"Amplified Energies (Atlas notable)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Prolific_Essence","title":"Prolific Essence (Atlas notable)","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Essence_of_Desolation","title":"Essence of Desolation","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28 (Mirage badge)"},{"url":"https://planners.maxroll.gg/profiles/poe/qzn97032","title":"Corrupted Essences atlas planner (embedded in the guide as #3)","publisher":"Maxroll planner (user Zenm)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29 (tree version 3290)"},{"url":"https://planners.maxroll.gg/profiles/poe/o3n7w034","title":"Yellow Map Essence atlas planner (embedded in the Deafening guide as #3)","publisher":"Maxroll planner (user Zenm)","date":"2026-08-04","patch":"3.29 (tree version 3290)"},{"url":"https://github.com/grindinggear/atlastree-export","title":"Atlas passive tree export (tag 3.29.1), used to turn planner node IDs into names and stat text","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Essence","title":"Essence","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown (version history runs to 3.29.3)","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Essence_Scarab_of_Stability","title":"Essence Scarab of Stability","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (introduced 3.24.0, no later changes listed)"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Scarab_of_Adversaries","title":"Scarab of Adversaries","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (introduced 3.24.0, no later changes listed)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Scarab_of_Adversaries","title":"Scarab of Adversaries","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Crystal_Resonance","title":"Crystal Resonance","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (last change listed 3.25.0d)"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/City_Square","title":"City Square Map","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.poewiki.net/wiki/Strand","title":"Strand Map","publisher":"PoE Wiki","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (mentions 3.28.0)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Horticrafting","title":"Horticrafting","publisher":"poedb","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Essence","title":"Allflame essence exchange prices (snapshot fetched 2026-11-04)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/poe1/api/economy/exchange/current/overview?league=Allflame&type=Currency","title":"Allflame currency exchange prices (snapshot fetched 2026-11-04)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","patch":"3.29"}]},"kingsmarch":{"title":"Kingsmarch (Settlers): shipping and town","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Kingsmarch is the Settlers town. Workers mine, smelt and farm, and you ship ore, bars, crops and Thaumaturgic Dust to seven ports. Since 3.28, ore and bars return currency, crops return equipment, and the port you pick decides the Tattoo or Runegraft type. 3.29 made no shipping changes. Maxroll rates ore farming and map farming B tier, and both are active farms now, not passive ones.","howTo":[{"text":"Do not start Kingsmarch on day one. Ease in around days 2-3, once your mapping and Gold income are up.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"The town starts fully built. Buildings have not been upgradable since 3.26; only workers level, ranks 1-5. Ignore 3.25 guides about Town Hall, Port or Smeltery tiers.","stage":["all"],"cite":[22,24]},{"text":"Hire Rank 5 Miners, Smelters and Farmers plus one team of Shippers. Mining and smelting speed limit how fast you can ship.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"To hire, use the cheaper 4,000 Gold recruit reroll. The high-quality reroll at Raulf costs 16,000.","stage":["all"],"cite":[22,23,12]},{"text":"Do not give the Mapper tag to workers who are not mapping, because it raises their wages.","stage":["all"],"cite":[12,10,7]},{"text":"Ore and bars return currency. Crops return equipment. Send each for that purpose.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,1,17]},{"text":"Smelt before you ship. A bar counts 5x toward a port quota and adds about 4x to shipment value (PoEDB data).","stage":["all"],"cite":[8,11]},{"text":"A shipment must be worth between 50,000 and 50,000,000.","stage":["all"],"cite":[8]},{"text":"Reroll a port's Favoured Resources (quota) for 15,000 Gold until it asks for the ore or bars you hold. Then each big shipment also fills the quota.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,12]},{"text":"A completed quota adds a random +20% to +100% to shipment value plus an extra item, usually a Unique. Quotas can span several shipments, never expire, and refresh once completed.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6,8]},{"text":"Add Thaumaturgic Dust (from disenchanting at Rog) up to about the same value as your bars. Past that it scales by square root. Dust does not count toward quotas or Tattoo/Runegraft thresholds.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[6,8,10,12,16,13]},{"text":"Mix two or more resource types in a shipment. One type caps the return at 500 currency items; mixing lifts it to 800.","stage":["late"],"cite":[10]},{"text":"Send crops on their own. Never add ore or dust to a crop shipment.","stage":["all"],"cite":[10,16,12]},{"text":"Ship only when the port shows 0% risk. Higher-rank shipper crews lower the risk.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[10,12,14]},{"text":"Pick the port by the Tattoo or Runegraft type you want. All ports pay currency from the same table.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0,10]},{"text":"If a mapper is kidnapped, guides say ransoming them for up to 50,000 Gold is worth it.","stage":["all"],"cite":[12,10,7]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Risk rises with shipment value. AOEAH says Kalguur keeps about a 10% risk floor on high-value shipments even with six Rank 5 shippers. Never send bars to a port with active risk.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[10,12,14]},{"text":"There are 20 failure outcomes: losing a quarter, half, three quarters or all of the cargo (or only its ore, crops or dust), returns cut by 25-75%, a dead crew member, a delay, or a pirate takeover.","stage":["all"],"cite":[8,7]},{"text":"If pirates take a ship you can fight them (one portal; fail and you lose everything), pay a 50,000 Gold ransom (cargo and crew back, no boss loot), or abandon it. Crew can be lost for good.","stage":["all"],"cite":[6,8]},{"text":"In 3.29 you cannot be damaged or stunned while channelling Verisium. A fully charged deposit still spawns fights like Delve depth 800-1000. Stop at about 60-70% unless your build is strong.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[18,11,25]},{"text":"Workers with the Mapper or Disenchanter tag cost several times more in wages; one guide saw 19k rise to 68k Gold/hour. Farmers draw about 300 Gold/hour each even when idle.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[10,11]},{"text":"Crimson Infusion speeds maps up but fills them with the cheapest ore, which lowers big-shipment value.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[10,12]},{"text":"Lost in Transit swaps 6% of deposits for Lost Shipments. A 3.28 guide warns it reduces ore.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[29,25]},{"text":"Shipping no longer gives gems, scarabs or Stacked Decks. Guides built around those rewards are obsolete.","stage":["all"],"cite":[10,12,26]},{"text":"Dust past parity adds very little. Do not dump huge stacks into one shipment.","stage":["late"],"cite":[11,8]},{"text":"In 3.28, Mirage could duplicate ore, turn it into dust, or lose it in transit. Mirage was the 3.28 league, so this may not apply in 3.29.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[12,10]}],"sell":[{"text":"8-mod corrupted Nightmare/Originator maps from Kalguuran map farming.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[4]},{"text":"Timeless Splinters: in 3.29 they drop only from Legion and from maps run by Atlas Runners.","stage":["mid","late","ssf"],"cite":[18,2]},{"text":"10 Runegrafts only come from shipping: Agile, Connection, Consecration, Fury, Imbued, Rallying, Resurgence, Rotblood, Spellbound, Suffering.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,17]},{"text":"Shipping-only uniques (likely from quota completions): Cadigan's Authority, Ynda's Stand, Tawhoa's Felling, Kaom's Command.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[28]},{"text":"AOEAH says the Kalguuran Scarab of Refinement becomes the priciest Kalguuran scarab later in the league.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"Rares from crop shipments and Atlas Runners roll lower tiers since 3.28, so they are worth less to sell.","stage":["all"],"cite":[0]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Settlers Ore Farming (Maxroll)","investment":"Low; rated Very Easy","stage":["league-start","mid"],"steps":["Run maps with Niko Sulphite veins and the Refiner's Bargain keystone.","Refiner's Bargain turns map Sulphite into random ore at 10% of its value.","Mine the deposits and have workers smelt the ore into bars.","Ship bars with matching dust to a 0% risk port."],"atlasPassives":["Refiner's Bargain (keystone)"],"scarabs":["Kalguuran Scarab","Sulphite scarab","Kalguuran Scarab of Refinement","Kalguuran Scarab of Enriching"],"cite":[3,9]},{"name":"Kalguuran Map Farming (Maxroll, 3.29.1)","investment":"Low; average profit, above-average difficulty","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run T16 Originator-influenced Jungle Valley, which cannot spawn boss altars.","Take Searing Exarch altars.","Sell the 8-mod corrupted Nightmare/Originator maps.","Keep the ore as a byproduct for shipping."],"scarabs":["Cartography Scarab of Escalation","Kalguuran Scarab of Guarded Riches","Kalguuran Scarab x2","Cartography Scarab of Corruption"],"cite":[4]},{"name":"Late-game bar + dust shipments (AOEAH plan)","investment":"Not rated by the source; needs millions of bars and dust per shipment","stage":["late"],"steps":["Aim for about 92% ore deposit chance on the atlas, counting blockers.","Plan about 4M in bars and about 4M in dust per shipment.","Add the Refinement scarab once smelters cannot keep up.","Activate Bismuth first and Verisium last, and stop at a difficulty your build can handle."],"atlasPassives":["Yield Upon Yield","Fortune's Favour","Lost in Transit (6%, may reduce ore)","Verisium Infusion","Crimson Infusion (other guides warn against it)","Bismuth Infusion","Prospector's Luck"],"scarabs":["Kalguuran Scarab","Kalguuran Scarab of Enriching","Kalguuran Scarab of Refinement"],"cite":[11,25,28,10,12]},{"name":"Crop shipments for targeted gear","investment":"Low; needs farmers and crops only","stage":["mid","ssf"],"steps":["The crop picks the item slot; the port picks the attribute or base type.","Send crops on their own, with no ore or dust.","Use Blue Zanthimum for jewellery: Rings at Riben Fell, Belts at Pondium, Amulets at Kalguur.","Use the Karui ports for armour of one attribute.","Rares from shipping roll lower modifier tiers since 3.28."],"atlasPassives":["Refiner's Bargain (map Lifeforce becomes crops at 250% value)"],"cite":[8,12,10,9,0]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough: a shipment worth about 700k gives roughly a 50% chance of a Divine. A full 50M shipment averages about 2.5 Mirror Shards.","who":"AOEAH 3.28 cheat sheet (unattributed)","date":"2026-03","cite":[10,11]},{"text":"Rough: the same 700k / 50M figures, repeated for 3.29. Player forum reports from 3.28 are lower.","who":"AOEAH 3.29 cheat sheet","date":"2026-07","cite":[11]},{"text":"Rough: bar shipments worth 100k-150k occasionally return a Divine (community reports). The late-game plan is about 4M bars plus 4M dust per shipment.","who":"AOEAH, citing community reports","date":"2026-03 / 2026-07","cite":[10,11]},{"text":"Rough: a 241k bar shipment becomes 482k with matching dust, but another 30M dust adds only a few million.","who":"AOEAH 3.29 example","date":"2026-07","cite":[11]},{"text":"Rough: one player saw 50M ships drop from 3-6 Mirror Shards in 3.27 to 0-1 in 3.28. Another put a 50M ship at about 10-20 Divines if you farm the dust yourself. GGG did not respond.","who":"Players on the official forum","date":"2026-02 / 2026-03","cite":[26,27]},{"text":"Rough, unsupported: 8-15 Divines/hour for experienced T15-16 ore farmers and 3-6 for newer ones. No data is given.","who":"WowCarry FAQ (unsigned)","date":"2026-05","cite":[14]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.1-3.29.3","text":"Nothing for shipping. 3.29.3 only made the Farm Plot and Workers dropdowns taller.","cite":[19,20,21]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"No shipping changes. Isla can identify items, Atlas Runner maps still drop Timeless Splinters, and channelling Verisium makes you immune to damage and stun.","cite":[2,18]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Rewards swapped: ore and bars return currency, crops return equipment.","cite":[0,1,17]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Added a seventh port, the Karui port Mota Aro (PoEDB spells it Moti Aro).","cite":[0,1,8]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Ports no longer favour a currency type. Each port gives one Tattoo or Runegraft category.","cite":[0,10,8]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Port Favoured Resources (quota) can be rerolled for 15,000 Gold.","cite":[0,8]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Smelters work twice as fast but cost more Gold. Farmer wages halved; mapper wages up 25%.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Rares from Shipping and Mapping roll lower modifier tiers. Mappers no longer return Cluster Jewels above item level 83.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Added 10 shipping-only Runegrafts.","cite":[0,17]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Shipping no longer returns gems, scarabs or Stacked Decks.","cite":[10,12,26]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The base Kalguuran Scarab adds 2 ore deposits (was 1). Added the Kalguuran Scarab of Enriching.","cite":[0,1,17]},{"patch":"3.28.0c","text":"Every Lost Shipment chest except the central one can be broken by damage. The central chest got a clearer label.","cite":[33]},{"patch":"3.28.0e","text":"Fixed magic monsters near Bismuth ore getting duplicate mods.","cite":[34]},{"patch":"3.28.0j","text":"Added an overview estimate of how long map device jobs take. During the (now ended) Return of the Ancestors event, Karui ports gave Runegrafts instead of Tattoos.","cite":[35]},{"patch":"3.27","text":"The high-quality recruit reroll at Raulf now costs 16,000 Gold (was 20,000).","cite":[23]},{"patch":"3.26","text":"Settlers went core. Buildings no longer upgrade, and worker ranks dropped from 10 to 5.","cite":[22,24]}],"tables":[{"title":"Ore / bar shipment value per unit (PoEDB data vs AOEAH 3.29 sheet: they disagree)","columns":["Ore","PoEDB ore","PoEDB bar","AOEAH 3.29 ore","AOEAH 3.29 bar"],"rows":[["Crimson Iron","4","16","4","16"],["Orichalcum","5","19","5","22"],["Petrified Amber","6","24","7","30"],["Bismuth","9","37","12","50"],["Verisium","16","64","22","90"]],"cite":[8,11]},{"title":"Ports: Tattoo / Runegraft type","columns":["Port","Side","Tattoo / Runegraft","Crop gear"],"rows":[["Ngakanu","Karui","STR Tattoos","STR armour"],["Te Onui","Karui","DEX Tattoos","DEX armour"],["Mota (Moti) Aro","Karui","INT Tattoos (from tables only)","INT armour"],["Riben Fell","Kalguuran","Runegrafts (PoEDB: DEX)","See crop table"],["Pondium","Kalguuran","Runegrafts (PoEDB: STR)","See crop table"],["Kalguur","Kalguuran","Runegrafts (PoEDB: STR, unconfirmed)","See crop table"]],"cite":[8,10,3]},{"title":"Crop rewards by port (crop picks slot, port picks base)","columns":["Crop","Value/unit","Riben Fell","Pondium","Kalguur","Karui ports"],"rows":[["Wheat","12","Staves/Warstaves","Wands","Sceptres","Body Armours"],["Corn","15","Claws","Daggers","Bows/Quivers","Helmets"],["Pumpkin","18","Swords","Maces","Axes","Boots"],["Orgourd","21","Ward Boots","Ward Gloves","Ward Helmets","Gloves"],["Blue Zanthimum","24","Rings","Belts","Amulets","Shields"]],"cite":[8]},{"title":"Dust scaling: Total = Base x (1 + sqrt(Dust/Base)) above parity","columns":["Resource value","Dust","Shipment value"],"rows":[["1,000","4,000","3,000"],["1,000","9,000","4,000"],["241k","241k","482k"]],"cite":[8,11]},{"title":"Key numbers","columns":["Item","Value"],"rows":[["Min / max shipment value","50,000 / 50,000,000"],["Quota reroll","15,000 Gold"],["Pirate ransom","50,000 Gold"],["Quota completion bonus","+20% to +100% value + extra item"],["Bar weight","5x ore toward quota, ~4x toward value"],["Return cap","800 currency items (500 if one resource type)"],["Recruit reroll","4,000 Gold (high quality 16,000)"]],"cite":[8,0,6,10,23,12]}],"quickCard":["Smelt ore into bars before shipping","Dust up to about your bar value, no more","Ship only to ports showing 0% risk","Reroll quota (15k Gold) to match your ore","Crops alone; the port picks the gear type","Verisium last; stop charging at ~60-70%"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Patch Notes - Content Update 3.28.0 - Path of Exile: Mirage","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-02-27 (updates to 2026-03-06)","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-28-mirage-patch-notes","title":"3.28 Mirage Patch Notes for Path of Exile","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown (assets dated 2026-07)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/settlers","title":"Settlers League Start Strategy (Settlers Ore Farming)","publisher":"Maxroll (Milkybk_, reviewed by IBoilerUp)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/kalguuran-map-farming","title":"Kalguuran Map Farming","publisher":"Maxroll (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-03","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-09-19","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe-vault.com/guides/settlers-of-kalguur-league-mechanic-guide-shipping","title":"Settlers of Kalguur League Mechanic Guide: Shipping","publisher":"poe-vault (PatrickHatTrick)","date":"2026-03-06","patch":"3.25 title, with 3.28 changes section"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Settlers_league","title":"Settlers league","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"current data (3.28+ patch-note lines)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Kingsmarch","title":"Kingsmarch","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"current data"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Refiners_Bargain","title":"Refiner's Bargain","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"current data"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4440--poe-328-kingsmarch-guide-shipping-cheat-sheet-kalguur-atlas--mapping","title":"PoE 3.28 Kingsmarch Guide (Shipping Cheat Sheet, Kalguur Atlas & Mapping)","publisher":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"2026-03-10","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://www.aoeah.com/news/4707--poe-329-kingsmarch-shipping-cheat-sheet-atlas-scarabs--plan-strat","title":"PoE 3.29 Kingsmarch Shipping Cheat Sheet, Atlas, Scarabs & Plan Strat","publisher":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.iggm.com/news/poe-3-28-kingsmarch-ore-crops-bounty-changes-farming-strategies","title":"PoE 3.28 Kingsmarch Ore, Crops, Bounty Changes & Farming Strategies","publisher":"IGGM (currency seller)","date":"2026-03-13 (modified 2026-06-25)","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-28-kingsmarch-guide-how-to-farm-ore-and-maximize-profit.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.28 Kingsmarch Guide: How to Farm Ore and Maximize Profit","publisher":"MMOexp (currency seller)","date":"2026-04-16","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://wowcarry.com/blog/path-of-exile/poe-328-ore-kingsmarch-farming-detailed-atlas-strategy-guide","title":"PoE 3.28 Kingsmarch Ore Farming Guide - Mirage League","publisher":"WowCarry (John Langan; boosting seller)","date":"2026-05-18","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-gold-farming-guide-kingsmarch","title":"PoE 3.29 Gold Farming Guide (Kingsmarch & Kalguur Ore)","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (boosting seller)","date":"2026-08-20","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.ssegold.com/poe-3-28-kingsmarch-guide","title":"PoE 3.28 Kingsmarch Guide","publisher":"SSEGold (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0 - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown (mirrors March 2026 notes)","patch":"3.28.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 — Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991672","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0 - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0 - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.27.0"},{"url":"https://www.ssegold.com/poe-3-26-kingsmarch-guide-resource-management","title":"PoE 3.26 Kingsmarch Guide","publisher":"SSEGold (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://www.elyxir.gg/guide/path-of-exile/poe-1-328-kingsmarch-ore-shipment-farming-fast-maps-dust-setup-and-reliable-shipment-routes","title":"PoE 1 3.28 Kingsmarch Ore Shipment Farming","publisher":"Elyxir.gg","date":"2026-03-31","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3918725","title":"Kingsmarch mirror shards nerfed. (Feedback and Suggestions)","publisher":"Official PoE forum (player posts)","date":"2026-03-12","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392/page/29","title":"3.28.0 patch notes thread, comment page 29","publisher":"Official PoE forum (player posts)","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28 (pre-launch reaction)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Settlers_of_Kalguur","title":"Settlers of Kalguur (Atlas mastery) - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Lost_in_Transit","title":"Lost in Transit - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Crimson_Infusion","title":"Crimson Infusion - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current game data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Runegraft","title":"Runegraft - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Tattoo","title":"Tattoo - PoEDB","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3921511","title":"3.28.0c Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-03-18","patch":"3.28.0c"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3924293","title":"3.28.0e Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-03-26","patch":"3.28.0e"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3974219","title":"3.28.0j Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-06-24","patch":"3.28.0j"}]},"vendor":{"title":"Vendor recipes","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Vendor recipes turn items you sell to an NPC into currency or useful gear. The Chaos/Regal full-set recipe, 6-socket and 6-link sales, quality recipes and leveling recipes all still work in 3.29. White sockets in 3.29 made the RGB-to-Chromatic recipe worth picking up again. Most guides use recipes for a league's first 10-20 Chaos, in SSF, or for junk you already pick up. They are not treated as a farming strategy.","howTo":[{"text":"A recipe set is one two-hander (or two one-handers), plus body armour, helmet, gloves, boots, belt, amulet and two rings. Every piece must be rare. Normal, magic and unique items do not count, and sockets do not matter.","stage":["all"],"cite":[4,9,18]},{"text":"The lowest item level in the set decides the payout, not your character level. 1-59 pays Orb of Chance, 60-74 pays Chaos and 75+ pays Regal.","stage":["all"],"cite":[4,9,11]},{"text":"Chaos set (60-74): 1 Chaos if identified, 2 if every piece is unidentified, 3 if every piece is unidentified and at 20% quality. PoEDB also lists 2 for a set that is all 20% quality.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[4,11]},{"text":"Regal set (75+): 1 Regal, 2 if all unidentified or (per PoEDB) all 20% quality, 3 if both.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[9,11,21]},{"text":"Chance set (lowest ilvl 1-59, PoEDB): 1 Orb of Chance, 2 if all unidentified or all 20% quality, 3 if both.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[11,20]},{"text":"Full set where every item shares the same influence: 1 Exalted Orb, or 2 if every item is unidentified (since 3.28). PoEDB gives no item-level condition for this set.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[0,13,11]},{"text":"Use a loot filter that shows ilvl 60-74 rares in every slot, because many default filters hide them. Rings and amulets are usually the slots you run short of.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[4,18]},{"text":"Keep three stash tabs split by item size, and never identify recipe gear.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[4]},{"text":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer (community tool): logs in with OAuth (no POESESSID) and reads your stash from the PoE servers, refreshing each time you change zone. It can read guild tabs, shows which slots you still need for chaos, regal, chance or exalted sets, and highlights the pick order. It can only edit an offline loot filter.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[12,25,24]},{"text":"6-socket item, any rarity or quality: sells for 7 Jeweller's Orbs. Only body armours and two-handed weapons can have six sockets.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,5,11,9]},{"text":"6-linked item: sells for 20 Orbs of Fusing. This replaces the 6-socket payout, so you never get both.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3,5,9]},{"text":"Item with linked red, green and blue sockets: sells for 1 Chromatic Orb. The recipe is unchanged in 3.29.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[6,9,11]},{"text":"Quality recipes: items of one category whose quality totals at least 40% sell for one quality currency. Gems give a Gemcutter's Prism, flasks or tinctures a Glassblower's Bauble, weapons a Blacksmith's Whetstone, armour an Armourer's Scrap.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7,9,11]},{"text":"Movement speed: normal boots + any Quicksilver Flask + Orb of Augmentation gives magic boots with 10% movement speed. Repeating it raises the tier, up to 30%.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3,9]},{"text":"Chaos resistance: any ring or amulet + any Amethyst Flask + Orb of Augmentation. Repeating it raises the tier, up to tier 2.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Physical damage weapon: a weapon (guides use a normal Corroded Blade) + Rustic Sash + Blacksmith's Whetstone. A magic sash gives Heavy (40-49%), a rare sash Serrated (50-64%). Use a Chain Belt instead for the caster version.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3,9]},{"text":"+1 spell weapon: a white wand, sceptre, staff or rune dagger + gems of one spell tag whose quality totals 40%. It gives a magic weapon with +1 to that tag's gems.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[11,9,3]},{"text":"+1 minion helmet: magic helmet + Greater Life Flask 'of Animation' + Orb of Alteration. Get the Animation flask by selling a Bone Spirit Shield + a Greater Life Flask.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Base swaps: Iron Ring + Heavy Strike gives a Ruby Ring, + Fireball a Sapphire Ring, + Splitting Steel a Topaz Ring. Any amulet + all three gems gives an Onyx Amulet. Each result is a new normal-rarity base.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Flasks: three life or mana flasks of the same base give one of the next tier. Ruby + Sapphire + Topaz 'of Iron Skin' give a Granite Flask, and the same three 'of Reflexes' give a Jade Flask.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3,9,11]},{"text":"1 Divine Orb + any 5 flasks sell for 5 Divine Vessels.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[3,11]},{"text":"7 Vaal skill gems + any Sacrifice fragment sell for a Vaal Orb.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3,11]},{"text":"Orb of Alchemy: 3 identified rares with the same name, or 2 if both are 20% quality. Straight Flush (one normal, one magic and one rare, all at 20% quality) also pays an Alchemy.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"X of a Kind (PoEDB): 3 identified same-name rares, all at 20% quality, sell for a Regal Orb.","stage":["ssf"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"Orb of Chance: 2 identified same-name rares give 1 (PoEDB). A pair of mirrored items with the same name gives 1, and they need not be identical. One normal, one magic, one rare and one unique of the same base give 5.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[20,3]},{"text":"5 unidentified rare (or magic) items of the same base give 1 unidentified item of that base. It takes the lowest item level of the inputs and drops any influence.","stage":["mid","ssf"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"A Harbinger unique sells for a Fracturing Shard. Harbinger item pieces and The Beachhead do not count.","stage":["late"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"Maxroll's March 2026 page lists Orbs of Fusing for sale from a vendor at 4 Jeweller's each.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[3]}],"dangers":[{"text":"The unidentified bonus is all-or-nothing. One identified piece drops a Chaos set back to 1 Chaos.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[4]},{"text":"One piece below item level 60 turns the whole set into an Orb of Chance payout.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[11,4,9]},{"text":"Price-check a 6-link before vendoring it. A good 6-linked base can sell for several Divine Orbs, far more than 20 Fusings.","stage":["all"],"cite":[5]},{"text":"Items below item level 50 cannot roll six sockets with Jeweller's, so they can never feed the 6-socket recipe.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[5]},{"text":"The mirrored-pair Orb of Chance recipe can destroy value. Strongboxes often drop mirrored 6-socket or 6-link items, so you might vendor the wrong one.","stage":["all"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Do not bench-craft RGB for the Chromatic recipe. The single-colour crafts are gone, and the new crafts cost 5, 20 or 75 Chromatics to return 1.","stage":["all"],"cite":[14,19]},{"text":"Quality is not totalled across the whole sale. Each 40% group must reach the threshold alone, and 39% pays nothing.","stage":["all"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Outdated: ExpCarry still shows the Gavel + map chisel recipe as current, but 3.28 removed all chisel recipes.","stage":["all"],"cite":[9,13]},{"text":"Outdated: PoEDB's recipe page still lists the same-influence set as paying Exalted Shards (2, or 4 unidentified). Since 3.28 it pays 1 Exalted, or 2 unidentified.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[11,13,0]},{"text":"Misleading: MMOSO says Chromatic vendor recipes were removed in 3.29. Only the vendor sale of Chromatics for Jeweller's was removed, and the RGB recipe still works.","stage":["all"],"cite":[19,14,6]},{"text":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer makes no Terms of Service claim. It only says it is not affiliated with or endorsed by GGG.","stage":["all"],"cite":[24,25]},{"text":"GGG policy: standalone tools are 'not encouraged' but allowed with a public OAuth client. Tools that touch the game or its files lead to termination, and a macro must be manual and perform only one action.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26]},{"text":"GGG says it cannot process new OAuth applications right now and can remove API access without notice, so recipe tools may stop working.","stage":["all"],"cite":[26]}],"sell":[{"text":"Day-one vendor targets: full rare sets (Chaos/Regal), 6-socket and 6-link items, and RGB-linked items. Check poe.ninja for live rates.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[8]},{"text":"Trade valuable 6-link bases instead of vendoring them, because they can be worth several Divines.","stage":["all"],"cite":[5]},{"text":"Stop skipping RGB-linked drops. Chromatics are rarer and no longer sold by vendors, so 1 Chromatic per item is worth it again.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Basic shard sales: normal item gives a Scroll Fragment, unidentified gives Transmutation Shards, magic a few Alteration Shards, rare several Alteration Shards. Rare rings and amulets, and uniques, also add an Alchemy Shard.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[3]},{"text":"Maxroll's Alch and Go sells drops in bulk on trade (essences, spare Alchemy, Vaal and Regal Orbs) instead of vendoring them.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[22]}],"strategies":[{"name":"League-start Chaos recipe","investment":"Low: three stash tabs split by item size and a loot filter that shows ilvl 60-74 rares. Chaos Recipe Enhancer is optional.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Set your filter to show ilvl 60-74 rares in every slot.","Pick up rares unidentified and sort them into three tabs by size.","Watch rings and amulets, which are the usual bottleneck.","Before selling, check every piece is 60+ and unidentified.","Sell the set to a vendor for 2 Chaos.","Stop after about 10-20 Chaos, once you can farm end-game content."],"cite":[4,18,12]},{"name":"Pick-up-anyway vendoring while mapping","investment":"None: only junk you already pick up.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Vendor convenient 6-socket items for 7 Jeweller's.","Price-check 6-links and vendor only unwanted ones for 20 Fusings.","Pick up RGB-linked items for 1 Chromatic each.","Group quality items so each category reaches 40% on its own.","Drop any recipe once sorting and pickup cost more than it pays."],"cite":[9,5,6,7]},{"name":"SSF recipe use","investment":"Stash space and a temporary filter section for recipe ingredients.","stage":["ssf"],"steps":["Keep Chaos/Regal sets going longer, because you cannot buy currency from players.","Keep quality-currency recipes going and save low-value quality gems and flasks for crafting.","Add a temporary loot filter section for recipe ingredients.","Use leveling recipes (movement speed, +1 weapons, flask tiers) while you level."],"cite":[9,11,3]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough: 1-3 Chaos per set. Recommended for the first 10-20 Chaos only, with no per-hour figure given.","who":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo)","date":"2026-08-18","cite":[4]},{"text":"Rough: raising pieces to 20% quality for the 3-Chaos payout costs Scraps and Whetstones and is usually not worth it.","who":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo)","date":"2026-08-18","cite":[4]},{"text":"Rough: one already-20% gem for a Prism is close to break-even. Quality recipes are free income from junk, not a farm.","who":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo)","date":"2026-09-16","cite":[7]},{"text":"Rough: a good 6-link base can sell for several Divines, compared with 20 Fusings from the vendor.","who":"Timesaver.gg","date":"2026-08-26 (updated 2026-09-09)","cite":[5]},{"text":"Rough, for comparison: Maxroll's 3.29 Alch and Go league start uses no vendor recipes, rates profitability 'Low' and gives no per-hour figure.","who":"Maxroll (Zen_M)","date":"2026-07-24","cite":[22]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29","text":"Sockets are white by default, so naturally RGB-linked items are much rarer. The RGB recipe triggers less often, but each Chromatic is worth more.","cite":[2,6,14]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Vendors no longer sell Chromatics for Jeweller's Orbs, and Chromatics were made rarer.","cite":[2,10,9]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Chromatic supply shifted. The Bestiary 8-Chromatic craft now makes a Rare four-linked helmet, Heist trinket mods were changed, and Currency Exchange gold fees for Chromatics rose.","cite":[2,10,14]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Colour-specific bench crafts were replaced with 'at least 2, 3 or 4 non-white sockets' for 5, 20 or 75 Chromatics.","cite":[2,6]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Jeweller's, Tainted Jeweller's, Binding and bench socket crafts add white sockets. The 6-socket and 6-link recipes are unchanged.","cite":[2,6,14,5]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"The Chaos/Regal set recipe is unaffected, because it ignores sockets, links and colours. The four quality recipes are also unchanged.","cite":[4,7,14]},{"patch":"3.29.0b","text":"No vendor, recipe, shard or socket changes.","cite":[23]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"All vendor recipes that made Cartographer's Chisels were removed.","cite":[0,1,13]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Cartographer's Chisels can no longer be obtained, but existing ones work and always add +20% map quality. Map Device chisel crafts were removed.","cite":[0,13]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"On Standard, the chisel bonus was cut to +10% Item Quantity at 20% map quality (was +20%), and 20% map quality itself does less.","cite":[13]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The same-influence full set pays 1 Exalted Orb (was 2 Exalted Shards), or 2 Exalted if all unidentified.","cite":[0,13]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Most Currency Shard drops were removed, but the vendor recipes that pay shards are unchanged.","cite":[0,1]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"Harbinger was removed as a core league. Ancient, Binding, Engineer's, Harbinger's and Horizon Shards and the matching orbs can no longer be obtained, and existing shards were deleted, so no recipe pays them.","cite":[0]},{"patch":"3.28","text":"The notes say one new vendor recipe was added (listed twice) but never say what it is.","cite":[0,13]},{"patch":"3.26.0 / 3.27.0 / 3.29.1","text":"No vendor-recipe changes were found in the readable parts of these notes.","cite":[16,17,15]},{"patch":"3.19","text":"The 6-link vendor reward became 20 Fusings. The old Divine Orb payout is gone.","cite":[3,5,9]}],"tables":[{"title":"Full set rewards (lowest item level decides)","columns":["Set","Lowest ilvl","Identified","All unID (or all 20% qual, PoEDB)","All unID + all 20% qual"],"rows":[["Orb of Chance","1-59","1 Chance","2 Chance","3 Chance"],["Chaos","60-74","1 Chaos","2 Chaos","3 Chaos"],["Regal","75+","1 Regal","2 Regal","3 Regal"],["Same influence (since 3.28)","no condition listed","1 Exalted","2 Exalted (unID)","not stated"]],"cite":[4,11,20,21,9,0,13]},{"title":"Socket and link recipes (3.29)","columns":["Sell","Get","Note"],"rows":[["Any 6-socket item","7 Jeweller's Orbs","Body armour or 2H only; ilvl 50+ to roll 6"],["Any 6-linked item","20 Orbs of Fusing","Replaces 6-socket payout; price-check first"],["Linked R-G-B sockets","1 Chromatic Orb","Rarer drops since white sockets"]],"cite":[3,5,6,9,11]},{"title":"Quality recipes (40% per group)","columns":["Items","Get"],"rows":[["Gems","Gemcutter's Prism"],["Flasks or tinctures","Glassblower's Bauble"],["Weapons","Blacksmith's Whetstone"],["Armour","Armourer's Scrap"]],"cite":[7,9,11]},{"title":"Leveling recipes","columns":["Sell","Get"],"rows":[["Normal boots + Quicksilver Flask + Augmentation","10% movement speed boots (repeat to 30%)"],["Ring/amulet + Amethyst Flask + Augmentation","Chaos resistance (repeat to tier 2)"],["Weapon + Rustic Sash + Whetstone","Phys weapon: magic sash 40-49%, rare sash 50-64%"],["Same with Chain Belt","Caster version"],["White wand/sceptre/staff/rune dagger + 40% quality gems of one tag","+1 to that tag's gems"],["Magic helmet + Greater Life Flask of Animation + Alteration","+1 minion gems"],["3 life or mana flasks, same base","Next-tier flask"],["Iron Ring + Heavy Strike / Fireball / Splitting Steel","Ruby / Sapphire / Topaz Ring"]],"cite":[3,9,11]},{"title":"Other currency recipes","columns":["Sell","Get","Source"],"rows":[["3 identified same-name rares (2 if both 20%)","Orb of Alchemy","PoEDB"],["Normal + magic + rare, all 20% quality","Orb of Alchemy","PoEDB"],["3 identified same-name rares, all 20%","Regal Orb","PoEDB"],["2 identified same-name rares","1 Orb of Chance","PoEDB"],["2 mirrored items, same name","1 Orb of Chance","Maxroll"],["Normal + magic + rare + unique, same base","5 Orbs of Chance","PoEDB"],["7 Vaal gems + Sacrifice fragment","Vaal Orb","Maxroll, PoEDB"],["Divine Orb + any 5 flasks","5 Divine Vessels","Maxroll, PoEDB"],["5 unID rare/magic, same base","1 unID item of that base","PoEDB"],["Harbinger unique","Fracturing Shard","PoEDB"]],"cite":[11,20,3]}],"quickCard":["Chaos set: all rare, lowest ilvl 60-74, all unID = 2c","One piece under ilvl 60 = Orb of Chance","6S = 7 Jewellers, 6L = 20 Fusings (price-check 6L)","Pick up RGB-linked items: 1 Chromatic","Quality: 40% per group, 39% pays nothing","Stop set recipe after first 10-20 Chaos"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3913392","title":"Patch Notes - Content Update 3.28.0 - Path of Exile: Mirage","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-02-27 (updates through 2026-03-06)","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-28-mirage-patch-notes","title":"3.28 Mirage Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll (Cptn Garbage, reviewed by Tenkiei)","date":"2026-02-27","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-patch-notes","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll (Cptn Garbage)","date":"2026-07-22","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/resources/vendor-recipes","title":"Important Vendor Recipes for Beginners","publisher":"Maxroll (terence_, reviewed by Facefoot)","date":"2026-03-20 (last updated; first published 2022-07-30)","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-chaos-recipe-guide-3-29","title":"PoE Chaos Recipe Guide (3.29): Item Levels, the Full Set & Whether It's Still Worth It","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo) - currency/boosting seller","date":"2026-08-18","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-6-link-6-socket-vendor-recipe-3-29","title":"PoE 6-Link / 6-Socket Vendor Recipe 3.29","publisher":"Timesaver.gg - currency/boosting seller","date":"2026-08-26 (updated 2026-09-09)","patch":"3.29 (3.29.3)"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-socket-colours-chromatic-orbs-rgb-recipe","title":"PoE 3.29 Socket Colours, Chromatic Orbs & RGB Recipe","publisher":"Timesaver.gg - currency/boosting seller","date":"2026-08-11 (updated 2026-09-09)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-quality-currency-vendor-recipes-3-29","title":"PoE Quality Currency Vendor Recipes 3.29","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo) - currency/boosting seller","date":"2026-09-16","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-30-league-start-currency-fast","title":"PoE 3.30 League Start Currency Fast","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo) - currency/boosting seller","date":"2026-10-15 (updated 2026-11-02)","patch":"3.29 mechanics, written for 3.30 launch"},{"url":"https://expcarry.com/poe-1-vendor-recipes-leveling-currency-league-start","title":"PoE 1 Vendor Recipes: Leveling, Currency & League Start","publisher":"ExpCarry Editorial Team - boosting seller","date":"2026-09-02 (last modified)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://expcarry.com/poe-3-29-socket-changes-white-colored-best-bases","title":"PoE 3.29 Socket Changes: White vs Colored, Best Bases","publisher":"ExpCarry Editorial Team - boosting seller","date":"2026-07-25","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Vendor_recipe_system","title":"Vendor recipe system","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (data partly pre-3.28)"},{"url":"https://github.com/ChaosRecipeEnhancer/EnhancePoEApp","title":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer (EnhancePoEApp)","publisher":"ChaosRecipeEnhancer (GitHub, community tool)","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.28.0","title":"Version 3.28.0 (Mirage) patch notes mirror","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.28"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0 (Curse of the Allflame) patch notes mirror","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.29.1","title":"Version 3.29.1 patch notes mirror","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.26.0","title":"Version 3.26.0 (Mercenaries of Trarthus) patch notes mirror","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Version_3.27.0","title":"Version 3.27.0 (Keepers of the Flame) patch notes mirror","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.27"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/how-to-chaos-recipe-guide","title":"How to Chaos Recipe guide","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2025-01-30 (last updated)","patch":"unknown (pre-3.26)"},{"url":"https://www.mmoso.com/news/poe-white-sockets-chromatic-crafting-bench","title":"PoE white sockets, Chromatic and crafting bench","publisher":"MMOSO (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Orb_of_Chance","title":"Orb of Chance","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Regal_Orb","title":"Regal Orb","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/currency/league-start-alch-and-go","title":"League Start Alch And Go Farming Strategy","publisher":"Maxroll (Zen_M, reviewed by Facefoot)","date":"2026-07-24","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3989412","title":"3.29.0b Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (official forum)","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29.0b"},{"url":"https://github.com/ChaosRecipeEnhancer/ChaosRecipeEnhancer","title":"ChaosRecipeEnhancer README","publisher":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer team (GitHub)","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://chaos-recipe.com","title":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer","publisher":"Chaos Recipe Enhancer Team","date":"2026 (copyright)","patch":"unknown"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/developer/docs","title":"Developer Docs (third-party policy)","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"unknown","patch":"not patch-specific"}]},"mercenaries":{"title":"Mercenaries of Trarthus (core since 3.29)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Mercenaries of Trarthus became core content in 3.29. From Act 3 onward you can wager gold to duel a Mercenary. If you win, you can take one of its items, take its Warrant, or keep it as a temporary ally. The mechanic now has its own Atlas passives and four Trarthan Scarabs, and Maxroll's 3.29 farming tier list rates Mercenary Rushing (Infamy + Renown scarabs, aiming for jackpot uniques) S tier.","howTo":[{"text":"Mercenaries can show up in any area from Act 3 onward. It is a chance, not a guarantee, except in a few special areas.","stage":["league-start","all"],"cite":[1,8,21,20]},{"text":"To fight one, wager gold for one of its items. If you lose the duel, the gold is gone and the Mercenary teleports away. If you win, it joins you as a temporary ally for a few areas and you keep the spoils.","stage":["all"],"cite":[21,1,8]},{"text":"Instead of the ally, a win can take one equipped or inventory item (gems excluded). Rematch makes it drop a Warrant that brings the same Mercenary into a later map. Each Mercenary gives a Warrant only once.","stage":["all"],"cite":[1,21,46]},{"text":"You can have only one temporary Mercenary at a time. In the campaign it fights for you for at most 3 areas, then leaves.","stage":["league-start","all"],"cite":[1,8,20]},{"text":"Four campaign areas always have a Mercenary: The Sceptre of God, The Grand Arena, The Ridge and The Hidden Underbelly. These carry no Rucksack items.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[11,21,20]},{"text":"Since 3.29.1 the Act 10 Control Blocks always has a Mercenary, even if you are over-levelled for the area.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[4,3,23]},{"text":"A hired Mercenary scales its passives and skills to the current area level, up to level 68. The item level it can equip stays capped at the level of the area where you found it.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[21,46]},{"text":"Gearing a Mercenary: cap its resistances at 75% and add armour, evasion, energy shield or block. Skip +maximum Life, since its base Life is already high.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Mercenary Rares beat typical ground drops, which makes them useful at league start. Their pockets usually hold currency and scarabs.","stage":["league-start","ssf","all"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"A Mercenary is not a party member in 3.29. It adds no monster life and no item quantity or rarity. Guides from 3.26 that say otherwise are out of date.","stage":["all"],"cite":[21,9,11,14]},{"text":"Only the Scion's Luminary ascendancy can hire permanently, through Noble Blood: up to 3 Mercenaries (1 active, 2 stored in town or the hideout). It can change their gear and still have one temporary Mercenary on top.","stage":["all"],"cite":[1,8,21,2]},{"text":"Luminary's Legendary nodes let the Mercenary equip uniques in weapon, shield, quiver, glove, helmet, boot, ring, amulet and belt slots. Legendary Arms adds damage for each unique it wears.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[37]},{"text":"When rushing, check each Mercenary's Rucksack and gear first. Kill it if it holds something valuable; otherwise hire it to help clear. Kill the Wild Mercenaries before the main one.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[16,17]},{"text":"Not farming Mercenaries? The Civil War in Trarthus notable removes them from your maps and stops Trarthan Scarab drops.","stage":["all"],"cite":[27]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Gold drain: the wager is not refunded if you lose, and resurrecting a dead Mercenary also costs gold.","stage":["league-start","ssf","all"],"cite":[8,1,21]},{"text":"Enemy Mercenary casters were the reported one-shots. 3.29.2 lowered Conflagration, Divine Ire, Flame Wall, Soulrend of Reaping, Storm Call and Infernal Blow, and cut Conflagration's debuff from 4s to 2s.","stage":["all"],"cite":[24,48,30]},{"text":"3.29.3 lowered enemy Frostbolt, Ice Nova (and Ice Nova of Projection), Flameblast, Fireball (and Fireball of Impact) and Rolling Magma. Allied versions were not changed.","stage":["all"],"cite":[25,12,49]},{"text":"Since 3.29.2, Infamy's Wild Mercenaries keep fighting after their leader dies. They can also attack players who did not join the duel, which matters in party rushing.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[24,48]},{"text":"Surprising Alliances makes each Wild Mercenary harder for every other Wild Mercenary in the area. Stacking it with Infamy or many Rogue Exiles adds a lot of risk.","stage":["late"],"cite":[21,7]},{"text":"Faith in Arms (30% aura effect + random Shrine buff) and Trarthan Vapours (30% cooldown recovery + Onslaught) make map Mercenaries stronger. That is a risk when you fight them.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[35]},{"text":"High Stakes doubles wager costs but gives back only 30% more gold on a win. It loses gold if you sometimes lose duels.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[27,35]},{"text":"The Valdo map mod that reduces damage for each equipped item also hits a Luminary's Mercenary and its minions.","stage":["late"],"cite":[20]},{"text":"Watch for outdated guides: 3.26 guides treat Mercenaries as party members, and pre-3.29.2 guides say killing the main Mercenary ends the fight.","stage":["all"],"cite":[21,24]},{"text":"Early-league reports of low Mercenary rates came from a bug, fixed in 3.29.0b, where Atlas extra-content passives did not apply to Mercenaries.","stage":["all"],"cite":[22]}],"sell":[{"text":"Warrants: trade them. A Warrant brings the same skills with new items, and each Mercenary gives a Warrant only once.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1,21,46,9]},{"text":"Mercenary skills cannot be changed, so value is in the fixed combo. Auras that also buff you (e.g. Determination) and Gilded Fortification for allies stand out. Mismatched supports make a brick.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[9,1]},{"text":"Sellable types per MMOExp: multi-aura, six-link, strong ranged (Ice Shot + Returning Projectiles, Ballista) and Kineticist/Manyshot/Combatant. Make a Warrant, price check it, then list it.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[17,19]},{"text":"Since 3.29.2, stash search can find the skill information on Warrants, so you can sort them by skill before pricing.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[24,48]},{"text":"Mercenary-only uniques (poe.ninja, 4 Nov): Hand of Heresy ~60c, Binds of Bloody Vengeance ~39c, Azadi Crest ~34c, The Ghastly Theatre ~18c, Howlcrack ~2c, Scornflux ~1c.","stage":["all"],"cite":[11,21,20,45]},{"text":"Trarthan gems no longer come from Heist Gem Chests. They are rare finds in a Mercenary's inventory.","stage":["all"],"cite":[11,21,1]},{"text":"Infamous Mercenaries come from one of four Trarthus families and always wear one Unique. They are the only source of Rares with Infamous modifiers.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Endgame Rucksacks can no longer roll Transmutation or Augmentation orbs, so the low-value filler is gone.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[21,11]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Basic Merc Rush (Infamy + Renown)","investment":"About 23 chaos in scarabs per map (poe.ninja, 4 Nov 2026), plus the map. Low to medium.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Atlas: take Mercenary spawn chance (Minor Fiefdoms +30%, small nodes +10% each), Loot and Pillage, unique chance, Infamous chance and the extra-item nodes.","Map device: Trarthan Scarab of Infamy + Trarthan Scarab of Renown (limit 1 each).","Infamy makes the Mercenary Infamous and adds two Wild Mercenaries. Renown makes all of their equipment Unique, which is the jackpot.","Pick fast maps with the boss near the start, such as City Square or Mesa. Aim for about two minutes per map.","Weaker character: white or alch-and-go maps. Strong character: 8-mod maps. The Mercenaries gain nothing from map mods.","Higher-tier maps raise the Infamous rate: from 3.29.1, about 1.5x in tier 1 up to about 2x in tier 16.","Check the Rucksack, kill the Wild Mercenaries first, then the main one. Leave."],"atlasPassives":["Minor Fiefdoms","Mercenary spawn chance small nodes (x8)","Loot and Pillage","Mercenary unique chance small nodes (x3)","Mercenary Infamous chance small nodes (x4)","Mercenary Additional Item Dropped (x2)","Contract Killers"],"scarabs":["Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","Trarthan Scarab of Renown"],"cite":[0,6,27,35,16,17,44,3,23]},{"name":"Rogue Exile Merc variant (Surprising Alliances)","investment":"About 89 chaos in scarabs per map (4 Nov 2026), mostly from Surprising Alliances. High investment and depends on the market. ExpCarry suggests a separate third Atlas tree.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Map device: Infamy + Renown + Trarthan Scarab of Surprising Alliances + 2 Anarchy Scarabs.","The two Anarchy Scarabs add 10 Rogue Exiles. Surprising Alliances gives each Wild Rogue Exile a 50% chance to bring a Wild Mercenary.","Atlas (POECurrency tree): Loot and Pillage, Ruckus and Exiled Will for Rogue Exiles, Contract Killers, plus Templar Astrolabe nodes.","Their easier tree reaches 90% Mercenary spawn chance, or 100% with two blocker nodes.","With a Templar Astrolabe, maps count only if you kill the boss, so skip Jungle Valley (its boss is far from the entrance) and use boss-near maps.","Difficulty rises with every extra Wild Mercenary. A seller guide calls this full-clear setup often not worth the risk for weaker builds."],"atlasPassives":["Loot and Pillage","Ruckus","Exiled Will","Contract Killers","Minor Fiefdoms","Templar Astrolabe nodes"],"scarabs":["Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","Trarthan Scarab of Renown","Trarthan Scarab of Surprising Alliances","Anarchy Scarab x2"],"cite":[0,15,16,13,7,33,36,44,17]},{"name":"Deli Merc Rush (seller guide)","investment":"Infamy (~12.2c) plus Delirium Scarab of Paranoia (~20.5c each, limit 5) on 8-mod maps (prices from 4 Nov 2026). High.","stage":["late"],"steps":["MMOExp pairs Trarthan Scarab of Infamy with Delirium Scarab of Paranoia on 8-mod maps.","Paranoia makes Delirium encounters in the map generate 2 extra reward types.","Their target pace is about 40 maps per hour.","Profit figures come from a currency seller and are not verified (see profit)."],"scarabs":["Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","Delirium Scarab of Paranoia"],"cite":[18,34,44]},{"name":"Campaign and league-start Mercenaries","investment":"Gold only.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Duel the guaranteed Mercenaries in The Sceptre of God, The Grand Arena, The Ridge, The Hidden Underbelly and the Act 10 Control Blocks. Expect no Rucksack loot from these.","Their Rares beat typical ground drops, so take items for your own gear.","Or hire one to help clear for up to 3 areas, with capped resistances and defences over Life.","Luminary: since 3.29.1, permanent Mercenaries have no damage penalty before level 45. The penalty grows to its full size at level 83.","Since 3.29.1, attack-based Mercenaries are relatively stronger than casters at lower levels."],"cite":[11,21,20,4,3,23,1]},{"name":"Self-found Trarthan Scarabs","investment":"None beyond normal mapping.","stage":["ssf","mid"],"steps":["Betrayal: Vagan's Transportation safehouse reward is now a chest of Trarthan Scarabs.","Searing Exarch altar options can drop Mercenary scarabs.","Minor Fiefdoms makes map scarab drops 30% more likely to be Trarthan Scarabs.","The small spawn chance nodes also raise the chance of Trarthan Scarab drops."],"atlasPassives":["Minor Fiefdoms","Mercenary spawn chance small nodes"],"scarabs":["Trarthan Scarab","Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","Trarthan Scarab of Renown"],"cite":[21,46,35,27]},{"name":"Targeting a Mercenary type or Warrant","investment":"Atlas points only.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Azadi, Cyaxan and Keitan Supremacy notables give +100% chance for that house.","The 75%-less Strength, Dexterity or Intelligence alignment notables remove unwanted types.","Use these to steer spawns toward an archetype you want to keep, or to Warrant and sell."],"atlasPassives":["Azadi Supremacy","Cyaxan Supremacy","Keitan Supremacy","75% less Str/Dex/Int alignment notables"],"cite":[27,2]}],"profit":[{"text":"Rough: 15-20 div/hr for fast players (8-10 for slower) from basic merc rushing, not counting jackpots. 5-10 div per sold Mercenary, 25+ for premium ones. Unsourced seller claim.","who":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-10","cite":[17]},{"text":"Rough: 'Deli Merc Rush' (Infamy + Paranoia on 8-mod maps, ~40 maps/hr) claimed 35-40 div/hr after costs. Unsourced seller claim.","who":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-17","cite":[18]},{"text":"Rough: recommends City Square with Renown + Infamy (rush the boss, kill the Mercenary, leave) for weaker builds. Profit figures unverified.","who":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-10","cite":[17]},{"text":"Rough: each Trarthan scarab cost about 15-35 chaos at the time.","who":"POECurrency (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-29","cite":[15]},{"text":"Scarab prices: Surprising Alliances ~61c, Infamy ~12.2c, Renown ~10.6c, base Trarthan ~3.4c, Anarchy ~2.4c, Paranoia ~20.5c. Divine Orb ~412c.","who":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[44]},{"text":"Derived scarab cost per map: basic rush (Infamy + Renown) ~23c; Rogue Exile variant (+ Surprising Alliances + 2 Anarchy) ~89c.","who":"poe.ninja (derived)","date":"2026-11-04","cite":[44]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Further damage cuts to enemy Mercenary Frostbolt, Ice Nova, Flameblast, Fireball and Rolling Magma.","cite":[25,12,49]},{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Closed the exploit where Infamy Wild Mercenaries dropped loot without being killed.","cite":[25,49,12]},{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Fixed a bug that blocked hiring a third permanent Mercenary.","cite":[25,49]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Lowered damage on several enemy Mercenary skills and shortened Conflagration's debuff from 4s to 2s.","cite":[24,48]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Infamy Wild Mercenaries keep fighting after their leader dies and can target players outside the duel.","cite":[24,48]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Deep Altar currency conversion blessings now apply to Mercenaries. Stash search now reads Warrant skills.","cite":[24,48]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Act 10 Control Blocks always has a Mercenary, even if you are over-levelled.","cite":[4,3,23]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"The permanent Mercenary damage penalty now phases in: none before level 45, full at level 83. This followed GGG's 27 July note that permanent hires were too weak for their cost.","cite":[4,3,5,26]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Attack Mercenaries became relatively stronger than casters at lower levels, and map Mercenary skills got slightly more supports on average.","cite":[3,23,47]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Infamous Mercenaries became 50% more common in tier 1 maps, scaling to about 2x in tier 16.","cite":[4,3,23,9]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Added the Contract Killers notable: allied Mercenaries deal 100% more damage to Mercenaries and Rogue Exiles.","cite":[4,3,27,10]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Revived permanent Mercenaries can rejoin an area they retreated from. In maps, that only works when you re-enter through a Map Device portal. Maxroll's 'can now be respawned' summary overstates this.","cite":[4,3,23]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Permanent Mercenaries now get the Golden Lantern quantity and rarity buffs in Charts and Voyages.","cite":[4,3]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Fixed rematch requests failing for level 68 Mercenaries.","cite":[47]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Mercenaries became core, with their own Atlas passives and Trarthan Scarabs.","cite":[2,13,21,20]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"A Mercenary no longer counts as a party member, so it adds no monster life and no item quantity or rarity. In 3.26 it counted as half a player.","cite":[21,9,11,14]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Temporary Mercenaries leave after a set number of areas. Only Luminary can hire permanently.","cite":[2,8]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Hired Mercenaries scale passives and skills to the area level, capped at 68.","cite":[46,21]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Six uniques are Mercenary-only again. Trarthan gems are Mercenary-only again. Endgame Rucksacks lost Transmutation and Augmentation orbs.","cite":[21,20,11]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Vagan's Transportation safehouse reward is now a Trarthan Scarab chest, and Searing Exarch altars can drop Mercenary scarabs.","cite":[21,46]},{"patch":"3.29.0b","text":"Fixed Atlas extra-content passives not applying to Mercenaries.","cite":[22]}],"tables":[{"title":"Trarthan Scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Effect","Drop level","Limit","poe.ninja 4 Nov"],"rows":[["Trarthan Scarab","Map area has a Mercenary","68","1","~3.4c"],["Scarab of Infamy","Mercenaries are Infamous + 2 Wild Mercenaries","73","1","~12.2c"],["Scarab of Renown","All Mercenary equipment is Unique","78","1","~10.6c"],["Scarab of Surprising Alliances","Wild Rogue Exiles: 50% Wild Mercenary escort; harder per Wild Mercenary","73","1","~61c"]],"cite":[6,7,28,29,31,32,21,44]},{"title":"Companion scarabs","columns":["Scarab","Effect","Drop level","Limit","poe.ninja 4 Nov"],"rows":[["Anarchy Scarab","+5 Rogue Exiles","68","5","~2.4c"],["Anarchy of Partnership","Wild Rogue Exiles 50% in pairs","not listed","1","not listed"],["Anarchy of Gigantification","30% chance to replace with a Rogue Giant","not listed","2","not listed"],["Anarchy (Exceptional)","Adds an Exceptional Rogue Exile","not listed","2","not listed"],["Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","Delirium gives 2 extra reward types","73","5","~20.5c"]],"cite":[33,34,44]},{"title":"Mercenary Atlas passives","columns":["Node","Effect","Use"],"rows":[["Minor Fiefdoms","+30% map Mercenary chance; scarabs 30% more likely Trarthan","Farm"],["Spawn chance small (x8)","+10% map Mercenary chance each","Farm"],["Loot and Pillage","10% chance a defeated map Mercenary drops all items; always full Rucksacks","Farm (core)"],["Unique chance small (x3)","15% higher chance worn items are Unique","Farm"],["Infamous chance small (x4)","10% higher Infamous chance","Farm"],["Additional Item Dropped (x2)","Drops 1 untaken item on defeat","Farm"],["Extra support small (x2)","20% chance for an extra support on their skills","Warrants"],["Contract Killers (3.29.1)","Allied Mercenaries 100% more damage vs Mercenaries and Rogue Exiles","Farm"],["High Stakes","Wagers cost 100% more gold, 30% more gold back on a win","Risky"],["Faith in Arms","30% aura effect + random Shrine buff for map Mercenaries","Makes them harder"],["Trarthan Vapours","30% cooldown recovery + Onslaught for map Mercenaries","Makes them harder"],["Azadi / Cyaxan / Keitan Supremacy","+100% chance of that house","Targeting"],["Str / Dex / Int alignment","75% less chance of that alignment","Targeting"],["Civil War in Trarthus","No Mercenaries, no Trarthan Scarab drops","Turn off"]],"cite":[27,35,4,3]},{"title":"Mercenary-only uniques","columns":["Unique","Base (req)","Key effect","poe.ninja 4 Nov"],"rows":[["Hand of Heresy","Martyr Gloves (78)","Excommunicate on melee hit; 15% aura area","~60c"],["Binds of Bloody Vengeance","Vanguard Belt (78)","After taking a crit, next attack's hits within 4s all crit","~39c"],["Azadi Crest","Lacquered Buckler (60)","Lucky/Unlucky use three rolls","~34c"],["The Ghastly Theatre","Teak Round Shield (58)","Triggers level 20 Physical Aegis; +2 socketed supports","~18c"],["Howlcrack","Ezomyte Burgonet (60)","Non-instant warcries ignore cooldown; cost +15% life","~2c"],["Scornflux","Satin Slippers (54)","Arcane Surge on movement skill; its cast speed also applies to move speed","~1c"]],"cite":[38,39,40,41,42,43,45,21,11]},{"title":"Mercenary tier list (Timesaver, 3.29)","columns":["Tier","Type"],"rows":[["S","Aura carriers and fortify/support"],["A","Attack DPS (above casters after 3.29.1)"],["B","Casters"]],"cite":[9]}],"quickCard":["Act 3+: duel mercs for gear; lost wager = gold gone","Rush: Infamy + Renown, boss-near map, ~2 min","Check Rucksack: valuables = kill, else hire","Kill Wild Mercs first; they fight on alone","Good skill combo? Take the Warrant, sell it","Not farming? Spec Civil War in Trarthus"],"readMore":[{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/tierlists/endgame-farming-tier-list","title":"Endgame Farming Tier List","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"Last updated 2026-09-19 (changelog entry 2026-08-11)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/resources/mercenaries-of-trarthus-guide","title":"Mercenaries Of Trarthus Guide (Zen_M)","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-08-01 (updated for 3.29 on 2026-07-17)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-reveal-summary","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Reveal Summary","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29 (pre-launch reveal)"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-1-patch-notes","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll.gg","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991633","title":"Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes 3.29.1 Preview","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (forum, Natalia_GGG)","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3989358/page/1","title":"Curse of the Allflame launch feedback / improvements announcement","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games (forum, Community Team)","date":"2026-07-27","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Trarthan_Scarab","title":"Trarthan Scarab","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Trarthan_Scarab_of_Surprising_Alliances","title":"Trarthan Scarab of Surprising Alliances","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29 (current data)"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-3-29-mercenaries-guide-hire-warrants-luminary","title":"PoE Mercenaries Explained (3.29): How to Hire, Gear & Keep Them","publisher":"Timesaver.gg (Sam Okonkwo)","date":"2026-08-07 (updated 2026-08-21)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-mercenaries-tier-list-3-29","title":"PoE Mercenaries Tier List 3.29","publisher":"Timesaver.gg","date":"2026-09-22","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://timesaver.gg/blog/poe-atlas-passive-tree-guide-3-29","title":"PoE Atlas Passive Tree Guide (3.29)","publisher":"Timesaver.gg","date":"2026-09-20","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://overgear.com/guides/poe/mercenaries-of-trarthus/","title":"PoE Mercenaries of Trarthus - Pro Tips","publisher":"Overgear","date":"2026-07-20","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://allthings.how/cursed-ducats-and-mercenary-nerfs-in-path-of-exile-3-29-3/","title":"Cursed Ducats and Mercenary nerfs in Path of Exile 3.29.3","publisher":"allthings.how","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://expcarry.com/poe-1-atlas-farming-strategies-mechanics-scarabs-maps-budget","title":"PoE 1 Atlas Farming Strategies: Best Mechanics, Scarabs and Maps by Budget","publisher":"ExpCarry","date":"2026-09-01","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://www.poe-vault.com/guides/mercenaries-of-trarthus-league-mechanic-info","title":"Mercenaries of Trarthus League Mechanic Guide (PoE Secrets of the Atlas 3.26)","publisher":"PoE Vault (PatrickHatTrick)","date":"2025-06-18","patch":"3.26"},{"url":"https://www.poecurrency.com/news/poe-3-29-rogue-exiles-mercenaries-farming-strategy-15-divines-per-hour-mageblood-drops","title":"PoE 3.29 Rogue Exiles & Mercenaries Farming Strategy","publisher":"POECurrency.com (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-29","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.iggm.com/news/poe-3-29-rogue-exiles-farming-trarthan-scarabs-turn-mercenaries-to-mageblood","title":"PoE 3.29 Rogue Exiles Farming Guide: How Trarthan Scarabs Turn Mercenaries into a New Path to Mageblood?","publisher":"IGGM (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-29","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-29-mercenary-farming-guide-best-boss-rush-strategy-for-fast-currency.html","title":"Path of Exile 3.29 Mercenary Farming Guide: Best Boss Rush Strategy for Fast Currency","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller, Marta Kowalska)","date":"2026-08-10","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-deli-merc-rush-guide-35-40-divines-per-hour-max-profit-farm.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Deli Merc Rush Guide: 35-40 Divines Per Hour","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-17","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/poe-3-29-mercenary-farming-guide-best-strategy-to-find-valuable-mercenaries.html","title":"PoE 3.29 Mercenary Farming Guide: Best Strategy to Find Valuable Mercenaries","publisher":"MMOExp (currency seller, Amelie Laurent)","date":"2026-08-30","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Version_3.29.0","title":"Version 3.29.0","publisher":"poedb.tw (mirror of GGG patch notes)","date":"unknown (news images dated 2026-07-14/17)","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/3-29-curse-of-the-allflame-patch-notes","title":"3.29 Curse of the Allflame Patch Notes","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-22","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Version_3.29.0b","title":"Version 3.29.0b","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.0b"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Version_3.29.1","title":"Version 3.29.1","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Version_3.29.2","title":"Version 3.29.2","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Version_3.29.3","title":"Version 3.29.3","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29.3"},{"url":"https://maxroll.gg/poe/news/upcoming-changes-and-farming-strategies-in-3-29","title":"Upcoming Changes and Farming Strategies in 3.29","publisher":"Maxroll","date":"2026-07-29","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Atlas_passive_skill","title":"Atlas passive skill list","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current client data, assumed 3.29)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Trarthan_Scarab_of_Infamy","title":"Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current client data)"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/Trarthan_Scarab_of_Renown","title":"Trarthan Scarab of Renown","publisher":"poedb.tw","date":"unknown","patch":"unknown (current client data)"},{"url":"https://www.mmoexp.com/News/path-of-exile-3-30-endgame-changes-explained-mercenaries-loot-ghost-flame-crafting-and-more-from-the-allflame-podcast.html","title":"PoE 3.30 endgame changes explained (Allflame podcast summary)","publisher":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29/3.30"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Trarthan_Scarab_of_Renown","title":"Trarthan Scarab of Renown","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Trarthan_Scarab_of_Infamy","title":"Trarthan Scarab of Infamy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Anarchy_Scarab","title":"Anarchy Scarab","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Delirium_Scarab_of_Paranoia","title":"Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Mercenaries","title":"Mercenaries (uniques, Atlas tree modifiers)","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Templar_Astrolabe","title":"Templar Astrolabe","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Luminary","title":"Luminary","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Azadi_Crest","title":"Azadi Crest","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Binds_of_Bloody_Vengeance","title":"Binds of Bloody Vengeance","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Hand_of_Heresy","title":"Hand of Heresy","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Howlcrack","title":"Howlcrack","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/Scornflux","title":"Scornflux","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poedb.tw/us/The_Ghastly_Theatre","title":"The Ghastly Theatre","publisher":"PoEDB","date":"unknown","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/economy/allflame/scarabs","title":"Allflame scarab prices (exchange overview API)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 (fetched)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://poe.ninja/economy/allflame/unique-armours","title":"Allflame unique armour prices (stash overview API)","publisher":"poe.ninja","date":"2026-11-04 (fetched)","patch":"3.29"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3985332","title":"Content Update 3.29.0 - Path of Exile: Curse of the Allflame","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-07-17","patch":"3.29.0"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3991672","title":"3.29.1 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-07-31","patch":"3.29.1"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3994431","title":"3.29.2 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-08-06","patch":"3.29.2"},{"url":"https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3996516","title":"3.29.3 Patch Notes","publisher":"Grinding Gear Games","date":"2026-08-13","patch":"3.29.3"}]},"atlas":{"title":"Atlas farming strategies (3.29 tier list)","asOf":"3.29","summary":"Your Atlas tree, scarabs and map choice decide what your maps drop. In 3.29 Maxroll puts eight farms in S tier: Ethereal Scarabs, Nightmare Boss Rush, Inscribed Ultimatum, Harvest, Unstable Breach, Divination Cards, Mercenary Rushing and Curse of the Allflame (Charts and Voyages). There is no single best farm. Choose one that suits your build and budget, and treat every profit figure as a snapshot that changes with the market.","howTo":[{"text":"League start: run Alch & Go. Get to yellow maps quickly, because they drop Shrieking Essences (white maps only go up to Screaming).","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Alch & Go: run any map and skip mods your build can't handle. Transmute, alch or vaal maps you still need for completion bonuses, and sell most of your drops.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"A zero-cost alternative is Destructive Play. Run T16 Silo, kill only the extra Destructive Play bosses and leave the main boss alive.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[9,32]},{"text":"For SSF or a slow start, pohx's League Start Harvest works on Mesa or City Square and needs no scarabs.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"cite":[11]},{"text":"Finish your Voidstones early. Income after the first two is said to dwarf what you make before them.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[6]},{"text":"Each Voidstone adds 0.4% for a T16 map to become a Nightmare map. Nightmare completions give 5 of the 138 atlas points.","stage":["all"],"cite":[15]},{"text":"Atlas Anomalies (Nameless Seer, Reflecting Mists) can appear after Voidstone maps. They cost no map, ignore your tree and fragments, and you can run them any time.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[22]},{"text":"Once you have your first divines, move to Harvest, Corrupted Essences, 8-mod map selling or Nightmare Boss Rush.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[32]},{"text":"Pick a farm that matches your build. Boss rushes need strong single-target damage, and juiced maps need survivability.","stage":["all"],"cite":[10,1,50]},{"text":"8-mod Originator maps: run them yourself if they have 100%+ More Maps, otherwise sell them. Price them from 1 div and lower the price every couple of hours.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[8]}],"dangers":[{"text":"Ethereal: avoid three dangerous scarab-quantity mods. Rares with volatile cores. Monster damage that can ignite, freeze or shock (carry a freeze-immunity flask). Players have less defences, which is deadly for ES and evasion builds.","stage":["late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Ethereal: your build must kill the boss fast, or you lose much of the currency.","stage":["late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Ethereal needs a big bankroll. Farm of Exile says it pays off only over 50+ maps, with a couple of hundred divines of buffer.","stage":["late"],"cite":[33,0]},{"text":"Ultimatum: avoid Stalking Ruin, Sawblades, Reduced Recovery, Blood Altar, Less Cooldown Recovery, Treacherous Auras and Drought.","stage":["late"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Ultimatum: you will fail some encounters. Walk away with the loot you have already earned.","stage":["late"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Harvest: avoid chaos damage-over-time map mods and altar mods that add a lot of chaos damage to minions.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[34]},{"text":"Harvest T4 bosses have an uninterruptible phasing animation. Walk out of the thorn ring.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[34]},{"text":"Reflect was reworked in red maps. Rares now get Physical Thorns (800) or Elemental Thorns (1500).","stage":["all"],"cite":[22]},{"text":"The Valdo map modifier now also applies to a Luminary's Mercenary.","stage":["all"],"cite":[22]},{"text":"Voyages: after the 7th lantern, return to the Bathysphere or you drown and lose your loot.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[7]},{"text":"Boss rush needs high single-target damage. Ziggurat's boss has several invulnerability phases.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Mercenary rushing is gambling by the author's own admission (MMOEXP).","stage":["league-start","mid"],"cite":[21]},{"text":"Out-of-date guides: Betrayal and Catarina no longer drop Ethereal embers, Harvest Synthesise is gone, and many maps were removed.","stage":["all"],"cite":[22,27,11]},{"text":"Ignore Mirage-era (3.28) Breach profit figures, because 3.29 nerfed Breach density.","stage":["all"],"cite":[10,16]},{"text":"Maxroll's Stacked Deck page body is still the 3.28 version.","stage":["mid"],"cite":[5]}],"sell":[{"text":"Ethereal: top scarabs are Ambush Scarab of Containment, Ultimatum Scarab of Catalysing and Horned Scarab of Bloodlines. Vendor cheap scarabs 3-for-1.","stage":["late"],"cite":[0]},{"text":"Catalysing is valuable because Ultimatum is now the only source of Catalysts.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[22]},{"text":"Boss rush: sell Reality, Devouring, Blazing and Awakening fragments on the Currency Exchange.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[1]},{"text":"Ultimatum: five Inscribed Ultimatums with the same mod vendor for currency, with rewards up to a Mirror at 200%.","stage":["late"],"cite":[2]},{"text":"Harvest: sell lifeforce on the Currency Exchange. Sacred is about 137c and Sandswept about 699c. Vivid, Primal and Wild sell for under 1c (4 Nov).","stage":["mid"],"cite":[3,40]},{"text":"Unstable Breach: Divines, Valdo's Puzzle Box (about 287c, up 43% in a week), Chaos, Wombgifts and Hiveblood.","stage":["late"],"cite":[4,44]},{"text":"Destructive Play: sell Maven's Chisels, Shaped Astrolabes and influenced maps.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[9]},{"text":"8-mod Originator maps: list from 1 div and cut the price every couple of hours. Put Nightmare maps in a higher-priced tab.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[8]},{"text":"Reflecting Mist currency is about 4,308c (about 10 div). Mist objects now drop it more often.","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[40,22]},{"text":"Stacked Deck is about 8c. The Apothecary is about 15,132c and The Doctor about 361c (4 Nov).","stage":["mid","late"],"cite":[40,42]},{"text":"Alch & Go: sell most drops until your Voidstones are done.","stage":["league-start"],"cite":[6]}],"strategies":[{"name":"Ethereal Allflame Scarab Farm","investment":"High (Maxroll). Very hard and needs a lot of management. Three embers are about 1,577c (about 3.8 div) per map on 4 Nov 2026.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Run T16 Originator-influenced Crater, chosen for its very high monster density.","Roll maps for 80%+ more Scarabs before you apply the chisel.","Add a Maven's Chisel of Scarabs, 1-5 Blacksmith's Delirium Orbs and a Templar Astrolabe.","Use Eater of Worlds altars for quantity and scarab duplication.","Rush the boss first, then clear the map.","Expect at least 2-3 portal trips to pick up the loot.","Sell the top scarabs. Vendor cheap scarabs 3-for-1."],"atlasPassives":["Ultimatum cluster, taken only for better odds on Ultimatum scarab drops (mostly Catalysing). You don't run the encounters.","Complete the full Originator questline so Originator maps drop."],"scarabs":["3x Allflame Ember of the Ethereal (up to 4 allowed)","Horned Scarab of Bloodlines","Betrayal Scarab of the Allflame (limit 1)"],"cite":[0,29,30,33,41,31]},{"name":"Nightmare Boss Rush","investment":"Below average (Maxroll). The three scarabs cost under 10c per map on 4 Nov 2026.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Buy Nightmare maps in bulk through Asynchronous Trade.","Abomination is the main map because it biases Reality fragments. Ziggurat is the slower backup because its boss has invulnerability phases.","Use Searing Exarch influence and Wrath of the Cosmos.","Rush the boss and skip full clears.","Only add mechanics you pass on the way, such as Delirium or Beasts.","Sell the fragments on the Currency Exchange."],"atlasPassives":["Settlers nodes for Starfall Craters, which can hold Svalinn. Only do them if they are on the way to the boss.","Voidstones raise the chance of Nightmare maps dropping."],"scarabs":["Scarab of the Dextral","Scarab of the Sinistral","Scarab of Stability"],"cite":[1,31,15,39]},{"name":"Inscribed Ultimatum","investment":"High (Maxroll). Very hard. Scarabs cost 2.5-9c each on 4 Nov 2026.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Run T16 Jungle Valley with Searing Exarch altars.","Clear for Eldritch Altars and click Domination Shrines before you start the encounter.","Skip harsh Ultimatum modifiers (see Dangers).","Keep Inscribed Ultimatums that have 'more Monster Life'.","Vendor weak ones 5:1 to reroll them, using about 20c of value as the cut-off."],"scarabs":["2x Ultimatum Scarab of Bribing","Domination Scarab","Optional: Ultimatum Scarab of Dueling or Inscription"],"cite":[2,28,39]},{"name":"Cornucopia Harvest","investment":"Average (Maxroll), with low management.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run 8-mod T16 Jungle Valley with Eater of Worlds altars and a Fruiting Astrolabe.","Clear the map and leave the Grove for last.","Kill the Tier 4 seed bosses first (usually Vivid).","Walk out of the thorn ring instead of using a movement skill.","Sell lifeforce on the Currency Exchange."],"atlasPassives":["Farm of Exile / ImSidVicious tree: poeplanner.com/a/65ht"],"scarabs":["Harvest Scarab of Cornucopia","Harvest Scarab of Doubling","Cartography Scarab of Escalation","Scarab of Monstrous Lineage","Influencing Scarab of Hordes"],"cite":[3,34]},{"name":"League Start Harvest (pohx)","investment":"None to low. The base version needs no scarabs.","stage":["league-start","ssf","mid"],"steps":["Run Mesa or City Square.","Juiced version: add Harvest Scarab of Doubling, 2x Monstrous Lineage and 2x Mortal or Sacrifice Fragments.","pohx calls Jungle Valley a bad map for this strategy.","Alternatives: AOEAH runs only Doubling on 8-mod corrupted Mausoleum. ExpCarry lists a City Square rush with one Harvest Scarab and an optional Sacrifice Fragment."],"atlasPassives":["40 points: poeplanner.com/a/6ZV1","80 points: poeplanner.com/a/6ZVX","120 points: poeplanner.com/a/6gL0"],"scarabs":["None (base)","Harvest Scarab of Doubling (juiced)","2x Scarab of Monstrous Lineage (juiced)"],"cite":[11,19,10]},{"name":"Unstable Breach","investment":"Extremely high (Maxroll). Above-average difficulty. Still rated the best raw currency farm.","stage":["late"],"steps":["Run T16 Originator Dunes with Eater of Worlds altars and a Grasping Astrolabe.","Add a Maven's Chisel of Avarice and 1-5 Armoursmith's Delirium Orbs.","Roll 92%+ more Currency for the budget version or 140%+ for high investment.","Open at most 2 Unstable Breaches at once. The patch cap is 2, even though Maxroll still says 3."],"atlasPassives":["Synthesised Stability, plus the generic Breach passives"],"scarabs":["Scarab of Wisps","2x Breach Scarab of Instability","Budget: 2x Scarab of Monstrous Lineage","High investment: Horned Scarab of Bloodlines and Cartography Scarab of Risk"],"cite":[4,22,31]},{"name":"Stacked Deck (Cloister)","investment":"Low (Maxroll). Five Cloisters were about 233c per map on 4 Nov 2026.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run T16 8-mod Jungle Valley with Eater of Worlds.","Complete Rituals so the Doedre's Devoted packs respawn.","Each Devoted monster has a 5% chance to drop a Stacked Deck, and there are 40-60 packs.","Note: Maxroll's page body is still the 3.28 version."],"atlasPassives":["The 5th map-device slot is needed to run 5 scarabs"],"scarabs":["5x Divination Scarab of the Cloister"],"cite":[5,13,39]},{"name":"Targeted Divination Cards","investment":"Not stated in sources.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["The Apothecary (Mageblood) now drops only in Cage Map, because Defiled Cathedral was removed.","The Doctor (Headhunter) drops in Burial Chambers.","Scrying Orbs store the map they dropped in, so you can scry that map's cards onto another atlas map."],"atlasPassives":["Altered Prophecy cluster: its notable gives T14+ maps a 4% chance to drop a Scrying Orb, and its small passives raise card drop chance"],"cite":[14,22]},{"name":"Mercenary Rushing","investment":"Low per map. The two scarabs were about 23c together on 4 Nov 2026.","stage":["league-start","mid"],"steps":["Run white maps, or City Square with a Templar Astrolabe.","Kill the boss and the Mercenary, then leave within about 30 seconds.","Since 3.29.3 you must actually defeat the Infamy Wild Mercenaries to get their loot.","Since 3.29.2 Wild Mercenaries keep fighting after their leader dies."],"atlasPassives":["Contract Killers: allied Mercenaries deal 100% more damage to Mercenaries and Rogue Exiles"],"scarabs":["Trarthan Scarab of Renown (all Mercenary gear is Unique)","Trarthan Scarab of Infamy (Infamous Mercenary plus 2 Wild Mercenaries)"],"cite":[21,28,31,47,46,15,39]},{"name":"Curse of the Allflame: Charts & Voyages","investment":"Not stated. Dead Man's Sulphur is about 0.01c each, so a 9,000-Sulphur reroll ceiling is about 94c.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Stock at least 50 Charts. Each Voyage uses 9.","Roll Charts before charting them, because you can't change them once placed.","Reroll border modifiers with up to 9,000 Sulphur, looking for 'Rare Monsters drop an additional Divine Orb'. The cost doubles with each reroll.","If you don't find it, prioritise Operative Strongbox Charts.","Sea Pillars is the only required Unique Room.","After the 7th lantern, return to the Bathysphere or you drown and lose the loot.","From 3.29.3 you can socket up to 3 Cursed Ducats in the Voyage Planner to Empower runs."],"atlasPassives":["3.29 added atlas nodes for the Voyage system"],"cite":[7,47,40,15]},{"name":"Map Farming (Nightmare/Originator)","investment":"Low (Maxroll), with excellent profitability.","stage":["mid","late"],"steps":["Run T16 Originator Dunes under Searing Exarch.","Run 8-mod maps that have 100%+ More Maps and sell the rest.","List Nightmare maps in a higher-priced tab and move unsold ones back from time to time."],"scarabs":["Cartography Scarab of Escalation","3x Cartography Scarab of the Multitude"],"cite":[8]},{"name":"Kalguuran Map Farming","investment":"Not stated. Needs solid survivability and damage.","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run T16 Originator Jungle Valley with 70%+ More Maps under Searing Exarch.","Sell the 8-mod corrupted Nightmare and Originator maps."],"scarabs":["Cartography Scarab of Escalation","Kalguuran Scarab of Guarded Riches","2x Kalguuran Scarab","Cartography Scarab of Corruption"],"cite":[50]},{"name":"Destructive Play","investment":"Zero","stage":["league-start"],"steps":["Run T16 Silo (T14+ Maven-influenced Silo maps).","Kill only the extra Destructive Play bosses and leave the main boss alive.","Sell Maven's Chisels, Shaped Astrolabes and influenced maps."],"cite":[9,32]},{"name":"Alch & Go","investment":"Very low, with low profit","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Run any map. Transmute, alch or vaal it as needed.","Push to yellow maps for Shrieking Essences.","Sell most drops to fund your build until your Voidstones are done."],"cite":[6]},{"name":"80% Deli Farm (PoE Vault)","investment":"Low to medium","stage":["mid"],"steps":["Run Dunes with 4 Fine or Diviner's Delirium Orbs."],"atlasPassives":["poeplanner.com/a/6glO"],"scarabs":["2x Delirium Scarab of Mania","3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia"],"cite":[12]},{"name":"Manni's Delirium Orb Printer (pohx)","investment":"Not stated","stage":["late","ssf"],"steps":["Run Strand, Tropical Island, City Square or Dunes.","Juiced version adds Mania and Neuroses scarabs (T11+)."],"atlasPassives":["40: poeplanner.com/a/6g3b","80: poeplanner.com/a/6g3a","120: poeplanner.com/a/6g3F","138: poeplanner.com/a/6g3V"],"scarabs":["3x Delirium Scarab of Paranoia","Juiced: Mania and Neuroses"],"cite":[11]},{"name":"Strongboxes + Deli + Beyond (pohx, SC only)","investment":"Not stated","stage":["late"],"steps":["Run Haunted Mansion on T16.5 maps rolled for 90%+ Currency or Scarabs.","Avoid -max res, no regen and less recovery mods."],"atlasPassives":["poeplanner.com/a/65Dr"],"scarabs":["Ambush Scarab of Containment","Ambush Scarab of Discernment","Ambush Scarab of Potency","Ambush Scarab","Ambush Scarab of Compartments"],"cite":[11]},{"name":"Starter Atlas with Breach & Shrines (pohx)","investment":"Low. Skip the scarabs if they are expensive.","stage":["league-start","ssf"],"steps":["Run open maps such as Jungle Valley or Beach."],"atlasPassives":["80 points: poeplanner.com/a/6g4N (40 and 120-point versions also on pohx.net)"],"scarabs":["2x Breach Scarab of Instability"],"cite":[11]}],"profit":[{"text":"Ethereal Allflame: about 42 div/h (rough, seller claim). It used about 100c embers, which now cost about 526c.","who":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-29","cite":[17,41]},{"text":"Ethereal Allflame rated Good profitability. No div/h given.","who":"Maxroll (BawLoch)","date":"2026-08-11","cite":[0]},{"text":"Inscribed Ultimatum on white T16 Jungle Valley: about 5.3 div/h net after about 1.2 div/h input (rough, community test).","who":"ExpCarry","date":"2026-09-01","cite":[10]},{"text":"4x Cloister Stacked Decks: about 11 div/h gross, about 5.2 div/h net (rough, early 3.29 test).","who":"ExpCarry","date":"2026-09-01","cite":[10]},{"text":"5x Cloister: about 65c in, about 60c net per map (rough). Outdated now that Cloisters are about 47c each.","who":"Timesaver.gg (currency seller)","date":"2026-09-05","cite":[13,39]},{"text":"Cornucopia Jungle Valley: about 11.3 div/h, a little over 1 div per map (rough, a price model, not a measured rate).","who":"Farm of Exile (ImSidVicious)","date":"2026-11-03","cite":[34,36]},{"text":"Harvest: about 0.2 div per 3-minute map. League start with the full tree: 600-1,000c/h (rough).","who":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"2026-07-28","cite":[19]},{"text":"Charts and Voyages: 21.65 div/h over 100 Charts and 11 Voyages (rough, one logged test).","who":"Timesaver.gg citing empyriangaming","date":"2026-09-05","cite":[13]},{"text":"Voyage best case: 105 guaranteed divines with the Divine border mod and 15 strongboxes. This is a ceiling, not a per-hour figure.","who":"Maxroll","date":"2026-08-03","cite":[7]},{"text":"Mercenary rushing: 15-20 div/h fast, 8-10 div/h slower, without jackpots (rough, no source given).","who":"MMOEXP (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-10","cite":[21]},{"text":"Fortress boss rush: about 30 div/h with late-league quantity stacking (rough). IGGM's figure of over 25 div/h is from 3.28.","who":"AOEAH (currency seller)","date":"2026-08-01","cite":[20,37]},{"text":"High-investment Abyss with Searing Exarch altars on Jungle Valley: 20-30 div/h, about half from altars (rough, late 3.29 test).","who":"ExpCarry","date":"2026-09-01","cite":[10]},{"text":"pohx publishes no div/h figures, because they change weekly.","who":"pohx.net","date":"unknown","cite":[11]}],"changes":[{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Infamy Wild Mercenaries now drop loot only when defeated. Some enemy Mercenary skills deal less damage.","cite":[47,26]},{"patch":"3.29.3","text":"Added 6 Cursed Ducats for the Voyage Planner, up to 3 socketed at a time.","cite":[47]},{"patch":"3.29.3b","text":"No Mercenary, scarab or drop changes in 3.29.3b or Hotfix 4.","cite":[48,49]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Infamy Wild Mercenaries keep fighting after their leader dies.","cite":[46,25]},{"patch":"3.29.2","text":"Chart gold-find mods now give item rarity instead. Deep Altar Blessing conversion is now 10%, up from 4%.","cite":[46]},{"patch":"3.29.1","text":"Infamous Mercenaries are about 2x as common in T16 and 50% more common in T1. Added the Contract Killers notable. Hired Mercenaries now get Golden Lantern buffs.","cite":[23,24,45]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Syndicate Leaders no longer drop Allflame Embers. The Mastermind drops only the Ember of Kulemak.","cite":[22,27]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Ethereal embers now come from the Mercenaries mechanic instead of Catarina. They are easier to get but still expensive.","cite":[33,31]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Breach nerfs: smaller packs, 15% fewer Unstable Breach packs (with 25% more kill progress), Swelling Ranks down to 10% and Evolving Hives at 15%.","cite":[22,10,16]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"At most 2 Unstable Breaches can be open at once, down from 3. Maxroll's 3.29.1 guide still says 3.","cite":[22,4]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Ultimatum is now the only source of Catalysts. Brave the Tower gives 10 of a random Catalyst, and the stack size is now 20. Maxroll still says a full stack.","cite":[22,2]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"The Harvest Synthesise craft was removed.","cite":[22,19]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Horned Scarab of Awakening was removed (per AOEAH).","cite":[19]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"28 maps were added and 28 removed, including Defiled Cathedral, Crimson Temple, Ashen Wood, Carcass, Racecourse, Coves, Dry Sea and Wharf.","cite":[11]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Nameless Seer and Reflecting Mists now appear only in Atlas Anomalies. Mist currency drops more often but gives a smaller modifier boost.","cite":[22]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"New Altered Prophecy cluster adds Scrying Orbs and better card drop chance.","cite":[22,14]},{"patch":"3.29.0","text":"Mercenary rucksacks in maps no longer give Transmutation or Augmentation orbs.","cite":[22]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"Maxroll moved Rare Monster Scarab farming and Betrayal down to C tier.","cite":[31]},{"patch":"3.29","text":"New atlas nodes for Mercenaries and Voyages. The core 138-point tree and Voidstones are otherwise unchanged.","cite":[15]}],"tables":[{"title":"Maxroll S tier at a glance","columns":["Farm","Stage","Investment","Profit","Difficulty","Map"],"rows":[["Ethereal Scarabs","late","High","Good","Extreme","T16 Originator Crater"],["Nightmare Boss Rush","mid/late","Below average","Excellent","Above average","Abomination (Ziggurat backup)"],["Inscribed Ultimatum","late","High","not stated","Extreme","T16 Jungle Valley"],["Cornucopia Harvest","mid","Average","Average","Average","8-mod T16 Jungle Valley"],["Unstable Breach","late","Extremely high","Best raw currency","Above average","T16 Originator Dunes"],["Divination Cards","mid/late","not stated","not stated","not stated","Cage Map / Burial Chambers"],["Mercenary Rushing","league-start/mid","not stated","not stated","not stated","City Square or white maps"],["Charts & Voyages","mid/late","not stated","not stated","not stated","Voyages (9 Charts each)"]],"cite":[31,0,1,2,3,4,14,21,7]},{"title":"Input prices (poe.ninja, 4 Nov 2026)","columns":["Item","Price","Used in"],"rows":[["Allflame Ember of the Ethereal","~526c","Ethereal (x3 = ~1,577c)"],["Horned Scarab of Bloodlines","~613c","Ethereal, high-inv Breach"],["Betrayal Scarab of the Allflame","~0.68c","Ethereal"],["Scarab of the Dextral / Sinistral / Stability","~4.1c / 3.1c / 2.1c","Boss Rush"],["Ultimatum Scarab of Bribing / Dueling / Inscription","~2.5c / 6c / 9.2c","Ultimatum"],["Domination Scarab","~3.3c","Ultimatum"],["Scarab of Wisps","~30c","Unstable Breach"],["Scarab of Monstrous Lineage","~9.3c","Breach, Harvest"],["Maven's Chisel of Avarice","~372c","Unstable Breach"],["Armoursmith's Delirium Orb","~16.6c","Unstable Breach"],["Breach Scarab of Instability","no price line","Unstable Breach"],["Divination Scarab of the Cloister","~47c","Stacked Deck"],["Harvest Scarab of Doubling / Cornucopia","~126c / 199c","Harvest"],["Trarthan Scarab of Renown / Infamy","~10.6c / 12.2c","Mercenary Rushing"],["Dead Man's 